    <node id="Civil Engineer">
      <data key="d0">Civil Engineer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A civil engineer is a professional engineer registered to practice in civil works, focusing on design and construction for public use.&lt;SEP&gt;The Civil Engineer prepares approved grading plans and is responsible for the inspection and approval of grading operations and drainage systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The civil engineer is responsible for overseeing the preparation of ground for fills and ensuring compliance with grading plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Civil Engineer recommends modifications for safety and stability of retaining walls and other structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A Civil Engineer is a professional responsible for planning and certifying structural and environmental aspects of construction projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cef5b7e32b0ddd3edba870d372388da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db123662a7e9dede9c2ca3b9af268f75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d8a7c5169d0acda3f7ceac0b42dee14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b0a262fe914a0c7fcb75c7815be4a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5ea5fe5eea40eab34623aa7e60f482</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781099</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Soil Engineer">
      <data key="d0">Soil Engineer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A soil (geotechnical) engineer is a civil engineer qualified in the practice of soil engineering through education and training.&lt;SEP&gt;The Soil Engineer's role involves providing professional inspection and approval regarding ground preparation and compaction testing.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil engineer is responsible for the inspection and approval of ground preparation, ensuring it meets engineering standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cef5b7e32b0ddd3edba870d372388da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db123662a7e9dede9c2ca3b9af268f75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706782d1588e72967037b624ff644c38</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779847</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Engineering Geologist">
      <data key="d0">Engineering Geologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An engineering geologist is a geologist experienced in engineering geology and registered in the State of Oregon.&lt;SEP&gt;The Engineering Geologist is responsible for inspecting the natural ground's adequacy for receiving fills and ensuring slope stability based on geological factors.&lt;SEP&gt;The engineering geologist evaluates natural ground adequacy for fills and assesses geological factors affecting grading.&lt;SEP&gt;The Engineering Geologist assesses geological factors that may affect the design and stability of retaining walls.&lt;SEP&gt;The Engineering Geologist assesses geological conditions and provides recommendations for safe construction practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cef5b7e32b0ddd3edba870d372388da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db123662a7e9dede9c2ca3b9af268f75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d8a7c5169d0acda3f7ceac0b42dee14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b0a262fe914a0c7fcb75c7815be4a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d41d5cef81888f4a8f2657cd2edf9d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779847</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
