    <node id="Flood Hazard Areas">
      <data key="d0">Flood Hazard Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Flood Hazard Areas are designated regions identified as being at risk for flooding and are subject to specific construction and development regulations intended to mitigate potential risks. These areas are established based on assessments of flood risk and are essential for ensuring safety and effective stormwater management. 

Flood Hazard Areas encompass all lands located within floodway boundaries and other identified flood zones. They play a crucial role in shaping development requirements, as construction activities within these zones often necessitate compensatory measures to address potential floodwater displacement. Furthermore, these areas are regulated by municipal authorities, reflecting their significance in urban planning and community safety. 

In summary, Flood Hazard Areas serve as critical zones where the interaction of topography, weather, and human activity is managed through stringent regulations to minimize flooding risks and safeguard both infrastructure and inhabitants.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-caa2864f9db143b33db40ca11a516e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-701594b3b5395a053d09f27e4da7dcee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbba9ae1b324ef0410472174c02e9e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616337655b3a110b38e3cef90183ec87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3d014b174352ce9ad5757f1156a2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ee09234912e67470de67393ca93ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14f8246c5fe0e568217638fa85d97ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189a3579e304a7efcf0f543eaaad1a8</data>
