    <node id="OSSC">
      <data key="d0">OSSC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The OSSC (Oregon State Structural Code) defines the building standards and classifications relevant to seismic improvement evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;The OSSC (Oregon Structural Specialty Code) is the governing document for building codes and design standards unless otherwise noted.&lt;SEP&gt;The OSSC (Oregon Structural Specialty Code) provides regulatory requirements and standards for building construction and safety in Oregon.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oregon Structural Specialty Code (OSSC) provides guidelines for structural safety and building regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffa3eb9ed7fae286e6c7cbef13d5c1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad313e169428e5341b6a990dbd9f9bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5902d8c6d32e1e8323685d7234c2507e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7b1be8af44bb34ea4e9d761716215e</data>
