    <node id="State of Oregon">
      <data key="d0">State of Oregon</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The State of Oregon is a U.S. state, referenced in the context of engineering and architectural law compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The State of Oregon is a U.S. state where the relevant regulations and engineering licensing apply.&lt;SEP&gt;The State of Oregon is a U.S. state where engineering geologists must be registered to practice.&lt;SEP&gt;The State of Oregon is a U.S. state where the structural engineer and hazardous material professional are licensed to operate.&lt;SEP&gt;The State of Oregon is the U.S. state where specific safety standards for private Helicopter Landing Facilities are mandated.&lt;SEP&gt;The State of Oregon is involved in the regulatory approval process for helicopter landing facilities through its Aeronautics Division.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d8a7c5169d0acda3f7ceac0b42dee14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407245345ef716e5e0d52e90aa6e4851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60990f5dab82c2b537b14b43e0a453ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ee09234912e67470de67393ca93ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21fff4b96769197d29b5065fb50894e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ca5fc3d28aa819abc484b86dc468ed</data>
