    </node>
    <node id="Demolition Permit">
      <data key="d0">Demolition Permit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Demolition Permit is a legal authorization required for the lawful demolition of structures on a site. It outlines the specific conditions and requirements that must be met prior to commencing any demolition activities. This permit is particularly necessary for residential structures and involves a formal application process, which includes notifications to relevant authorities.

In addition to the basic requirement for a demolition permit, there are important considerations related to tree preservation and protection. The issuance of a demolition permit is contingent upon a thorough review process, ensuring that all necessary criteria are satisfied before legal demolition can proceed. 

Overall, a Demolition Permit serves as a critical regulatory mechanism that governs the legal removal of structures while safeguarding the environment and adhering to local regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4e4166aaef8e1cf6d96fa7a807af0de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2eaaf54ea337fd1c606b95b01bf732d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851e46c6798be63a5ed200499e9b955d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495efc01559ae21a68e9da3b57998769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4271bb9cc0287dcb0b401b760eb4864e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e75ce8cc1ed34d85d9e574add4504b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781096</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
