      <data key="d5">1768779849</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="New Manufactured Home Park">
      <data key="d0">New Manufactured Home Park</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">New Manufactured Home Park is a land parcel divided into lots for manufactured homes, requiring service facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;New manufactured home park designates parcels of land divided into multiple manufactured home lots for rent or sale, with construction completed post-October 18, 1979.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db63c93213cb06b155d2b22811e90c9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ordinary High Water Mark (OHWM)">
      <data key="d0">Ordinary High Water Mark (OHWM)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ordinary High Water Mark is defined as the shore line established by water fluctuations indicated by physical characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pre-Implementation Compliance Measures (PICM) Riparian Buffer Zone">
      <data key="d0">Pre-Implementation Compliance Measures (PICM) Riparian Buffer Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PICM Riparian Buffer Zone refers to a designated area within a flood hazard zone relating to the OHWM, including nearby waterways.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Substantial Damage">
      <data key="d0">Substantial Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Substantial damage means significant damage to a structure that equates to 50% or more of its market value before the damage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Substantial Improvement">
      <data key="d0">Substantial Improvement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Substantial improvement refers to repairs or changes that equal or exceed 50% of a structure's market value and may involve any structural alteration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Top of Bank">
      <data key="d0">Top of Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Top of bank indicates the highest slope decrease near the OHWM of a water body and is determined by specific measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Top of bank refers to the default location described in Chapter 33.930 concerning flood management.&lt;SEP&gt;Top of Bank is defined as the highest point of a slope relative to water bodies, influencing zoning and construction regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Top of bank refers to the highest point of a riverbank where measurements for environmental assessments are taken.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbba9ae1b324ef0410472174c02e9e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84efb40ac49907b061aeb00bb2d08948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70e49b32e27402af67173acaf34a3c9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Water Surface Elevation">
      <data key="d0">Water Surface Elevation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Water surface elevation describes the height of water during design floods at any point along a watercourse.&lt;SEP&gt;Water surface elevation indicates the height of the water surface of the design flood for any point along a watercourse.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbba9ae1b324ef0410472174c02e9e9d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Watercourse">
      <data key="d0">Watercourse</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Watercourse is a channel where water flows continuously or intermittently, which can be natural or artificial.&lt;SEP&gt;Watercourse is a channel in which water flows, either continuously or intermittently, and can be natural or artificial.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbba9ae1b324ef0410472174c02e9e9d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bureau of Environmental Services">
      <data key="d0">Bureau of Environmental Services</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bureau of Environmental Services (BES) is the agency responsible for regulating and overseeing a variety of environmental services, with a strong focus on managing stormwater and sanitary waste disposal systems. This regulatory authority ensures compliance with environmental standards throughout urban areas, including the administration of stormwater management and landscaping standards in urban planning initiatives.

BES holds authority over the approval and certification of eco-roofs, focusing on their compliance with specific stormwater management criteria. The bureau also evaluates and approves landscape plans for revegetation projects, ensuring these meet the necessary environmental regulations. In addition to its responsibilities for managing stormwater runoff from various urban sources, such as parking lots, BES sets standards for stormwater systems and environmental compliance within designated plan districts, including the Johnson Creek Basin Plan District and the West Portland Multicultural Plan District.

Furthermore, the Bureau of Environmental Services conducts technical reviews for reclamation plans associated with landfill uses and verifies sewer and stormwater management systems to ensure they meet the established standards for proposed developments. The bureau oversees the evaluation and acceptance of sanitary waste disposal systems, ensuring that these facilities comply with required environmental regulations for public safety and environmental health.

Overall, the Bureau of Environmental Services acts as a comprehensive governing body aimed at protecting the environment through rigorous standards and effective management practices related to stormwater, sanitation, and landscaping within urban development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0822aa249af1cada3cc5aa958e97dce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05299df3decd7e8061aff48bb1ba2029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bcfb59e4095f5b02abc8ac31213ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c98d267897f87dec14edb30985e788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a079f6fb5c8d245b04e7b9c62fbfa8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873d10749dbc15173a36fece7c83683d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b26f7d2f189f75baf65a70e0e0ddf9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023787323ecc1bdd6b648be267e3ae8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32085ee92ea490a135a4678599552bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31a92cc8ee690c44538d0568e543e8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e596f70f1bcab1802ff190bf7807a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8491ef6a94a83bd06029a3a52c0a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feff08f8742feb2b38fee34824605dc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-546f125167252089bdfedd0eae022ba2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2c06f5978724095d6914de0f870d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ee84d998824c1408d6153086fc99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c1ff44e4a06a65a47b8c351d06d59b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc3ba891360a2a54cb8bbb9f425464c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5814020534bf1fbc0a6e4c64746ca31d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d54757bbd8eb99b2b0cd39a957603d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59602cfae2cfed1834328c9ad24adf39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c50fc0ff9e807e9d3489aba2b4c9f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a2edce75cc1c84e8d78d82be31fd43b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed8af90c52cb663785082c6731625b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e7feaddec557941c697fec7b2e2763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d28f6febcf4de65239d0203f2197382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4177bfbc917fc82fda498c4d1f0e571f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23bdb6b78c43cbe3cee1a2bacbb57a5f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recreational Vehicle">
      <data key="d0">Recreational Vehicle</data>
      <data key="d1">vehicle</data>
      <data key="d2">A recreational vehicle is defined as any vehicle built on a single chassis designed primarily for temporary living quarters for various types of use.&lt;SEP&gt;Recreational Vehicle is defined as any vehicle designed for temporary living quarters, built on a single chassis and under specific size limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Recreational Vehicles are designed for leisure activities or as temporary living quarters for travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ba12577414f8d5a3adb28727f2e0ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2b499d5c2e57ccff7be29d1a99659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6c39f118dd3cc1984138088ad67005</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781119</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Appeal Board">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Appeal Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Administrative Appeal Board reviews decisions related to the application and interpretation of the Building Code, and its findings can be appealed to the Code Board of Appeal.&lt;SEP&gt;The Administrative Appeal Board is responsible for hearing appeals related to requirements or decisions made under the chapter.&lt;SEP&gt;The Administrative Appeal Board reviews decisions related to the application of the codes and offers a pathway for appeals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ba12577414f8d5a3adb28727f2e0ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7ce09240c58c0153b8be45ed992be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d97f5eef5c0648c052fbe7643fc599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2934c450fcc75ab9c66c0de792267b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 24.10">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 24.10</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 24.10 contains regulations governing permits and inspections related to construction in Portland.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 24.10 outlines the procedures for appeals regarding decisions made under this legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ba12577414f8d5a3adb28727f2e0ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54361a566e85890eaf247234d7d1990a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
