    <node id="Building Permit">
      <data key="d0">Building Permit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Building Permit is an official approval issued by local governing authorities, such as Portland Permitting &amp; Development, that allows for the construction or alteration of buildings and structures. This permit is mandated before any construction activities can commence and is designed to ensure compliance with local development regulations and standards.

To obtain a Building Permit, applicants must fulfill various requirements, including addressing any identified deficiencies and ensuring adherence to specific regulations. Furthermore, for certain construction activities, permits may necessitate the submission of archaeological resource recovery plans and agreements with tribal governments, particularly in sensitive areas.

The Building Permit serves as a formal authorization that not only approves new development and changes to existing structures but also facilitates compliance with local codes and regulations. It is crucial for maintaining safety and consistency in construction practices across urban areas. The permit process typically involves the payment of fees and other conditions, ensuring that all significant alterations or constructions are proceeded with a comprehensive understanding of regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5adf814a146242df9673b129a2f1e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a98088aa848c3a646425801c36c9f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1b829449e430ca472af4da987d81a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7e7d1e624354524b6833b6427f9866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47812462d7ccc96ffd0025a366f98586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc38fc86828ecd90586e33007486e5d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285f052019746f5b49b63ae041c898aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f5238f416f69c282caa09bc226ffbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059e173ef884a58e8cd223998e6158d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df192280c989d3e1d2bc59bf520124ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2c7926ceca17c4d0d7614d1c8acec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a1f6c75ad3d0c1fd2c336ca22bead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608046d7256ca4fab03fcfe5e6c5d66b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Permit Application">
      <data key="d0">Permit Application</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Permit Application is a formal request submitted to Portland Permitting &amp; Development to obtain a building permit for construction or development work.&lt;SEP&gt;Permit Application is a request submitted to Portland Permitting &amp; Development for obtaining permission to undertake major residential alterations or additions.&lt;SEP&gt;A Permit Application is required for establishing, constructing, or modifying manufactured dwelling parks and accessory structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A Permit Application is a formal request submitted by an applicant to obtain approval for building or development activities within specified regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5adf814a146242df9673b129a2f1e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af19833dca55553fa53ce719e59dfd2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d97f5eef5c0648c052fbe7643fc599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2001ba277158737c9b888248e680d7ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781143</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Maintenance Agreement is a legal contract outlining responsibilities for the upkeep of building elements that cross property lines.&lt;SEP&gt;A Maintenance Agreement is a legal document that outlines responsibilities for repair and upkeep of structures or utilities crossing property lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5adf814a146242df9673b129a2f1e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616337655b3a110b38e3cef90183ec87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Abandoned Structure">
      <data key="d0">Abandoned Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An abandoned structure is defined as a building that has been vacant for over six months or constitutes an attractive nuisance or hazard when vacant for less than six months.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d061032da80389dd5b777b1e5e8bc61</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agreement/Contract to Repair/Work">
      <data key="d0">Agreement/Contract to Repair/Work</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An agreement or contract to repair/work is a written pact where an owner agrees to perform repairs on an abandoned or unsafe structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d061032da80389dd5b777b1e5e8bc61</data>
