    <node id="Title 29">
      <data key="d0">Title 29</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 29 contains regulations governing compliance inspections for residential buildings proposed to be moved.&lt;SEP&gt;Title 29 encompasses the specific regulations and procedural guidelines related to administration and enforcement in the context of building and demolition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e8c1c7b39585a7a7e3106344983f67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6462811b852b5096dfd03e84ed0979</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779851</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 24.70">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 24.70</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 24.70 outlines regulations related to flood protection and construction standards for buildings in flood-prone areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 24.70 specifies requirements for the removal of foundations and excavations following demolition work.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 24.70 outlines the regulations regarding clearing and grading as part of land development activities and vegetation management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e8c1c7b39585a7a7e3106344983f67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a06ad2f76c555340d2a3febc2894de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbcf1c43cb59d25662f5af1b9ac994a8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781133</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Base Flood Elevation">
      <data key="d0">Base Flood Elevation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Base flood elevation is the minimum elevation required to provide protection from flooding, applied in the context of new constructions and land development.&lt;SEP&gt;Base Flood Elevation refers to the elevation that floodwaters are expected to reach during a base flood event.&lt;SEP&gt;Base Flood Elevation refers to the height level at which flood risk is assessed for building and development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Base Flood Elevation is the calculated elevation level at which floodwaters are expected to reach during a base flood event, influencing flood management regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Base Flood Elevation (BFE) is a defined level indicating the height of floodwaters during a base flood, referenced by the Federal Emergency Management Agency in flood insurance maps.&lt;SEP&gt;Base Flood Elevation (BFE) is a standard measurement used to determine the height at which flooding is expected during a flood event, referenced in the context of the Federal Emergency Management Agency Flood Insurance Rate Maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a06ad2f76c555340d2a3febc2894de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3d014b174352ce9ad5757f1156a2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a47da3153ff3a91ef0d0af937548b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14f8246c5fe0e568217638fa85d97ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64960cc4adf91b7f6ea0964bf7f6dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d39e794ab5c802105ac492ea170724</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781030</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Johnson Creek Flood Risk Area">
      <data key="d0">Johnson Creek Flood Risk Area</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Johnson Creek Flood Risk Area is a designated zone where special flood management provisions are implemented to mitigate flooding risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Johnson Creek Flood Risk Area is designated for regulating development to prevent flooding and maintain flood storage capacity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a06ad2f76c555340d2a3febc2894de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14f8246c5fe0e568217638fa85d97ac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768779851</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Federal Emergency Management Agency">
      <data key="d0">Federal Emergency Management Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) provides guidelines and regulations related to flood management, including the installation of manufactured homes in flood hazard areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) is a U.S. government agency responsible for coordinating the federal government's response to natural disasters and for flood insurance mapping.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) provides floodplain elevation definitions relevant to tree planting regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) is responsible for coordinating disaster responses and managing flood hazard designations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a06ad2f76c555340d2a3febc2894de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e934d288b532969001ac5c602e3192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d39e794ab5c802105ac492ea170724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-198e1551ae650afd9098fb33de845850</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
