    </node>
    <node id="Johnson Creek Basin Plan District">
      <data key="d0">Johnson Creek Basin Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Johnson Creek Basin Plan District is a designated planning area that implements specific land use and development regulations to ensure environmental preservation and urban planning compliance. This District focuses on developing standards that facilitate safe and efficient land development while addressing physical features and constraints within the area.

The District encompasses the regions surrounding Johnson Creek and is governed by regulations outlined in Title 33, specifically mentioned in Chapter 33.535, which has been recently renumbered for organizational purposes. Key regulations pertain to outdoor shelters, which must comply with development standards tailored to the unique environmental context of the area.

Additionally, the Johnson Creek Basin Plan District enforces development regulations that include restrictions on the transfer of development rights and mandates the necessity for tree preservation within its land use policies. These efforts are part of a broader strategy to balance urban development with environmental management and resource sustainability, ensuring that the area's ecological character is safeguarded while accommodating growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9a8cfd0b35d4420d886b74a453a0e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e03486b757e08e3d165c5c60acde4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-253ac235ab4d20d7cfd5ecc312a981ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd54e5b638113595ce88bbc6ccf94bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de298aa875613309b192e347dc83983f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd8d8658cc4857f6fce07f7f2b7850e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d54757bbd8eb99b2b0cd39a957603d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8cd0a693bdee1928f1f0600d5193c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
