    <node id="Hearings Officer">
      <data key="d0">Hearings Officer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Hearings Officer is an official established by city code specifically tasked with managing code enforcement hearings. This role encompasses a broad range of responsibilities related to property inspections and compliance issues, ensuring that properties adhere to regulations set forth by local ordinances.

The Hearings Officer has the authority to mandate demolition actions in accordance with property maintenance regulations, particularly under specific conditions within a National Register District. This power underscores the Officer's crucial role in upholding property standards and managing safety concerns.

Additionally, the Hearings Officer oversees the appeals process, making decisions related to appeals lodged against property compliance rulings and land use issues. The Officer is responsible for making written decisions concerning planning and zoning appeals, as well as land use actions and amendments, based on evidence and testimony presented during public hearings. This includes notifying all involved parties about the outcomes and recommendations stemming from these hearings.

In summary, the Hearings Officer functions as a designated official who ensures that property and land use regulations are enforced fairly and consistently while providing a structured avenue for appeals and compliance through public hearings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a78f1876fb134d98c03a24e26b94fa88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44500823ae619d4a2c4e588251577618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14945c9dafbb0b5a4864c97b10515585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdaeb46ee0afe6f8cbf449de5ce1578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fed5b9206a5c4a294b3284cd70adcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8e06f7fcece5e199a44dcbdcbf9d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60dcf59d4eb9520c7bf8e9968ecf967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5786b7f8c1ac1620534c8b4098445f90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781048</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Owner">
      <data key="d0">Owner</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Owner" refers to any individual or entity that possesses an interest in a property. This encompasses a range of roles and responsibilities, particularly in contexts such as property management, land use applications, and regulatory compliance. An Owner may hold legal title to real property or may be a contract purchaser, which gives them certain rights and responsibilities regarding the property.

In the context of land use applications, the Owner is often the individual or entity that holds title to the property involved. This role is significant as the Owner may be subject to inspection and safety regulations, and they are notified of decisions concerning the application. Additionally, the Owner must be informed about any proposed alterations, especially if the property is slated for demolition.

Moreover, in decision-making processes regarding land use, the Owner's interests are considered, thereby making them a critical stakeholder. They may receive notices pertaining to these applications and have the opportunity to participate in the appeals process. The Owner's legal standing and vested interests create a need for their engagement in matters affecting the property, ensuring that their rights as titleholders are recognized and considered during regulatory and planning reviews.

In summary, the Owner is a key figure in the landscape of property law and land use, intertwined with the legal and bureaucratic aspects of property ownership, regulatory compliance, and participatory rights in the planning process.&lt;SEP&gt;Owner refers to the individual or entity legally responsible for the center's operation and certification requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a78f1876fb134d98c03a24e26b94fa88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44500823ae619d4a2c4e588251577618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14945c9dafbb0b5a4864c97b10515585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f69badbdc0a01b4a234db008584a915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4263b41e43a7e8a83f6017fb2cf1c50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200b9b34fa908e42e599f92db53639cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63396adc71a2e9185adb3bc7b8db5ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028c3c84ee58774048f304cfbc47c40a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a7904f1485b792ad0d6843358b9f8d</data>
