    <node id="Oregon Structural Specialty Code">
      <data key="d0">Oregon Structural Specialty Code</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Oregon Structural Specialty Code (OSSC) establishes a comprehensive set of standards and regulations that govern structural construction and modifications throughout the state of Oregon. This code plays a crucial role in the permitting and inspection processes, ensuring that all building projects conform to the established safety and structural integrity guidelines. Specifically, the OSSC outlines requirements related to strength, stability, and overall safety that structures must meet. It serves as an essential reference for builders and architects by providing detailed regulations across various aspects of construction, including the design and construction of structural elements.

As part of Title 24, the OSSC integrates specific building regulations that must be adhered to within the jurisdiction, emphasizing the importance of legal standards in structural design. The code not only addresses general building safety but also delves into structural integrity requirements essential for various designs, including retaining walls. Furthermore, it defines construction regulations that include risk categories specifically for seismic design, which are vital given Oregon's geographical context.

In addition to structural safety, the OSSC specifies building standards and accessibility requirements that must be met for construction projects. This includes guidelines for accessibility in building design, compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, and specific standards for disabled persons parking and access. The OSSC outlines these accessibility regulations, ensuring that newly constructed and altered buildings cater to individuals with disabilities.

Moreover, the Oregon Structural Specialty Code addresses guidelines governing modifications to buildings, ensuring that safety and compliance are maintained during any changes. The OSSC also deals with standards for manufactured homes within residential neighborhoods, regulating their construction and appearance. Overall, the OSSC provides a fundamental framework for ensuring the safety, stability, compliance, and accessibility of buildings and structures in Oregon, influencing all stages of construction and design.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oregon Structural Specialty Code is a set of regulations outlining requirements for building safety, including egress and fire protection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oregon Structural Specialty Code is a set of regulations governing structural standards, including those for child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f1c1a120b8ba477f5a407d0777a44e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407245345ef716e5e0d52e90aa6e4851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d061032da80389dd5b777b1e5e8bc61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616337655b3a110b38e3cef90183ec87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8c1c7b39585a7a7e3106344983f67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54361a566e85890eaf247234d7d1990a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78f1876fb134d98c03a24e26b94fa88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d41d5cef81888f4a8f2657cd2edf9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44500823ae619d4a2c4e588251577618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d4fb6204c8defda427d1f8fff2f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567df924f86fd66f127e58c0497a37e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ee11d492136a3cb6116df2011b3bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ab6bd54c89f86d004823d37a33255e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ff07d99a0c758d3b51f7e05d950738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08792af032c7577571c2943db7371a28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14dcd96a6f149344a7f8451f7533b386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9e945a4de0eb93decd93ac5bbc54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7601bd156ec85bb1b68b1074e0ecd39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af58e78814991f9a5ecdccb7e8088e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2da4d204d050cba040fddbe243ce05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a1f6c75ad3d0c1fd2c336ca22bead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cb71ad267dca367ec15865890c913c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca846957ee3e21ee367da6260a78bc3</data>
