    <node id="City Administrator">
      <data key="d0">City Administrator</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The City Administrator is an official in Portland tasked with a broad range of responsibilities related to the enforcement of construction and building regulations. This role includes ensuring compliance with construction permits, conducting inspections, and overseeing overall building and zoning codes. The City Administrator has the discretion to grant extensions and reactivate permit applications as necessary, as well as the authority to approve methods related to construction and the surfacing of streets and parking areas.

In addition to permit management, the City Administrator is responsible for appointing staff members to the Administrative Appeal Board, which hears appeals presented against various administrative actions. This includes reviewing appeals related to stop work orders or citations issued by the Bureau of Planning and Development (PP&amp;D). The City Administrator also oversees maintenance agreements and access easements, ensuring that property lines are respected and regulations are met.

The enforcement of specific building regulations, such as Title 24, falls under the purview of the City Administrator, who may order corrections or vacating of buildings deemed unsafe. They also review previously prepared seismic studies and evaluations concerning building improvements related to seismic safety. Moreover, they designate hazardous materials and enforce regulations concerning flood hazard areas, indicating a broader role in public safety and environmental concerns.

Furthermore, the City Administrator manages grading operations and has the authority to require modifications to project designs, grant approvals for setbacks, and ensure compliance with regulations on grading and drainage operations. They also oversee the assignment of address numbers, maintaining records to ensure compliance with related regulations.

Overall, the City Administrator plays a critical role in maintaining construction integrity and public safety within Portland, balancing between regulatory compliance, public service, and emergency response roles as they pertain to building and construction management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cef5b7e32b0ddd3edba870d372388da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caa2864f9db143b33db40ca11a516e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27624e43bed080783f32570c691eed2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffa3eb9ed7fae286e6c7cbef13d5c1e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2934c450fcc75ab9c66c0de792267b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db123662a7e9dede9c2ca3b9af268f75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d8a7c5169d0acda3f7ceac0b42dee14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b0a262fe914a0c7fcb75c7815be4a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f1c1a120b8ba477f5a407d0777a44e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407245345ef716e5e0d52e90aa6e4851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad23b4588f34612e5e3486591895965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5adf814a146242df9673b129a2f1e89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706782d1588e72967037b624ff644c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616337655b3a110b38e3cef90183ec87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8c1c7b39585a7a7e3106344983f67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54361a566e85890eaf247234d7d1990a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6462811b852b5096dfd03e84ed0979&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7b1be8af44bb34ea4e9d761716215e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78f1876fb134d98c03a24e26b94fa88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81329d8cc341e48303e1cc13e7ae769d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60990f5dab82c2b537b14b43e0a453ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-134e99fe1ed81e0af91dacf0ec909533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d41d5cef81888f4a8f2657cd2edf9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14f8246c5fe0e568217638fa85d97ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44500823ae619d4a2c4e588251577618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d97f5eef5c0648c052fbe7643fc599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7ce09240c58c0153b8be45ed992be9</data>
