    <node id="PP&amp;D">
      <data key="d0">PP&amp;D</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">PP&amp;D, which stands for Planning, Property, and Development, is an organization responsible for multiple aspects of oversight related to construction and development activities in the city of Portland. The department manages the issuance and review of building permits, ensuring compliance with zoning standards and development regulations. This includes the processing of applications for land use reviews, tree preservation plans, and home occupation permits, particularly for Type B home occupations, which are granted for a two-year duration.

PP&amp;D also plays a crucial role in the inspection and approval processes, overseeing not only demolition activities but also the compliance of development projects with landscaping specifications and performance guarantees. Furthermore, the director of PP&amp;D has authority over remediation site plans, including the ability to waive certain items during reviews. The department handles the approval of acoustical reports, noise mitigation plans, and private sanitary sewage disposal systems for developments. 

Additionally, PP&amp;D is responsible for the tracking and collection of revegetation fees and administering the categorization of tree species. It requires documentation confirming compliance with various design standards, and any alterations proposed on sites exceeding $356,300 must be evaluated by the department. Reports and recommendations related to land use applications are prepared by PP&amp;D, which also manages notifications and final decisions regarding permit applications, ensuring consistent communication with stakeholders throughout the process.

Overall, PP&amp;D serves as an essential regulatory body that upholds the zoning regulations and land use standards necessary for sustainable development in Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60990f5dab82c2b537b14b43e0a453ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d1029e4cbf53e8d0067df848d061a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e735d7bf40b332127efe9da20dd2f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bcfb59e4095f5b02abc8ac31213ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d46c43c9570caf791239d0c34502c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdee8c33d0d52a7455e70087137ca492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ab6bd54c89f86d004823d37a33255e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a079f6fb5c8d245b04e7b9c62fbfa8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47812462d7ccc96ffd0025a366f98586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4263b41e43a7e8a83f6017fb2cf1c50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200b9b34fa908e42e599f92db53639cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145c2e6cf2a3147235dc3027efb2fd6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608046d7256ca4fab03fcfe5e6c5d66b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8537f80e77714b5b0188914023a593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-546f125167252089bdfedd0eae022ba2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f5238f416f69c282caa09bc226ffbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99992d12911944db6172dcc6b2ae4ab5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41abaceb8097519bba26a5ccb4274c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ca5b72e1693d958a1e3c385272e963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51dc10f7cf6f3ff9bea2eb170cf1c4dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16970d294fd2c64906945840f8f4c3ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0de2e33b17c8bed0fb16624ad72fab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-916bbd63b5bfa86ff2fa9073870d300d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a89d07e7c36f6a7d1b3f9ac2e0c0baf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8e06f7fcece5e199a44dcbdcbf9d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699f7379e9519e29f504f42bb94daaf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a414888338825a53493117bb9837d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60dcf59d4eb9520c7bf8e9968ecf967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2001ba277158737c9b888248e680d7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594964a698a9063f34a66127a99f84d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a43129b93ff8ead9df972bce81ecbb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a2edce75cc1c84e8d78d82be31fd43b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f231106269a7