    <node id="Accessory Structures">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Structures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessory Structures refer to additional buildings or installations that accompany primary manufactured dwellings, and are designed for various functions within a property. These structures can be either detached or attached to the main building and must adhere to specific size, code allowances, and setback requirements as outlined by local regulations. 

Accessory Structures serve a variety of purposes, including communal use, and may be found in shared spaces such as common greens and courts. Examples of these structures include gazebos, greenhouses, bike parking, and communal facilities like dugouts, concession stands, and restrooms typically associated with recreational areas. The provisions for these structures can include exemptions from certain building standards when they are strategically located far from street lot lines, allowing for more flexibility in their placement.

In matters of regulation, Accessory Structures must conform to the maximum building coverage allowed for dwelling units, and may be subject to additional oversight under conservation rules. Overall, Accessory Structures enhance the functionality and aesthetic of residential areas while providing communal benefits to residents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d6e64b6a4fbfd0d75a94e3d84c045f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4254e6eb792730b58dedb0301cbb63d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af8d828cbb38f1d71e4c9300bd4b4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85949d3f78909228a152d02b0d54f684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c54aa01b8a84d0bf5d8975d9c8cc8b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555b254650c4e6bcde7e85291a2480b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d4506f9183e501d03cc84da18500af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ab64be803cdc30ed89433c92047a024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d735bdaad55969341cee3cca65a09caf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab8e6f4ae4a675657fc86e7ca06a385</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781011</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
