    <node id="Dwelling Unit">
      <data key="d0">Dwelling Unit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Dwelling Unit refers to any structure designed for residential living or for occupancy by individuals or families.&lt;SEP&gt;A dwelling unit is a residential space within a structure that is subject to regulations concerning nonconformity and repair costs.&lt;SEP&gt;A Dwelling Unit is designed for residential occupancy with independent living facilities, excluding congregate housing facilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44500823ae619d4a2c4e588251577618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781067</data>
