    <node id="Walkways">
      <data key="d0">Walkways</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Walkways are paths that link buildings to public sidewalks and transit facilities, essential for pedestrian accessibility in urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97666bfb266fffc44c7d8886ece22a0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Sidewalk">
      <data key="d0">Public Sidewalk</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Sidewalks are walkable paths adjacent to roadways, providing access for pedestrians.&lt;SEP&gt;Public sidewalks are pedestrian pathways adjacent to streets that provide access and connection within urban environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97666bfb266fffc44c7d8886ece22a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcf2b390429bc7c420c7c4a2aa0cb76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Superblock">
      <data key="d0">Superblock</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Superblocks are large urban blocks that may contain multiple ownerships and require specific development and improvement standards for walkways and public areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Superblock is an urban design concept intended to minimize traffic and enhance pedestrian environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A Superblock is a large, continuous area containing a vacated street and private property with a minimum area of 75,000 square feet.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97666bfb266fffc44c7d8886ece22a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84efb40ac49907b061aeb00bb2d08948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Access Easement">
      <data key="d0">Public Access Easement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A public access easement allows public access to walkways within superblocks, ensuring connectivity for pedestrians.&lt;SEP&gt;A public access easement allows public entry to certain areas, such as walkways, ensuring community access.&lt;SEP&gt;Public access easements allow public access to shared areas and must be included in street tracts and other shared facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A public access easement is a legal right allowing the public to access certain areas such as sidewalks and roadways.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Access Easement is a legal right that allows the public to access certain land for specific purposes, defined in Planning and Zoning.&lt;SEP&gt;A Public Access Easement is a legal right granted to the public to use designated land areas for specific purposes, such as travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97666bfb266fffc44c7d8886ece22a0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8f030c470408395d5811f58b93edb14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfe18720ad9b5bf5dadab610a40b064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22acd36bdbe56e46354926a0904b7463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028c3c84ee58774048f304cfbc47c40a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Phased Development">
      <data key="d0">Phased Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Phased development refers to a construction approach where improvements are made in stages rather than all at once, particularly in large projects such as superblocks.</data>
