    <node id="Major Public Trails">
      <data key="d0">Major Public Trails</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Major Public Trails signify pathways designated for public use, often connecting various community areas and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Major Public Trails designate pathways intended for public use and recreational purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Major Public Trails are designated pathways intended for recreation and transportation by the general public.&lt;SEP&gt;Major public trails are designated routes that must comply with specific zoning regulations and may require easements for public use.&lt;SEP&gt;Major public trails are public access points along the Willamette River, intended to comply with the Comprehensive Plan and Willamette Greenway Plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Major public trails are designated pathways that facilitate public access along the Willamette River and the South Waterfront.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95bbc1bcc87570cccffede2c40cb383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4749d2209607255edbe985025b727249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2341ab772a74f1ba57e44df79eb3af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Willamette Greenway Plan">
      <data key="d0">Willamette Greenway Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Willamette Greenway Plan outlines requirements for landscaping and development to support riverbank and ecological health.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Plan outlines requirements for public access, view corridors, and maintaining natural habitats along the Willamette River.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Plan serves as a framework for managing the riverine environment along the Willamette River.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Plan focuses on the management and development of the Willamette River’s surrounding areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Plan includes guidelines to ensure access to the Willamette River and its natural resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Plan includes provisions for the preservation and development of scenic and recreational resources along the Willamette River.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c3e12ec08ee12d0c625c3b66e539b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7707c48b1e017649ebd08fb25641c1ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba31ae20af3e709ad848c12217e0c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2341ab772a74f1ba57e44df79eb3af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768780998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.272">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.272</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.272 specifies regulations for Major Public Trails, highlighting their purpose and application.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.272 sets forth the guidelines for public recreational trails and viewpoint requirements along the Willamette River.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.272 pertains to regulations regarding public trails, detailing requirements for viewpoints associated with major public trails.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.272 refers to specific legal regulations relating to Major Public Trails.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-877a823bd216070dbe9fd06f8befc552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc3a467f6b0a5b8fd0489088a17ca2d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2341ab772a74f1ba57e44df79eb3af</data>
