    </node>
    <node id="Maximum Building Coverage">
      <data key="d0">Maximum Building Coverage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum Building Coverage refers to the limits set on the coverage area of a building relative to the lot size, detailed in section 33.110.225.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum Building Coverage indicates the percentage of the site area that can be occupied by buildings, capped at 50% in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum Building Coverage refers to the regulation that limits the amount of site area that can be covered by buildings to 70%.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum Building Coverage refers to the limit placed on the area of a subdistrict that can be occupied by buildings to reduce impervious surfaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf0622768a7546eddc23c9aaa3ef4edb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f3910d4b4ea8a4a76516cfd107b355</data>
