    <node id="Type IV Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Type IV Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Type IV procedure involves reviews that require specialized attention, with recommendations made to the City Council.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV Procedure is used for reviewing proposals to demolish significant historic resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV procedure is a classification applicable to certain reviews, which has priority over others in the application process.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV Procedure is a classification indicating a more complex review process for land use matters.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV Procedure applies to specific types of land use reviews necessitating final action from the City Council.&lt;SEP&gt;Type IV Procedure is a specific processing method for all other proposals to demolish historic resources outside specific landmark classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69705150e078dd993ef14bd699a3bc12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614d099bcb8d71cfc787e0cbccc1ebbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bde6fb397c7366841124f779d183b6c</data>
