    <node id="Chapter 33.258">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.258</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.258 pertains to regulations governing Nonconforming Uses and Development, primarily influencing existing uses that do not comply with current zoning and development standards. This chapter specifically targets pre-existing uses and conditions that are classified as nonconforming, meaning they were permissible under earlier regulations but now violate current standards.

The regulations in Chapter 33.258 are applicable across various contexts, including market gardens, food membership distribution sites, and manufactured dwelling parks. It outlines specific requirements and reviews for these nonconforming situations, ensuring that they align with current planning and zoning regulations. Additionally, Chapter 33.258 addresses nonconforming situations in relation to occupied recreational vehicles, which became a focus as of October 24, 2025.

Moreover, the chapter provides guidance on nonconforming developments within greenway zones, indicating its comprehensive nature in addressing various aspects of urban development and zoning issues. Overall, Chapter 33.258 serves as a crucial regulatory framework for managing and guiding nonconforming uses and developments within the jurisdiction it governs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc573198faf9c1b51eb551532d91476d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5348591467a41c77d858f5dbd717c172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab78bf22476f90e50de5d511279727d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b31593c6056a4c4b7b5e1b873010f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a997e1b200b6816ddf145fba6c1929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-250f22c8b2433134e7522ccaf4bb55d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781003</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Service Storage">
      <data key="d0">Self-Service Storage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-Service Storage refers to a type of facility where individuals and businesses can rent space for the purpose of storing personal belongings or property. These facilities offer private units that individuals can access to keep their items secure. The primary function of Self-Service Storage is to provide designated areas for storage, allowing for ease of use and convenience.

Self-Service Storage facilities are subject to specific regulations and zoning laws, which dictate their establishment and operations. Certain areas, particularly near transit stations and within the Prime Industrial overlay zone, may prohibit the construction of these storage facilities. This means that while Self-Service Storage units are widely available, they are restricted in specific locations to maintain zoning integrity.

Overall, Self-Service Storage encompasses rental spaces that cater to diverse storage needs, ensuring that both individuals and businesses have access to secure and private storage solutions while adhering to established local guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91d7d14eda63788f4ff6c8272574de63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd57b33ee4fb90b8e15b4036d8b2f9e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f6c68627201b6a0d63e0a73012b8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b98f4030f1ba695567caadac80f6cd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781003</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temporary Disturbance Areas">
      <data key="d0">Temporary Disturbance Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Temporary disturbance areas refer to zones that must be planted with native species to mitigate environmental impact during construction.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary disturbance areas refer to regions that undergo temporary changes and must be replanted to achieve vegetation cover.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-539f4010f687efe24bc7e2b559aec360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc5413a0ad23895c5bdcf3326ac8a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781003</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Golf Course Vegetation">
      <data key="d0">Golf Course Vegetation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Golf course vegetation includes the plants used within golf courses, which may include native and non-native species based on specific planning standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-539f4010f687efe24bc7e2b559aec360</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
