    <node id="Commercial Outdoor Recreation">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Outdoor Recreation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial Outdoor Recreation refers to activities and facilities that provide outdoor recreational opportunities for profit. This category includes a range of recreational activities and spaces that are managed for public use, emphasizing engagement in various outdoor settings. It typically involves recreational activities that are organized within specific zones, such as the Prime Industrial overlay zone, which may impose size limitations on these activities.

In urban planning contexts, Commercial Outdoor Recreation is recognized as a permitted use within the Central City Plan District, subject to various outlined requirements to ensure compliance with local regulatory frameworks. The sector encompasses both small-scale and larger outdoor activities, including amusement parks and driving ranges, which offer entertainment and recreational services to the community.

Further, Commercial Outdoor Recreation specifically addresses outdoor urban spaces with facilities that support recreational services, while also adhering to regulations concerning parking and accessibility. This entity represents a vital contributor to outdoor amenity-based businesses, providing opportunities for leisure and physical activity while fostering economic benefits through tourism and community engagement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91d7d14eda63788f4ff6c8272574de63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33d0f030f285a86371b78f7278eb5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5a24cd6c84e70b31e0e64f3773ddd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-467b12ebf0546021f51b7429432586d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7707c48b1e017649ebd08fb25641c1ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781003</data>
      <data key="d6" />
