    <node id="Single-Dwelling Zones">
      <data key="d0">Single-Dwelling Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Single-Dwelling Zones are specific zoning classifications that designate areas for residential use, primarily focused on single-family residential development. These zones are regulated by distinct zoning regulations that dictate allowed uses, development standards, and construction guidelines for residential properties within these areas. They are designed to preserve land for housing, providing opportunities for individual households, while ensuring that development aligns with community standards.

The regulations surrounding Single-Dwelling Zones aim to maintain a certain scale, privacy, and aesthetic harmony between residences. This includes governing aspects such as building heights and setbacks, which are vital for appropriate development in residential neighborhoods. By imposing these standards, Single-Dwelling Zones help maintain the character of the community and protect the integrity of residential areas.

Under Title 33, Planning and Zoning, Single-Dwelling Zones are specifically outlined to ensure that living spaces are organized and function according to the intended use of these designated areas. In summary, Single-Dwelling Zones play a crucial role in urban planning and land use management, helping to create balanced and harmonious residential environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf0622768a7546eddc23c9aaa3ef4edb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4254e6eb792730b58dedb0301cbb63d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f013869c1ec32a0acb630a40f63c4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ffebbe5f5a48ace7018e8814873e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5348591467a41c77d858f5dbd717c172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-619bfdcc25aa9b9b415e2291e2bb9041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8df1a5c0d5ee049ecbdb2f03fc22c2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781004</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Official Zoning Maps">
      <data key="d0">Official Zoning Maps</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Official Zoning Maps serve as essential documents that visually illustrate the zoning designations and regulations applicable to specific sites within a jurisdiction, particularly within the City of Portland. These maps highlight designated zoning areas, including various classifications and overlays, which are critical for effective land use and urban planning.

These maps are authoritative resources that delineate the boundaries of multiple zoning districts, including but not limited to the Albina Community Plan District, Glendoveer Plan District, Guild's Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District, Hayden Island Plan District, Macadam Plan District, and York Plan District. Each map provides a visual representation of the varying zoning classifications as well as specialized areas such as historical landmarks and recreational trails.

The Official Zoning Maps also indicate sites that are subject to additional zoning regulations, particularly those involving overlay zones and plan districts. This includes locations recognized as National Register Landmarks, which notably impact local zoning and development proposals. By doing so, they ensure compliance with city regulations and assist in identifying required improvements relevant to development in designated areas.

These maps are not static; they may require updates to reflect corrections based on mapping errors and changes in local policies or regulations. Overall, the Official Zoning Maps are indispensable tools for city planners, developers, and stakeholders involved in urban development and land use, providing clarity and guidance on zoning laws and potential development opportunities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b77524960029823e92ccf376410363d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb991309bb84fc2868a6a6763b75b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ce54762dd350a2baa6b3563a59fff3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ea2fd8fad365f45c78f675d0630e553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-423bb58a4673879619218c3271a171e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851e46c6798be63a5ed200499e9b955d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdaeb46ee0afe6f8cbf449de5ce1578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2e828d0ef40701ea87d62c0b01bd2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003da3accff48fefdd77c15c879c2fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f06b0977a1322293e0781ce406d337f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d67d6ae3fefc0ae11f57c206f31b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fb2898717814420d5eea2fb274a45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d1801c38b4789f81c89f16cc033283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b121eab358b392062623a0c2554b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec40727e0d8bf940e01c40131ec7d220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab68c6faa3af9af6f5cd876312e30c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-721ec91bd394c742ab66be71cc2391f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c50fc0ff9e807e9d3489aba2b4c9f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d66ea593dc4ac52ad4236580e597c48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495d4288ccdffd88f955433753aaad68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-386ae62e0f06be64c345a3fd84815c6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835e0969f1f8d22f5d245f2db0653852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda537024724fbc12582034b555f1424</data>
