    <node id="Major Event Entertainment">
      <data key="d0">Major Event Entertainment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Major Event Entertainment refers to large-scale entertainment events that attract significant attendance and participation. This term encompasses various activities designed to engage large audiences, often focused on spectator activities. Such events can include concerts, festivals, exhibitions, and other public gatherings intended for enjoyment.

Within this framework, Major Event Entertainment is associated with specific venues and activities that require substantial space, often necessitating appropriate zoning permissions. For instance, large-scale events are permitted in designated areas, such as Subdistrict A, provided they are developed alongside hotels. However, it is important to note that Major Event Entertainment is prohibited in certain zones, such as the Prime Industrial overlay zone, thereby highlighting the need for compliance with local regulations.

In urban planning contexts, Major Event Entertainment is acknowledged as an allowed use in areas like the Central City Plan District, where it must adhere to specific guidelines. This strategic placement contributes to cultural engagement and enhances the vibrancy of urban areas through organized public events that foster community interaction and enjoyment. Overall, Major Event Entertainment plays a crucial role in attracting large crowds and delivering memorable experiences aimed at public enjoyment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91d7d14eda63788f4ff6c8272574de63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a373581b2a74183e9eed060dd888030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a901459905390cbd8ce9c02b74a9fd1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-467b12ebf0546021f51b7429432586d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7707c48b1e017649ebd08fb25641c1ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781005</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Portland Housing Bureau">
      <data key="d0">Portland Housing Bureau</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Portland Housing Bureau (PHB) is the governing body responsible for overseeing housing policies, regulations, and affordability standards in the city of Portland. It plays a crucial role in ensuring that housing developments comply with established affordability requirements, thereby supporting initiatives for affordable housing throughout the region.

The bureau certifies that developments meet the affordability criteria necessary for various housing projects, including compliance with inclusionary housing regulations. This certification is essential for developers seeking to participate in programs that allow for the transfer of floor area ratios (FAR) and ensure adherence to income restrictions for group living units. Additionally, the Portland Housing Bureau manages the Affordable Housing Fund, which finances affordable housing initiatives and collects related fees, including those for bonus floor area transactions.

In its regulatory capacity, the Portland Housing Bureau oversees the implementation of housing assistance programs and housing regulations. It provides guidance for compliance within developments, including those participating in specialized programs such as the System Development Charges Exemption Program. The PHB's responsibilities also extend to updating fee schedules associated with housing developments and certifying that projects align with the area's median family income requirements.

Overall, the Portland Housing Bureau serves as a pivotal entity in promoting affordable housing, ensuring compliance with relevant regulations, and providing financial support to achieve housing objectives in Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf0622768a7546eddc23c9aaa3ef4edb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e038f4d3687c0baca987d663a82852cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-903ef5f8da50cf2a59819dcb0eda03b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586262724750ed4bbb098ac0aed41049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f57fb6953e9769254bb5d2a323550c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c8009e101b1c5acef3b9262a76129e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861d2a39c6243daf2d9eb704cb764a04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5adc4cb7aae3d0001c977968b8799a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a962491a7cd2c102b96a01ffc8d4cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-916fae91f6b0da087cc62a6bce573a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c815f0219b3fa08de12163f428266e23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bcd05068dc776f6a4ff3953570df7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee4ba726d698227e002aae5c6cc82e38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd455847ef176484b9b460a4062a8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1347219a19de2480f10b4ab0d1cc91d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94342616311fab47b2c9483e52cd9046&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14dcd96a6f149344a7f8451f7533b386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7525c3c81ec880dec86a378f065ef6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64ae29063e6b41ec74fbbe9839ad342b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93214ee5c49fbb5384175df60c9eafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04d6cd35d45d8e93ff5e834df187ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2c7926ceca17c4d0d7614d1c8acec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc22ba039a9fe91f1dbd58c1c542c993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26d97abf5771d4460162667c195b262f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7afd4cd98781a0f8a75a7fa3cd365098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059e05beab69bbb7d4dc82bdd6ddff25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49acd712739227babe51a65cf9f9e8be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a043b4f466e82f380e009054fb98e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5aa8dbd7b64b3d8748a623b93037d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e1d49f86df4a02f01af7661478e4005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dfa716b92fafe3e0c5a60967fdfe220</data>
