    <node id="EX Zone">
      <data key="d0">EX Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The EX Zone is a zoning designation with a multifaceted framework intended to shape development practices in specified areas. It governs a range of factors, including floor area ratios, building setbacks, and exterior design standards aimed at maintaining the zone’s character and ensuring public safety. The EX Zone is characterized by its regulations that require street-facing facades to feature windows that enhance visibility, alongside pedestrian-friendly standards that promote active street life.

As an employment zone, the EX Zone enforces specific restrictions on exterior displays of goods and activities, prohibiting drive-through facilities to align with its intended urban design. It encompasses regulations that apply to outdoor shelters, similar to those in the C zone, and includes criteria for self-service storage facilities, reinforcing the zone's focus on controlled uses consistent with its employment purpose.

In the context of the St. Johns Plan District, the EX Zone also permits certain exceptions for exterior finish materials while maintaining regulations to mitigate conflicts between residential and industrial activities. It restricts residential uses to ensure compatibility with its primarily industrial character, and it includes provisions for the review of new mass shelters and alterations as either allowed or conditional uses.

Parking regulations within the EX Zone are specifically tailored, including maximum limits on parking spaces based on type of usage, as well as parking standards related to the streetcar alignment. The zone mandates that each lot maintain a front lot line of at least 10 feet, ensuring consistency in land use, dimensional requirements, and structural integrity.

Overall, the EX Zone embodies a regulatory framework balancing industrial employment needs with urban design standards to foster a coherent and functional environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-538cbb82e531686918c327bce0b104f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33d0f030f285a86371b78f7278eb5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfa11b893b09fc1fb7d6655be073aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e927f3c64b3afc1f943e861ae4fac76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1267f51ecc30ce027ed225a2c473621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b06e985a4445f1b158ef2343cff5b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37ff07ffa7013303eef3ff22ca4c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422a1c7b762d9ab38fe2197b504ec353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9a5a4577f7544b4671be7b0e59a2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8233be0787d6dbf29673028851524520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7</data>
