    <node id="R20 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R20 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The R20 zone is a regulatory area that imposes certain residential development standards, including width and height limitations for structures.&lt;SEP&gt;The R20 Zone requires a minimum lot area of 12,000 square feet for dwellings.&lt;SEP&gt;The R20 Zone permits one accessory dwelling unit per site with a house or manufactured home when certain lot size conditions are met.&lt;SEP&gt;The R20 zone is a residential zoning classification requiring a minimum lot area for accessory dwelling units.&lt;SEP&gt;The R20 Zone is a residential zoning classification that typically allows for single-family dwellings on larger lots.&lt;SEP&gt;The R20 Zone is a zoning category in Portland that allows specific types of residential development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5af8d828cbb38f1d71e4c9300bd4b4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d3dc1f275b21f3a0c1622695839a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e889d237f01a5093e629880a38d5a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe92a3f46b3bfc4baa1f040d200709a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fee5077b9b5bae2a7dec413478071a4</data>
