    </node>
    <node id="Landscaped Area">
      <data key="d0">Landscaped Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The landscaped area is defined as a designated space on a property that must adhere to specific depth and aesthetic standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaped area requirements stipulate the percentage of the site that must be designated for landscaping.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaped Area mandates a minimum of 15 percent of a site to be landscaped, with stipulations for exemption based on housing types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5af8d828cbb38f1d71e4c9300bd4b4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05299df3decd7e8061aff48bb1ba2029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2574af8787db7883bc15da7cbabd3a3b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781008</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Base Height">
      <data key="d0">Base Height</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Base Height is the standard height allowed for buildings in multi-dwelling zones, which varies based on specific conditions and zoning classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-199bdfd5f31802f14bb3bd7efff3a92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-753992cd5e3f8a1085d378bbba8d5aab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781008</data>
      <data key="d6" />
