      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chimneys and Vents">
      <data key="d0">Chimneys and Vents</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Chimneys and Vents are structural elements that may extend above the height limit under specific conditions outlined in zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-199bdfd5f31802f14bb3bd7efff3a92e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Design Commission">
      <data key="d0">Design Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Design Commission is an authority dedicated to enhancing public views and skyline diversity by providing design advice for various building proposals. This entity is crucial in the urban planning landscape of the Central City, as it evaluates and approves design proposals in adherence to established urban planning standards. Its responsibilities extend to reviewing design proposals within the North Interstate Plan District and the Northwest Master Plans, where it makes recommendations based on approval criteria.

Composed of seven members with specific qualifications, the Design Commission focuses on urban design and planning, offering leadership and expertise in these areas. The commission is instrumental in advancing the objectives of the Design overlay zone, which includes managing design guidelines specific to this zone and making pertinent recommendations to the City Council. 

Additionally, the Design Commission serves as a review body that assists in various decisions related to design and land use. It provides advice on design matters corresponding to land use requests and evaluates land use reviews according to specific procedural classifications. The commission is also involved in the legislative process, reviewing design standards and guidelines. Finally, it plays a proactive role in initiating amendments regarding these design guidelines, ensuring that the urban landscape evolves in a thoughtful and community-oriented manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69705150e078dd993ef14bd699a3bc12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b04cb33b3135ed3ccce916cd1c14a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d42b3010c15664b1fb208cc57e4facc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa5d2c57a95ae65f663a55f78fa3c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614d099bcb8d71cfc787e0cbccc1ebbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94342616311fab47b2c9483e52cd9046&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3687e34f528a78261767a8a0c1b6b6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc65f441d5b262a6e985063f42142907&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbf21d0ccd80cdf97bfee50d738455e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parking Area Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Parking Area Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking Area Regulations encompass standards and limitations for vehicle areas, including paving ratios and landscaping requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
