    <node id="Cascade Station/Portland International Center Plan District">
      <data key="d0">Cascade Station/Portland International Center Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cascade Station/Portland International Center Plan District is a designated planning area that encompasses the regions around Cascade Station and the Portland International Airport. This district is characterized by its distinct regulations regarding environmental zones, which include provisions for environmental and archaeological protections.

Serving as an overarching regulatory framework, the Cascade Station/Portland International Center Plan District includes Subdistrict A and outlines comprehensive development regulations applicable to both Subdistrict A and Subdistrict B. It influences various aspects of urban development, establishing specific land use regulations and requirements designed to guide growth and ensure sustainable practices in the area.

As part of its regulatory framework, the district mandates additional requirements for Transportation Impact Review applications, further asserting its role in overseeing urban planning and development processes. This plan district is vital in shaping the future development patterns within the Cascade Station vicinity, ensuring that environmental considerations and urban standards are well integrated into the planning efforts surrounding this strategic area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ceb5a192403b5b7a44ecca67568f01e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49a157902a76856c95e4e3a050a0ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cac4e6c1ba756a5bcff3c73c0fac10d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356d9265a5791545fa23fa54dee260f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16970d294fd2c64906945840f8f4c3ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113b51830712d7fe9de4004e74bb2601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-268246cbdbedd45b9a4db8cc36f29346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-905eb1c23a4b49a15e210b092e4ce855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d532a006f3aa47075d5f58cb0d7da4e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbee049dd9c661ea5a90ad39db328689</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781010</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Design Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">Design Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Design Overlay Zone is a regulatory framework that applies specific design standards to designated areas within urban planning and zoning. Its primary purpose is to promote architectural consistency and enhance aesthetic quality in developments. This designation is particularly relevant in commercial zones, where it ensures that new constructions and renovations align with established design requirements to integrate seamlessly into the urban fabric.

Within the Design Overlay Zone, additional zoning classifications may be applied, such as the Institutional Residential zone. The regulations specify enhanced design standards that must be adhered to for building projects, especially those located near historic landmarks. These standards not only govern the visual characteristics of new buildings but also influence the usability and accessibility of public spaces.

The Design Overlay Zone encompasses specific areas outlined by city planning regulations, where developments are subject to a more rigorous review process led by the Design Commission. This oversight guarantees that projects maintain high standards of design excellence and contribute positively to civic life and community aesthetic values. 

Overall, the Design Overlay Zone serves as a crucial element in urban development by ensuring that building designs within its jurisdiction meet particular standards, thus striving to enhance the visual quality of the environment and support the overall goals of urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69705150e078dd993ef14bd699a3bc12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff526385a57c5befe6ca7788e86d560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dbe6361f50442dc594b220f21f6d49e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c8009e101b1c5acef3b9262a76129e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d3dc1f275b21f3a0c1622695839a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f92d57fd526433c19e4bdb08e2032fe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b04cb33b3135ed3ccce916cd1c14a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c96a1e5b1eb94f3a586e5986daa73c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207bdd149614a77764e1c1161b9089e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faa24df5ddab0e7d0172ca67c9e0da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34a0bcc2ef40b300fb0774b97f4e1e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da53bf3df44bfaaa6ca8a2fda0a65fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cf98dff4ee5559ad6fd84e90727c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a93319af7a8f643cc123f328935418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-956eaa56417e66522506a103f450e0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495d4288ccdffd88f955433753aaad68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781011</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic Resource Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">Historic Resource Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Historic Resource Overlay Zone is a designated area established to protect and preserve resources of significant historical value through specific zoning regulations. This zone aims to manage the preservation of historic landmarks and resources, ensuring that their cultural and historical significance is safeguarded for future generations.

This overlay zone incorporates regulations governing the demolition and alteration of historic structures, influencing building and renovation standards within its boundaries. It acts as a framework for the preservation and review of historic resources, offering guidelines that help maintain the architectural integrity and character of these important sites. The regulations specify the types of modifications that are acceptable, allowing for some modern adaptations, such as the installation of solar energy systems, provided they conform to the historic character of the area.

The Historic Resource Overlay Zone thus serves multiple purposes: it not only regulates alterations and demolitions to historic structures but also designates areas for preservation, dictating particular standards and requirements for development. By focusing on significant historic resources, the zone works to balance the needs of modern development with the necessity of preserving historical integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-516f4309419d52a2c0f6920e39b0dbdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d4fb6204c8defda427d1f8fff2f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ee11d492136a3cb6116df2011b3bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd349cb529fd5cf21e341790c05e4bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851e46c6798be63a5ed200499e9b955d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-053c11d4643f486fc50c6afdae4be2ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74ebc7af6a19551e094bffa65ccb3a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-992925c33f931f469018e63e676d862e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f72437166c353de768d234823279f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bdd0a72bd1cfe3ef9d36a7ad4b1bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-250f22c8b2433134e7522ccaf4bb55d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781011</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Building Setbacks">
      <data key="d0">Building Setbacks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Building Setbacks are regulatory measures that determine the minimum distance buildings must be positioned away from property boundaries and public streets, particularly in residential zones. These regulations play a crucial role in urban planning by ensuring adequate space between structures and facilitating essential functions such as accessibility, light, and privacy within neighborhoods.

The concept of Building Setbacks also involves specific guidelines that vary based on factors such as building height and the zoning of the area. For instance, the required setbacks may differ for residential, commercial, or mixed-use developments, with adjustments made to maintain the character of neighborhoods and enhance overall land usage. 

Furthermore, Building Setbacks are instrumental in shaping architectural design, as they influence the placement of structures on a given lot. They dictate how close or far buildings can be from property lines, thereby affecting not only individual properties but also the overall aesthetic and functionality of a community. Special considerations are often made for setbacks along transit streets or in pedestrian zones, where urban density and foot traffic require additional planning efforts. 

Overall, Building Setbacks serve to uphold community standards by governing the spatial relationship between buildings and their surroundings, promoting safety, environmental considerations, and harmonious development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4254e6eb792730b58dedb0301cbb63d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97c549f439b335c735e299563e1e4c63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb810e875d66f848b351a4f1271e2a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4271bb9cc0287dcb0b401b760eb4864e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78755af7dcf0cbd31bb8a59f246d601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04d6cd35d45d8e93ff5e834df187ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d4506f9183e501d03cc84da18500af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b06e985a4445f1b158ef2343cff5b0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781011</data>
