    <node id="Historic Resource Review">
      <data key="d0">Historic Resource Review</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic Resource Review is a comprehensive procedural assessment designed to evaluate the historic significance of alterations or developments within designated historic boundaries. This process examines proposed changes to Conservation Landmarks and other contributing resources, ensuring compliance with established historical preservation standards.

The Historic Resource Review encompasses a set of regulations that govern modifications affecting the historical significance of historic properties. It is required for the designation and review of changes to both historic landmarks and conservation landmarks. Before any changes such as relocation or demolition are permitted, the historic value of the landmark must be assessed through this process.

This review is particularly crucial within Conservation Districts and National Register Districts, where it is employed to evaluate resources prior to alterations. In a National Register District, applicants may voluntarily engage in the Historic Resource Review to potentially qualify for exemptions from certain demolition reviews. The process is formalized to ensure that any changes to recognized historic structures or sites are critically assessed against established criteria and procedures.

Overall, the Historic Resource Review serves as a regulatory mechanism aimed at conserving and enhancing the significance of historic resources, ensuring that any proposed modifications align with the goals of historical preservation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-516f4309419d52a2c0f6920e39b0dbdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b56b9fdbb25d0d73793d586c98486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851e46c6798be63a5ed200499e9b955d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdaeb46ee0afe6f8cbf449de5ce1578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bc900b38790ffcdef889113926820f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08792af032c7577571c2943db7371a28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd455847ef176484b9b460a4062a8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5aa8dbd7b64b3d8748a623b93037d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dfa716b92fafe3e0c5a60967fdfe220</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781012</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial/Mixed Use Zones">
      <data key="d0">Commercial/Mixed Use Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial/Mixed Use Zones are designated areas intended for a combination of residential, retail, and commercial uses, supporting a blend of diverse activities within urban settings. These zones allow for a mix of commercial and residential developments under specific zoning regulations and planning standards, encouraging inclusivity in land use. 

The zoning classifications for Commercial/Mixed Use Zones enable flexibility in development, accommodating various types of commercial and mixed-use enterprises. Within these zones, particular regulations apply concerning development density and land use, often promoting a balance that incorporates industrial and agricultural services alongside consumer-oriented commercial activities. 

Current urban planning strategies identify Commercial/Mixed Use Zones as areas where certain development and zoning regulations are enforced, including potential Transportation Impact Reviews to assess transportation effects related to new developments. This fosters not only residential options but also the integration of businesses and services in a manner that enhances community interaction and economic vitality while adhering to planning frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30084c591a498854d4f7f08382fe2aff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a966c4eaabe25aca0a1be25bd188299e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aafe5a7a2907664ceccb93037cc2fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8491ef6a94a83bd06029a3a52c0a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8dedd6570aca440bb011dbffebca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ee84d998824c1408d6153086fc99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652d83d3265624b311b9bf8c778fdd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcf2b390429bc7c420c7c4a2aa0cb76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90656f21118fd0ad7c0ee7822eac4d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3994dbc2c6f464ef189000d5ce6654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7282e754cd453819f3e67c09c8e7a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbee049dd9c661ea5a90ad39db328689</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781013</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Type II Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Type II Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Type II Procedure is a defined review process widely utilized for a variety of modifications, applications, and land use scenarios that do not meet the criteria for Type III Procedures. This procedure specifically addresses nonconforming situations, allowing for the review of conditional uses based on established criteria that relate to existing structures and institutional uses.

The Type II Procedure is applicable for various types of conditional uses, including those related to mass and short-term shelters situated within structures that have been in place for at least five years. It governs processes related to infrastructure developments such as roads and septic systems, and it encompasses various public infrastructure and development considerations within specific zones, like the Pleasant Valley overlay zone. Moreover, it facilitates environmental reviews required for activities within the Airport Subdistrict.

Additionally, the Type II Procedure allows for minor adjustments to the PIR Master Plan and is utilized for processing changes in Planned Unit Developments, with distinct review criteria in comparison to other types. This simplified quasi-judicial review method is designed for scenarios that require less discretionary judgment and lower potential impacts, while still including provisions for appeals concerning decisions made by the Director of Planning, Projects, and Development (PP&amp;D).

Furthermore, it serves as a classification for land use reviews that adhere to specific regulations within the overall planning framework. The Type II Procedure provides protocols for processing amendments to resource plans not previously delineated and is involved in Central City Parking Reviews, where it follows defined criteria. It also incorporates provisions for reviewing helicopter landing facilities, assessing changes related to flight operations, and processing minor amendments regarding historic designs or structures along with tree preservation requests.

Overall, the Type II Procedure represents a versatile and essential framework in land use planning, allowing for various forms of development and modification that require structured evaluation while ensuring the integrity of existing community standards and environmental protections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69705150e078dd993ef14bd699a3bc12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a98088aa848c3a646425801c36c9f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a10cf031f788aa8206369e4c6c630d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c232ce107cc5a0bd00a23892d69d0561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4263b41e43a7e8a83f6017fb2cf1c50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86ce100d88532ab8ca2f1d785c9a636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2dff9267506b3019f40d39ac0b51e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e5352641a4a29255f045f1ffa49de30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614d099bcb8d71cfc787e0cbccc1ebbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b28b182d587540c8cdc8788f751c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96815c5a54ec29fd3986869ba3cf59e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a93319af7a8f643cc123f328935418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd54e5b638113595ce88bbc6ccf94bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ca5fc3d28aa819abc484b86dc468ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49961939512caa6917f2206eb92e7d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4670488f256f231024de0291feeec277&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f976aff1b8a931aa89584cca89b6bd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a4fda2a7ebb04a6a59cff745526b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644152b6276c54299003f76b5630241f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9157cebcd51ea7cec9c5bd83c0f3df47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23bdb6b78c43cbe3cee1a2bacbb57a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bde6fb397c7366841124f779d183b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa7a4d254279e02d605594ebe069be0</data>
