    <node id="Portland Plant List">
      <data key="d0">Portland Plant List</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Portland Plant List is a comprehensive documentation outlining various native, non-native, and nuisance plants that are relevant to landscaping standards within the Portland area. It serves as a critical resource for urban planning and environmental management, detailing plant species that are recommended for use in landscaping and restoration projects. The list encompasses both native trees and shrubs, along with guidelines for their selection based on specific environmental conditions and regulations.

The Portland Plant List includes a well-curated collection of native plant species that must be planted as part of development projects and environmental restoration efforts, particularly within designated zones such as the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone. It identifies both acceptable native plants as well as nuisance and prohibited species that must be removed prior to landscaping activities. This dual focus on promotion and restriction helps ensure compliance with local environmental guidelines.

Moreover, the list specifies plants that are applicable for use in mitigation areas, temporary disturbance areas, and replanting in violation areas, thereby enhancing ecological integrity and promoting sustainable landscaping practices. Native vegetation that can be planted using hand-held equipment is also acknowledged, supporting accessibility in environmental management efforts.

In addition to native species, the Portland Plant List classifies various nuisance plants and outlines the removal requirements as per development regulations. By providing this classification, the list aids in maintaining a balanced ecosystem while reinforcing compliance with urban landscaping laws. This makes the Portland Plant List an essential reference for anyone involved in landscaping, environmental remediation, or urban development within the city.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-539f4010f687efe24bc7e2b559aec360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0081003d43e7b772e5a8d3dfae39548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64960cc4adf91b7f6ea0964bf7f6dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a10cf031f788aa8206369e4c6c630d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2762500c7c689febd52ecacda4e0e39d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20addac2bd7bf67d0c780bffff45e581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f92d42feaabfd545cc35264c76fbed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370bd3a55fe045150292fe6445463a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2325c884efc6a13f1b84583326ff8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-899c4b9a2ac9d3d9713b5cef39a863b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfece86ae05751fbebb6324df767074f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356d9265a5791545fa23fa54dee260f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90974c5207e30c3839f91710f5169ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32085ee92ea490a135a4678599552bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b95c123bc42f5e9142018f60381ac37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b0b9956e9369e20a5f76498419272b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e460c58e359f4aa61eae2678eeb2a806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d39e794ab5c802105ac492ea170724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc5413a0ad23895c5bdcf3326ac8a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc3fc3ad91ea490a2f8ffb98e83e2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77c0e594bc319fd143848146f9ea56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ff3afda2034b66968957b4926a887c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe16dacd4c0cb29ef445c2340ee2812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9fa7bda2d110e7a4636f9b2c3016a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc38fc86828ecd90586e33007486e5d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8f7b7f798d73271c022ea233a96a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059e173ef884a58e8cd223998e6158d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d11d225e5566d1ff994f2025b1378ec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490cb02a9aa37ab5ed0231106009cb20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d37b0db2824c732a3a9a02ff910d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f85b49addeceea917b6328493401bacc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-198e1551ae650afd9098fb33de845850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8e044b1fd94ca567e1458bbd0323ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da06ccf2e9fcb917a0a33d7f94dc73f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fbbf35a5a5146ae4034375e7576374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dc64b571fc1e4051ea286aa94de68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c56c223dd5b