    <node id="Title 33 Planning and Zoning">
      <data key="d0">Title 33 Planning and Zoning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 33 Planning and Zoning serves as the regulatory framework governing land use and development within a specific jurisdiction. This framework establishes standards and procedures designed to manage various aspects of urban planning and development, including zoning practices, which detail how land can be utilized across different areas.

The regulations outlined in Title 33 provide comprehensive guidelines for zoning, development standards, and procedures that are pertinent to the implementation of land use policies. These guidelines cover a range of topics including parking and loading management, as well as specific regulations for distinct zones such as commercial, mixed-use, and employment areas. Additionally, Title 33 addresses the management of urban features, such as tree removal and the review of historic elements, which contributes to maintaining the character and integrity of the urban environment.

Overall, Title 33 Planning and Zoning is integral to facilitating organized and sustainable development by ensuring that land use aligns with regulatory standards while considering community needs and preserving important local features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30084c591a498854d4f7f08382fe2aff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05299df3decd7e8061aff48bb1ba2029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bcfb59e4095f5b02abc8ac31213ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b2323b48f41f87137658c4c38c98ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2fc1b73b6e1ae4e82cbaf205ce719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f06b0977a1322293e0781ce406d337f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
