    </node>
    <node id="Dwelling Units">
      <data key="d0">Dwelling Units</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dwelling Units are individual residential spaces on a site, subject to accessibility standards outlined in visitability requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Dwelling Units are residential spaces that must adhere to specific entrance and orientation standards in relation to the Common Outdoor Area.&lt;SEP&gt;Dwelling units refer to residential spaces designated for habitation, which can be calculated based on zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Dwelling units are residential living spaces that must comply with specific design standards in relation to street access.&lt;SEP&gt;Dwelling units are residential structures such as duplexes, triplexes, and fourplexes allowed in specific zoning areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff254476c2742dcdf5c26a1256fd36e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
