    </node>
    <node id="Duplex">
      <data key="d0">Duplex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Duplex is a type of residential building that houses two separate dwelling units, which must follow specific entrance and facade regulations when located on corner lots.&lt;SEP&gt;A duplex is a type of residential building comprising two separate housing units.&lt;SEP&gt;A duplex is a type of residential structure consisting of two dwelling units.&lt;SEP&gt;A Duplex contains two primary dwelling units on one lot that must share a common wall or floor/ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e927f3c64b3afc1f943e861ae4fac76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90656f21118fd0ad7c0ee7822eac4d60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781014</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Triplex">
      <data key="d0">Triplex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A triplex is a residential building containing three separate living units.&lt;SEP&gt;A triplex is a type of residential structure consisting of three dwelling units.&lt;SEP&gt;Triplex refers to a type of residential structure that consists of three living units.&lt;SEP&gt;A triplex is a housing structure consisting of three primary dwelling units on one lot that share common walls or floors/ceilings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e927f3c64b3afc1f943e861ae4fac76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fourplex">
      <data key="d0">Fourplex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A fourplex is a residential building that consists of four separate housing units.&lt;SEP&gt;A fourplex is a type of residential structure consisting of four dwelling units.&lt;SEP&gt;A Fourplex is a structure containing four primary dwelling units on one lot, sharing common walls or floors.&lt;SEP&gt;A fourplex is a type of housing structure that shares common walls or floors/ceilings with at least one other unit and can remain as such even when divided through a middle housing land division.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e927f3c64b3afc1f943e861ae4fac76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Dwelling Structure">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Dwelling Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-dwelling structures refer to buildings containing multiple residential units and have specific rules regarding the Type A accessory short-term rentals.&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-dwelling structure refers to any building that contains multiple residential units.&lt;SEP&gt;A multi-dwelling structure contains five or more dwelling units sharing common walls or floors/ceilings and is not divided into separate lots.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20fcfe46fc9e5d305800a15506d2337f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R Zones">
      <data key="d0">R Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R Zones refer to residential zoning areas that have specific landscaping and setback requirements for exterior displays.&lt;SEP&gt;R zones refer to residential zoning categories allowing specific types of housing developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C Zones">
      <data key="d0">C Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">C zones refer to commercial zoning categories where specific business activities are permitted.&lt;SEP&gt;C Zones are a zoning designation that sets forth land use and development standards relevant to urban planning.&lt;SEP&gt;C Zones are commercial zones that have specific regulations about building setbacks and allowed uses within the Hillsdale Plan District.&lt;SEP&gt;C zones are commercial or mixed-use areas designated for specific types of development, including energy production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de298aa875613309b192e347dc83983f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a773484e51a9cad486454fcfa9ec3959&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03d74d6b9596dd3ca6ee9b83679d2f9e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="E Zones">
      <data key="d0">E Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">E Zones are designated zoning areas subject to specific regulations regarding uses and structures.&lt;SEP&gt;E Zones are designated areas where proposals may substitute ground floor windows with public art under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;E zones indicate employment zones where commercial and industrial activities can occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2020f8cb9e1e9fff0f2699c2142d64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IR Zones">
      <data key="d0">IR Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">IR zones are industrial-restricted areas where specific industrial activities are permitted.&lt;SEP&gt;IR Zones are specialized areas associated with certain land use regulations, particularly for industrial and residential developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a185269200e9d231c5a69d32eb78c8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Office Uses">
      <data key="d0">Office Uses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Office uses pertain to spaces designated for professional and administrative work.&lt;SEP&gt;Office uses refer to spaces designated for business operations that are allowed in both Subdistrict A and Subdistrict B.&lt;SEP&gt;Office uses pertain to business spaces designated for office work, with regulations on parking space allowances.&lt;SEP&gt;Office Uses refer to the approved activities within historic industrial buildings that do not negatively impact the transportation system.&lt;SEP&gt;Office Uses involve office activities that operate in conjunction with primary allowed uses within specified planning zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a373581b2a74183e9eed060dd888030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2df84aea0e28175d739f9e39d7ac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12fb6a1cf486f1a95c94d657ea8ccfeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic or Conservation Landmark">
      <data key="d0">Historic or Conservation Landmark</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic or Conservation Landmarks can allow additional Floor Area Ratio transfer if they meet specific criteria set by regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Historic or Conservation Landmark is a building or site that is recognized for historical significance and is subject to preservation regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic or Conservation Landmarks are significant sites eligible for floor area transfers concerning zoning regulations and historic preservation.&lt;SEP&gt;A Historic or Conservation Landmark is a designated site of historical or cultural significance that may influence development regulations such as FAR transfers.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic or conservation landmarks are designated sites recognized for their historical, cultural, or architectural significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb0a8fdf55836bf22ae8a840cfbe18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567df924f86fd66f127e58c0497a37e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic or Conservation District">
      <data key="d0">Historic or Conservation District</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Historic or Conservation District is an area designated to preserve historical integrity and significance, where specific regulations apply.&lt;SEP&gt;A historic or conservation district is an area with significant historical resources classified for preservation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567df924f86fd66f127e58c0497a37e2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transit Station">
      <data key="d0">Transit Station</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A transit station is a facility where various forms of transportation, such as trains or buses, stop to facilitate passenger boarding.&lt;SEP&gt;A Transit Station is a reference point for site requirements within the Central City Plan District regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transit Station refers to a transport hub within 500 feet of which specific site requirements apply under the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Transit Station is a location referenced for connectivity and access in relation to the internal accessways of the Hayden Island Plan District.&lt;SEP&gt;A Transit Station is a location where light rail vehicles stop to load or unload passengers, consisting of the station platform.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7a46ce2a41072cf8f503e930128f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-467b12ebf0546021f51b7429432586d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7707c48b1e017649ebd08fb25641c1ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bc34687798d2c98cb9455da5ca08306</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manufacturing and Production">
      <data key="d0">Manufacturing and Production</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Manufacturing and Production refers to the activities involved in the production of goods, subject to specific regulations outlined in the input text.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing and Production describes a category of commercial activity focused on the creation of products through processing, assembling, or fabricating.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing and Production involves the processes used to create goods for various markets.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing and Production are activities that may qualify as ground floor active uses under specific zoning guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing and production refer to processes involving the creation and assembly of goods, and are permitted in certain zoning areas under specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b31593c6056a4c4b7b5e1b873010f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1548cc5d56ac0b8d2ab93d83d89c89</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal">
      <data key="d0">Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal is categorized under industrial primary uses in Single-Dwelling Zones, indicating a potential prohibited or allowed use based on regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal is a facility for the storage and transfer of large quantities of fossil fuels.&lt;SEP&gt;A Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal is a facility for storing fuel, necessitating neighborhood contact due to its potential impacts on local communities.&lt;SEP&gt;A bulk fossil fuel terminal is a facility dedicated to the import, export, and storage of fossil fuels in bulk.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminals engage in the transport and bulk storage of fossil fuels and may include activities like fuel blending and wholesaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk fossil fuel terminal refers to facilities engaged in the regional wholesaling and storage of fossil fuels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminal is a facility used for storing and handling fossil fuels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f6c68627201b6a0d63e0a73012b8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b658cbfd18f3e2a99c1c4a3af5c0505</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Waste-Related">
      <data key="d0">Waste-Related</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Waste-Related activities are designated under industrial primary uses in Single-Dwelling Zones, indicating their regulatory status.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste-Related covers activities, services, and facilities that deal with waste management and disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste-related activities involve the collection, processing, or disposal of waste materials, and are subject to specific zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste-Related is a category focused on facilities or services related to waste management and processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 190851">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 190851</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 190851 is an ordinance that became effective on June 30, 2022. This regulation incorporates amendments to Title 33 and pertains specifically to planning and zoning regulations. It signifies a framework for regulatory changes that were put into effect as part of development regulations.

References to Ord. No. 190851 indicate that it is a legally recognized ordinance, notably mentioned in the context of significant regulatory updates. The consistency across multiple descriptions underscores its importance in the amendment process within the legal and administrative landscape. 

Overall, Ord. No. 190851 is a comprehensive regulatory measure that reflects its effective date of June 30, 2022, and highlights various aspects of its implementation and relevance to planning and zoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30084c591a498854d4f7f08382fe2aff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c4f9e9e16adccaf92b860a8f225b4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d3dc1f275b21f3a0c1622695839a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0352df0641b29208d29e9ef4be447b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23f6f27b8a490522d8ea471d51807cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fee202a5a178704f7fab97145229db5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Detention Facility">
      <data key="d0">Detention Facility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A detention facility is a secure location for detaining individuals, often related to law enforcement or correctional activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76b8dd9a163666dc41c6d8fd73436eb5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781016</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Type III Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Type III Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Type III Procedure refers to a comprehensive review process employed in various contexts related to land use and urban planning. This procedure applies to new helicopter landing facilities, significant modifications, and other development proposals, requiring a detailed evaluation against specific criteria. It is particularly relevant for reviewing changes to school site uses and conditions, as well as for mass shelters and short-term shelters that do not qualify for Type II approval, thereby indicating its importance in community and safety assessments.

The Type III Procedure serves as a formal mechanism for the review of applications pertaining to the Central City Master Plan and the Northwest Master Plan, including any amendments or significant alterations to these plans. This classification is utilized for substantial decisions requiring thorough scrutiny, such as land division proposals involving eleven or more lots or those with significant environmental implications. It mandates a public hearing, indicating its role in ensuring community involvement and transparency.

Additionally, the Type III Procedure is instrumental in reviewing conditional uses, major alterations to land, and historic feature reviews within urban areas. It requires higher standards of investigation for proposals that have the potential for high impacts. The process is also applied to proposals related to the Gateway master plan, along with comprehensive reviews for natural resource plans and resource classification determinations. 

In conclusion, the Type III Procedure stands as the highest classification of procedural review in land use planning, aiming to ensure that critical developments and modifications are assessed rigorously within the regulatory framework. The procedure is characterized by its comprehensive nature, public involvement, and focus on substantial discretion in decision-making, making it a critical tool for orderly urban development and resource management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69705150e078dd993ef14bd699a3bc12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c232ce107cc5a0bd00a23892d69d0561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2fc1b73b6e1ae4e82cbaf205ce719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ff07d99a0c758d3b51f7e05d950738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ec46b8cc5650199d033fa9573b44034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa5d2c57a95ae65f663a55f78fa3c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd02cf4545f01a8b1a3eabb4ce881c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86ce100d88532ab8ca2f1d785c9a636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e5352641a4a29255f045f1ffa49de30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614d099bcb8d71cfc787e0cbccc1ebbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b28b182d587540c8cdc8788f751c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96815c5a54ec29fd3986869ba3cf59e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a93319af7a8f643cc123f328935418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ca5fc3d28aa819abc484b86dc468ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49961939512caa6917f2206eb92e7d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73cef7ee88bf3469ada732d2e4209747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a43129b93ff8ead9df972bce81ecbb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644152b6276c54299003f76b5630241f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9157cebcd51ea7cec9c5bd83c0f3df47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23bdb6b78c43cbe3cee1a2bacbb57a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bde6fb397c7366841124f779d183b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa7a4d254279e02d605594ebe069be0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
