      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carpool Parking">
      <data key="d0">Carpool Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Carpool Parking refers to parking spaces reserved specifically for vehicles with multiple passengers to promote shared travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6510246c4ac7809275aed03aa6705c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781020</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Detached Accessory Structures">
      <data key="d0">Detached Accessory Structures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Detached Accessory Structures are secondary buildings that exist independently from the primary structure on a property. These structures are subject to various zoning regulations, which include specific requirements for minimum setback distances, height standards, and overall coverage. The regulations ensure that these buildings adhere to design compatibility with the primary structures and maintain site balance within residential areas.

Examples of Detached Accessory Structures encompass a variety of additional buildings such as garages, storage sheds, garden structures, play equipment, gazebos, and bike parking areas intended for communal use. The zoning standards provide detailed guidelines for their development, targeting aspects like maximum height and occupancy limits, to ensure that they do not interfere with the aesthetic or functional integrity of the residential zone.

Detached Accessory Structures are significant because they are not counted towards the maximum setback standards applicable to the main building. This allows property owners to enhance their usage of space while still respecting the regulatory framework intended for maintaining privacy and separation from residential zones. Overall, these structures serve practical purposes while reflecting the organized development of residential spaces in compliance with local zoning laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-199bdfd5f31802f14bb3bd7efff3a92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65928458722d6696f7fafa7beda4c38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2cc6a137a6b419b9a37152153b673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a966c4eaabe25aca0a1be25bd188299e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e17537bd24336b2dd65681e37f4d9aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59644a82d0120b0f13d2a9d402862b9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f772c2b474f898ac2fe23797d82b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb810e875d66f848b351a4f1271e2a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d4506f9183e501d03cc84da18500af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ab64be803cdc30ed89433c92047a024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5555f01efc47b9ad220ce985153f9292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bdd0a72bd1cfe3ef9d36a7ad4b1bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495bf4fb125321f6e8595e2bd9e90b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec6039135156cca92456b8fc09b0f8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
