    <node id="Parking, Loading, And Transportation And Parking Demand Management">
      <data key="d0">Parking, Loading, And Transportation And Parking Demand Management</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking, Loading, And Transportation And Parking Demand Management encompasses the regulations pertaining to parking spaces, loading areas, and transportation demand management measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking, Loading, And Transportation And Parking Demand Management refers to regulations and standards set for managing parking spaces and transportation needs in urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6510246c4ac7809275aed03aa6705c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781020</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="100 Percent of the Spaces">
      <data key="d0">100 Percent of the Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">100 Percent of the Spaces is a requirement indicating that all parking spaces must include necessary electrical conduits for electric vehicle chargers when specified conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6510246c4ac7809275aed03aa6705c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic Districts">
      <data key="d0">Historic Districts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic Districts are areas where the maximum Floor Area Ratio is limited to 3 to 1 for developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic districts are designated areas that contain multiple historic resources, subject to specific regulations to preserve their character.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Districts are defined areas consisting of historic landmarks that undergo strict regulations to maintain their historical integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Districts are areas that are protected for their historic or cultural significance and are relevant to the actions of the Design Commission and Historic Landmarks Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Districts are designated areas with special regulations aimed at preserving historical landmarks and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Districts are designated areas requiring specific approval criteria for historic resource review, including Historic Landmarks and Conservation Landmarks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b04cb33b3135ed3ccce916cd1c14a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c00423593f4ba14979614a9190e4c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81cd4184be21ff7c937e2bc32ad5b35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd455847ef176484b9b460a4062a8e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RMP Zone">
      <data key="d0">RMP Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RMP Zone, or Residential Mixed Use Zone, is a zoning designation that serves multiple purposes related to residential developments, particularly for manufactured dwelling parks. It is characterized by specific regulations that govern building setbacks, density, and the establishment of manufactured dwelling parks. The RMP Zone is designed as a low-scale multi-dwelling area allowing for increased density and affordable housing bonuses under particular conditions, thus supporting the development of diverse housing options.

This zoning classification does not require a Floor Area Ratio, making it distinct from other zoning categories. It encompasses regulations tailored to ensure lower building coverage and appropriate standards for outdoor shelters, which are permitted under certain conditions. Additionally, the RMP Zone includes criteria for vehicle areas and mandates specific standards for recreation area implementation in land divisions, contributing to the overall planning and functional use of the area.

Overall, the RMP Zone is integral to housing development, providing a framework that supports the establishment of manufactured dwelling parks while promoting effective land use and community standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-903ef5f8da50cf2a59819dcb0eda03b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc573198faf9c1b51eb551532d91476d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13fbd22ccb86e669dc7d330d54f31def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09653fd8cb264cda4f3441bd478fe017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc6ceed3be738324a1eb3f18282ffbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1267f51ecc30ce027ed225a2c473621</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conservation Districts">
      <data key="d0">Conservation Districts</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Conservation Districts have similar regulations as Historic Districts regarding the maximum Floor Area Ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Districts are specific areas designated for conservation efforts to preserve historical character and community aesthetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation districts are areas identified for the protection of significant resources and characteristics, often incorporating historical elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Districts are designated areas that are governed by specific design standards to preserve their character and significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Districts refer to designated areas that have specific regulations regarding the preservation and review of historic landmarks and resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Districts are designated areas with specific guidelines regarding development and alterations to historic resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Districts are areas designated for the conservation of historic resources and require special approval for modifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd455847ef176484b9b460a4062a8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1347219a19de2480f10b4ab0d1cc91d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92124b64bdb5812f3a81c72fd6334a86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dfa716b92fafe3e0c5a60967fdfe220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c5e50780fccc672722393ad08acacb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stormwater Management Manual">
      <data key="d0">Stormwater Management Manual</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Stormwater Management Manual is a comprehensive document that provides essential guidelines for managing stormwater in developed areas, particularly within urban environments. It emphasizes the importance of ensuring compliance with ecological practices and outlines water quality goals and standards that must be met in the management of stormwater.

The manual contains specific recommendations for effectively managing stormwater in various contexts, such as landscaped areas and parking lots. It details the requirements for stormwater management related to new developments, ensuring that future construction projects adhere to established best practices. Additionally, it includes guidelines for the management of stormwater facilities within development projects, promoting efficiency and environmental sustainability.

Particularly noteworthy is the focus on landscaping requirements and usage standards, which help integrate stormwater management into the overall design of urban spaces. The manual highlights the importance of sustainable practices in managing stormwater, underlining its role in enhancing water quality and environmental health within city settings. 

Moreover, the Stormwater Management Manual specifies that Planned Developments must comply with certain stormwater management practices, establishing a clear framework to guide developers in their projects. Together, these elements paint a detailed picture of the manual's objectives, serving as a vital resource for property owners, developers, and urban planners aimed at fostering effective stormwater management practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bcfb59e4095f5b02abc8ac31213ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a079f6fb5c8d245b04e7b9c62fbfa8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80cb4c4524db16a443cea9724f5fd6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59602cfae2cfed1834328c9ad24adf39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189a3579e304a7efcf0f543eaaad1a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9a5a4577f7544b4671be7b0e59a2ab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RM1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">RM1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RM1 Zone is a low-scale multi-dwelling zoning classification characterized by one to three story buildings primarily located near single-dwelling residential areas. This zoning designation includes specific regulations for density, permitting a minimum of one housing unit per 3,000 square feet on lots that are adjacent to shared courts or common greens. 

Within the RM1 Zone, density can be transferred from RMP zoned sites, allowing for increased housing density under certain conditions. There are unique building setback requirements and regulations governing residential construction within this zone, ensuring that development aligns with community standards. Additionally, the RM1 Zone allows for the establishment of cottage clusters, contingent upon meeting requirements related to lot sizes and street access. 

Specific outdoor area standards are mandated for residential properties in the RM1 Zone, whereby outdoor shelters are permitted as long as they comply with outlined standards and limitations. The classification also outlines regulations concerning vehicle areas and overall building layouts, emphasizing compatibility for medium density development. 

Moreover, the RM1 Zone includes provisions for manufactured dwelling parks, demonstrating a versatility in residential types allowed in this zoning category. Overall, the RM1 Zone influences the options available for residential development, balancing density provisions with community design and environmental considerations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c86bea48b8b39caf895ea538d23c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95b223ce551df4ebded5324da87138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc573198faf9c1b51eb551532d91476d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59644a82d0120b0f13d2a9d402862b9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b659477574fcf7f35453f172163de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d4506f9183e501d03cc84da18500af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13fbd22ccb86e669dc7d330d54f31def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc6ceed3be738324a1eb3f18282ffbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eebc2b12ebf015db39e2792d62d9565e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1267f51ecc30ce027ed225a2c473621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="National Register Districts">
      <data key="d0">National Register Districts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">National Register districts are recognized areas that include historic landmarks and are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic Landmarks">
      <data key="d0">Historic Landmarks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic landmarks are individual sites or structures formally designated for their historical significance and recognized on zoning maps.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Landmarks are recognized structures that are subject to special regulations regarding alterations and demolition to preserve their integrity and significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Landmarks are buildings or sites recognized for their historical significance, with stricter regulations compared to Conservation Landmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic landmarks refer to significant buildings or structures that are exempt from the landscaping standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Landmarks are sites protected under zoning regulations that qualify for special use considerations due to their historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Landmarks refer to sites of historical significance that affect the regulations regarding Office use in the zoning districts.&lt;SEP&gt;Historic Landmarks are important historical sites that are regulated for their conservation due to their cultural and historical value.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b56b9fdbb25d0d73793d586c98486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc3fc3ad91ea490a2f8ffb98e83e2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c00423593f4ba14979614a9190e4c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfa11b893b09fc1fb7d6655be073aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0147b437f8af7c9b75d571f1f8e2392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conservation Landmarks">
      <data key="d0">Conservation Landmarks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Conservation landmarks are structures that have additional regulations preventing modifications that could alter their historic or cultural significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation landmarks are historic resources identified specifically for preservation efforts and are subject to related regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Landmarks are significant resources within the community that have protections under the Community Design Standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Landmarks are sites recognized for their conservation value and similarly governed by particular zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conservation Landmarks refer to resources recognized for their historical significance, subject to specific preservation criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7c5b32a510f170e1363780c7ccaa64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c00423593f4ba14979614a9190e4c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfa11b893b09fc1fb7d6655be073aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="National Register Landmarks">
      <data key="d0">National Register Landmarks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">National Register landmarks are significant structures or sites listed on the National Register, highlighting their importance to history.&lt;SEP&gt;National Register Landmarks are historic properties recognized by the National Park Service for their significance in American history, architecture, archaeology, or culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a6a80015da77a2175c0409b020ea13e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Resources">
      <data key="d0">Significant Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant resources are historic assets that contribute to the cultural heritage of a region and may be designated as protected under zoning laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Map 475-2">
      <data key="d0">Map 475-2</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Map 475-2 shows the top of bank information critical for development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Map 475-2 is a reference document illustrating the top of bank and associated regulations within the River Environmental Overlay Zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Map 475-2 is referenced for requirements related to planting and environmental regulations between the top of the bank and the Ordinary High Water Mark.&lt;SEP&gt;Map 475-2 provides crucial information regarding the top of bank and the ordinary high water mark in regulatory contexts for the area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f92d42feaabfd545cc35264c76fbed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e28ba6f352cf461311b1a12b892a5ff</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781022</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan">
      <data key="d0">River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">plan</data>
      <data key="d2">The River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan outlines regulations for protecting scenic resources along river areas, referenced in standards for public viewing areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan provides guidelines for maintaining visual quality and scenic resources along the river.&lt;SEP&gt;The River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan provides additional guidelines for preserving scenic resources along riverfront areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The River Plan / South Reach Scenic Resources Protection Plan is designed to protect scenic resources along Portland's riverfront.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65b28885692c418064f133f06efd688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659ec42acd09493cb815e59e2193d7bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b0b9956e9369e20a5f76498419272b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781022</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RM3 Zone">
      <data key="d0">RM3 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RM3 Zone is a designated zoning classification that permits specific uses primarily focused on residential development. It supports medium to high-density multi-dwelling structures, allowing for compact developments near transit and commercial services, with stipulations that buildings can rise up to six stories. 

As a zoning classification, the RM3 Zone specifies development standards for multifamily residential structures, which include particular setback guidelines, outdoor area requirements, and building size regulations. It is important to note that density may be transferred from RMP zoned sites, enhancing the flexibility of development in this zone. Additionally, the RM3 Zone allows mixed-use developments under certain conditions, promoting a blend of residential and commercial activities.

In terms of site requirements, the RM3 Zone includes regulations for parking areas and permits outdoor shelters, provided that specific conditions in the planning regulations are met. Furthermore, height exceptions may be granted under particular circumstances, reflecting the adaptability of this zoning classification to various development scenarios. 

Overall, the RM3 Zone serves as an integral part of urban planning, encouraging efficient land use while maintaining consistency with local zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c86bea48b8b39caf895ea538d23c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0471cd3f359b7c1de83040290a16c652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13fbd22ccb86e669dc7d330d54f31def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1267f51ecc30ce027ed225a2c473621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b58865c473bfa9835169ceac4d038b1d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781022</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Title 11.60.020.C">
      <data key="d0">Title 11.60.020.C</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 11.60.020.C specifies canopy size standards for trees that are part of the planting requirements in the River Environmental Overlay Zone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781022</data>
