    <node id="Flag Lots">
      <data key="d0">Flag Lots</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Flag Lots are properties that have an irregular shape, often with limited access from the street, which have specific zoning exemptions.&lt;SEP&gt;Flag lots are specific types of land plots designed to encourage additional housing while retaining existing homes and ensuring privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Flag Lots are a type of residential lot that is exempt from the maximum setback standards in the zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Flag lots are a type of lot configuration often affected by specific zoning standards, especially concerning slope and access-related regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Flag lots refer to specific types of lots that have unique zoning exemptions and regulations outlined in the land use standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Flag lots are a special type of lot configuration used in specific circumstances to minimize impacts and provide access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb1ab98a275a3e96b292afb310b8237d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e17537bd24336b2dd65681e37f4d9aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9ce8abdb14d484f7e951e27e2fec56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d66ea593dc4ac52ad4236580e597c48b</data>
