    <node id="EG1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">EG1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The EG1 Zone is a specific zoning designation within employment zones that has several defined regulations and restrictions aimed at controlling the development and character of buildings in this area. It imposes particular setback standards and outlines regulations for permitted activities and structures, ensuring that the overall character remains consistent with its primary purpose as an employment district.

This zone includes restrictions on development and exterior displays, aiming to maintain a professional environment. Furthermore, it specifies standards for lot dimensions, requiring compliance with defined criteria for land divisions. The EG1 Zone also addresses parking and vehicle area layouts, ensuring that these aspects align with the zoning goals.

Residential uses are generally prohibited within the EG1 Zone, although the conversion of existing hotels or motels to mass shelters is permitted in conjunction with short-term shelter conversions. Additionally, the zone controls nonconforming Household Living uses, placing regulations on how such uses can operate, thus maintaining the integrity of the employment setting.

Overall, the EG1 Zone serves as a controlled environment that promotes live/work developments while imposing restrictions on certain uses to preserve the area’s focus on employment and related activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2f99e9a7745139a1b31e101848816d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e6483ee1a0cf1415621eb7ccf6224b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b06e985a4445f1b158ef2343cff5b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422a1c7b762d9ab38fe2197b504ec353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781025</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RM4 Zone">
      <data key="d0">RM4 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The RM4 Zone is a designated high-density residential zoning classification that allows for multi-dwelling units typically comprising seven or more stories. It is primarily located close to pedestrian-friendly environments within urban areas, making it suitable for residential development. As per local zoning regulations, the RM4 Zone permits specific uses while also imposing certain restrictions outlined in various facets of planning and architectural design.

One of the key characteristics of the RM4 Zone is its maximum Floor Area Ratio (FAR) of 4 to 1, which indicates the possible building size in relation to the land area. However, this ratio is applicable except in designated Historic and Conservation Districts, where additional regulations may be in place to maintain the area's character. The RM4 Zone allows density transfer from RMP zoned sites, facilitating more efficient use of space.

The zoning classification also encompasses particular requirements for building setbacks and outdoor area standards. These standards dictate how far structures must be set back from property lines and regulate the outdoor space allocated for each unit, ensuring that developments maintain certain aesthetic and functional qualities. Furthermore, the RM4 Zone includes regulations concerning accessory parking and paving materials for development, contributing to the overall planning framework.

In addition to residential units, the RM4 Zone accommodates limited commercial uses, ensuring that the predominant character remains residential while also allowing a degree of mixed use. The zoning allows for outdoor shelters, provided they comply with defined regulatory standards, further enhancing the functionality of the spaces developed within this classification. 

Moreover, the RM4 Zone provides flexibility in construction by permitting height exceptions if the specified criteria are met, promoting creative architectural solutions that align with the zone's intent of high-density living while respecting the surrounding urban fabric. Overall, the RM4 Zone serves as a critical component of urban planning, aiming to balance density, residential character, and community needs within designated areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c86bea48b8b39caf895ea538d23c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0471cd3f359b7c1de83040290a16c652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13fbd22ccb86e669dc7d330d54f31def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b34f0df60116c5736f2d7981efaa2b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1267f51ecc30ce027ed225a2c473621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b58865c473bfa9835169ceac4d038b1d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781025</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CM1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">CM1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The CM1 Zone is a specific zoning classification that regulates the development and use of land within designated areas, primarily focusing on commercial and retail activities. It imposes particular limitations on the floor area ratio (FAR) and specifies that individual buildings typically cannot exceed 5,000 square feet. These regulations are tailored for industrial uses and retail operations, ensuring that developments remain proportionate to their site characteristics.

In addition to size restrictions, the CM1 Zone allows for external displays of goods, provided these comply with established restrictions. Vehicle area placement and usage standards are also integral to this zoning classification, ensuring orderly and efficient use of space. Furthermore, CM1 designates areas where drive-through facilities are permissible, aligned with regulations outlined in Title 33. 

The CM1 Zone also incorporates standards intended to encourage mixed-use development, with a focus on small-scale commercial activities, particularly in regions like the Lombard Street Plan District. This zoning classification creates opportunities for specific commercial uses while promoting compatibility with residential developments through density requirements. 

Notably, developments within the CM1 Zone must consider safety and livability standards when integrating facilities such as helicopter landing sites. Overall, the CM1 Zone facilitates a less intense commercial and mixed-use environment adjacent to the CM2 zone, promoting diverse economic activities while maintaining community standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95b223ce551df4ebded5324da87138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e889d237f01a5093e629880a38d5a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1c1bab5c230ae2f2d1c810ec319973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aafe5a7a2907664ceccb93037cc2fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d9e8d9a2a7e63e60180b8dfe9e9acda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da7d185f05e10a8fa434d3d4713ae5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2046790125dcdbb2805d0592a8edd3</data>
