    <node id="Accessory Dwelling Units">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Dwelling Units</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessory dwelling units are secondary housing units located on the same lot as a primary structure, subject to specific planning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Units are separate living spaces established on a residential property, often providing additional housing options.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Units are residential structures exempt from specific standards in Title 33 regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Units are additional housing units that can be established on properties under certain conditions to increase housing availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory dwelling units are secondary housing units included in minimum density calculations but excluded from maximum density calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Units are secondary housing units on a property; their creation is prohibited on lots divided through a Middle Housing Land Division.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory dwelling units are alternative housing options not covered by the specified standards relating to vegetated or landscaped roof areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65928458722d6696f7fafa7beda4c38d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c98d267897f87dec14edb30985e788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd63fde7af35a2611f3f81cc2e72e533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc3fc3ad91ea490a2f8ffb98e83e2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825dcc9caa885b9e5aef8f2ccbaf183d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe92a3f46b3bfc4baa1f040d200709a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
