    <node id="CM3 Zone">
      <data key="d0">CM3 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The CM3 Zone is a designated zoning classification that encompasses a variety of specific regulations concerning land use, building standards, and development practices. This classification is primarily aimed at promoting urban development while ensuring compatibility of various land uses, including residential, commercial, and industrial spaces, as well as maintaining livability in the area. 

The CM3 Zone permits higher building heights and specifies floor area ratio (FAR) limits. It enforces that the total net building area used for industrial purposes does not exceed the total square footage of the site. Furthermore, it allows for mixed-use developments but limits residential uses to 20 percent of the net building area. There are also regulations in place regarding the elimination of detached houses, ensuring that the zoning supports active ground floor uses outside of the Central City Plan District.

In addition to the height and area regulations, the CM3 Zone imposes restrictions concerning vehicle areas, paving materials, and accessory parking. The external display of goods is permitted under specific conditions, while landscaping and building standards are heavily regulated to maintain the area's character and functionality. 

Furthermore, the CM3 Zone includes provisions for bonus building height and floor area for development projects that meet certain criteria. It also addresses helicopter landing facilities to prevent significant disruptions to local livability. This classification is applicable within the St. Johns Plan District and is referenced in the approval criteria for Planned Developments, making it an integral part of the urban planning framework in the region.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1f1b130f7e5afceced958bf6e3d52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2f99e9a7745139a1b31e101848816d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0471cd3f359b7c1de83040290a16c652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7aa0bae5c7fef30a568af91c0f05e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab78bf22476f90e50de5d511279727d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1ec40ef0c834d42a666a80a8223118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aafe5a7a2907664ceccb93037cc2fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe97b08b11271bbcb78b5346a0c5bad8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b34f0df60116c5736f2d7981efaa2b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2c7926ceca17c4d0d7614d1c8acec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc22ba039a9fe91f1dbd58c1c542c993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad</data>
