    <node id="Port of Portland">
      <data key="d0">Port of Portland</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Port of Portland is a governmental body that plays a crucial role in the development, management, and regulation of transportation infrastructure in the Portland area, including overseeing the Portland International Airport. In its capacity, the Port of Portland requires commercial seaplane facilities to obtain approval prior to the issuance of building permits, ensuring that all construction projects align with regulatory standards.

The Port is actively involved in managing the noise impacts associated with air traffic, particularly within the PDX Noise Zone. As part of its responsibilities, the Port of Portland regulates noise easements and oversees sound insulation certification costs while offering consultation services related to acoustical engineering to mitigate the effects of aircraft noise on surrounding communities.

Moreover, the Port of Portland manages airport properties and plans for their development, which may include requesting Transportation Impact Analysis reviews related to airport growth initiatives. The organization is also dedicated to ensuring safety and environmental compliance through its Wildlife Hazard Management Plan, which addresses concerns regarding wildlife species that may pose risks to aviation operations. 

Overall, the Port of Portland serves as a vital entity in promoting safe, efficient transportation while balancing the needs of commercial development and environmental stewardship in the region.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1632ab80e73b4a2c163fe42dad2e6477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6e3473a810a12fa40e385deedea49f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f305efce488af07ac0258b91ef1d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed32ffcf90280c2cd045c39203b18c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1fd4b1eeb5d6c8b3aa79843d378284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b80bff0fbd16752d5db014bfe9946815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f1dbc710e403c474cc362ea8160571&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2001ba277158737c9b888248e680d7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2215c0dede8ee98027b1212757bd97af</data>
