    <node id="Transportation Element">
      <data key="d0">Transportation Element</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Transportation Element is a crucial part of the Portland Comprehensive Plan, focusing on the development, management, and regulation of transportation systems and infrastructure. It outlines guidelines, designations, and standards that dictate how transportation systems are planned and operated within the city.

This element encompasses several key areas, including street designations, which specify how various streets are classified and utilized within the transportation network. It also provides guidelines for street design, influencing the layout and functionality of roadways to enhance traffic operations and improve safety for all users.

Furthermore, the Transportation Element details the capabilities and requirements of transportation systems in relation to anticipated land uses, ensuring that transportation infrastructure is aligned with urban development goals. By including various standards and specifications relevant to transport planning, this element plays an essential role in shaping the overall transportation framework of Portland, aiding in both current and future mobility needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbc54ab4dbbc617d4c752a69733a5f32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd02cf4545f01a8b1a3eabb4ce881c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed8af90c52cb663785082c6731625b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e7feaddec557941c697fec7b2e2763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632a46b796dd8e7e5beca816ac0c1138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d28f6febcf4de65239d0203f2197382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44cf0420ca13ed6c3eed49130f77fb31</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
