    <node id="EG2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">EG2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The EG2 Zone is a designated area with specific regulatory frameworks governing various uses, primarily related to Household Living and Group Living under Title 33. It serves as an employment zone that facilitates the exterior display of goods, setting it apart from the EG1 Zone. This zone is classified within a broader category of employment zones, emphasizing particular development regulations that must be adhered to by stakeholders.

In addition to its employment-related designations, the EG2 Zone maintains building characteristics similar to the EG1 Zone while also accommodating certain nonconforming Household Living uses. Furthermore, the zoning regulations within the EG2 Zone impose limitations on vehicle area usage and prohibit residential development. However, it allows for the conversion of hotels or motels into mass shelters, contingent on adherence to specific conditions.

The EG2 Zone's classification indicates that certain regulatory standards are imposed, which include specifications on land divisions especially relevant for lots numbering ten or more—thus establishing requirements around lot sizes. Notably, this zoning classification does not enforce setbacks or height limits except when adjacent to residentially zoned sites. Additionally, it operates under regulations that may not conform to certain environmental standards, aligning with its broader zoning goals.

The EG2 Zone is operational within the Columbia South Shore Plan District, where it imposes distinct limitations on the uses permissible for retail and office spaces. Overall, the EG2 Zone's regulations impact the development and lot standards for properties within its jurisdiction, ensuring that land use aligns with designated planning objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9bca75f94d2f6ca963676dd23e65338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-221d1ae9cf50b3236ae14ae949934120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebeee1e9a6fdc5e2eb02bb6563ce14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e6483ee1a0cf1415621eb7ccf6224b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-441c51a51f44fd3d962a1948c121fd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4cc500f0cf6ffd63a8f594c9055457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422a1c7b762d9ab38fe2197b504ec353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
