    <node id="Easement">
      <data key="d0">Easement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An easement is a legal right to use another's land for a specific purpose, such as granting access for a public trail.&lt;SEP&gt;An easement is a legal agreement that allows an individual or entity to use land owned by another party for specific purposes, particularly in relation to plantings.&lt;SEP&gt;An easement is a legal right allowing the applicant access to remove piles or dolphins from property not owned by them.&lt;SEP&gt;An easement is a legal right for unrestricted public access to the open space during daylight hours, which the property owner must record.&lt;SEP&gt;An easement is a legal right to use someone else's land for a specified purpose, which may include temporary turnarounds and public access pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;An Easement is a legal right to use another's land for a specified purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;An Easement is a property owner's grant allowing others access for specific purposes, such as utility placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65b28885692c418064f133f06efd688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4749d2209607255edbe985025b727249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22acd36bdbe56e46354926a0904b7463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8fd3cd43b3e7770531d9235f454d5b9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781026</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biotechnical Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Biotechnical Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Biotechnical techniques involve using natural materials and processes for soil stabilization and habitat restoration in environmental management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
