    <node id="Outdoor Area">
      <data key="d0">Outdoor Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An outdoor area is designated for individual units, requiring specific dimensions and accessibility for residential use.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor areas are designated spaces intended for outdoor relaxation or recreation, with specific area requirements based on the zone.&lt;SEP&gt;An outdoor area is a designated space required for each dwelling unit, which must meet certain standards for surface materials and amenities.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor Area refers to the space required for recreation, relaxation, or food growth, ensuring accessibility for residents.&lt;SEP&gt;An outdoor area that includes individual units, common spaces, and publicly accessible areas, which must meet specific requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05299df3decd7e8061aff48bb1ba2029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b2cc8f6a45d17941e977fde3debc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab8e6f4ae4a675657fc86e7ca06a385</data>
