    <node id="Portland International Airport">
      <data key="d0">Portland International Airport</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Portland International Airport is the primary airport serving the City of Portland, Oregon. It plays a crucial role in regional transportation and is subject to various specific regulations that govern its operations, land use, and environmental impacts. The airport is notable for its designated Aircraft Landing Zone, which is established to enhance safety measures for aircraft operations.

The airport is at the center of various zoning regulations that affect land use in its surrounding vicinity. It is also associated with noise impact regulations, which include the management of noise contours to mitigate the effects of aircraft noise on residential areas. Additionally, the Noise Impact Overlay Zone is relevant to residential density regulations in the region surrounding the airport.

Portland International Airport is a significant regional transport facility and is referenced in connection with the Cascade Station/Portland International Center plan district, illustrating its importance in urban planning and development. The airport operates within specific plan district and subdistrict regulations that influence its development, including public notifications about changes or improvements.

Environmental management is another critical focus for Portland International Airport, which implements a Wildlife Hazard Management Plan as part of its environmental overlay zones. The airport's growth initiatives are assessed through the Airport Transportation Impact Analysis Review, which addresses transport needs and potential expansions.

Furthermore, Portland International Airport features landside development such as passenger terminals and maintenance facilities, aimed at supporting passengers, employees, and visitors. Proposed parking enhancements are also being considered to facilitate access to the airport and improve overall user experience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1632ab80e73b4a2c163fe42dad2e6477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda537024724fbc12582034b555f1424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4754016f12749d254a4dac403332ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1fd4b1eeb5d6c8b3aa79843d378284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d39e794ab5c802105ac492ea170724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2dff9267506b3019f40d39ac0b51e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24f1dbc710e403c474cc362ea8160571&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c858bb23efe67cb70612c0464f3e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3994dbc2c6f464ef189000d5ce6654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eec69c467b67bcbd30527c47bb489f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44cf0420ca13ed6c3eed49130f77fb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a652fe26732ad48c0b07b16d7b74511</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781027</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IG2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">IG2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The IG2 Zone is a specific zoning classification that plays a significant role in regulating land use and development within particular areas. It is characterized by restrictions on retail sales and service or office uses, focusing on their quantity and square footage. This zoning designation is part of the Columbia South Shore Plan District, where it allows certain retail uses to operate without needing conditional reviews. 

Moreover, the IG2 Zone has distinct building coverage standards that apply to development. These standards are not applicable to certain disturbances, indicating that some development activities may proceed with fewer limitations. The IG2 Zone also contains specific regulations governing proposed developments, including public notifications, which are essential for ensuring community involvement in the planning process.

In terms of land division, the IG2 Zone imposes standard requirements based on the number of lots, and it necessitates that sites be a minimum of 340,000 square feet to qualify under the regulations of Chapter 33.664. This indicates a focus on larger-scale developments within this zone. Furthermore, the IG2 Zone is categorized as an industrial zone, which can be subject to particular approval regulations related to land divisions, ensuring that developments align with the overarching planning goals and standards of the area.

Overall, the IG2 Zone combines various zoning functions that facilitate organized development, maintain regulatory controls, and provide for certain commercial activities, all while balancing community standards and land use optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1632ab80e73b4a2c163fe42dad2e6477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdb0ed86328221b3f3b4bc1f84ed339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebeee1e9a6fdc5e2eb02bb6563ce14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e460c58e359f4aa61eae2678eeb2a806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-441c51a51f44fd3d962a1948c121fd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4cc500f0cf6ffd63a8f594c9055457</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781028</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Permits">
      <data key="d0">Permits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Permits are official approvals or licenses required to carry out certain activities or developments under local regulations, including construction and land use changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a98088aa848c3a646425801c36c9f6b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781028</data>
