    <node id="Federal Aviation Administration">
      <data key="d0">Federal Aviation Administration</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) regulates landing area proposals and ensures safety compliance for helicopter landing facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration is a national agency responsible for regulating civil aviation and ensuring safe airspace operations, including regulations regarding tower illumination.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration is the governing body that oversees airspace regulations and is involved in the review process for developments affecting the Aircraft Landing Overlay Zone.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration is a regulatory body that reviews development proposals in the Cascade Station/Portland International Center to protect airport operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) oversees the development proposals to ensure safety and regulatory compliance for airport operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Aviation Administration governs the policies related to wildlife hazards near airports.</data>
