    <node id="Overlay Zones">
      <data key="d0">Overlay Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Overlay Zones are specialized zoning classifications that provide additional criteria or restrictions to the underlying base zones for environmental conservation or design.&lt;SEP&gt;Overlay zones are regulatory layers that apply additional restrictions or guidelines relevant to specific subjects in various city areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Overlay Zones are zoning classifications that impose specific regulations or guidelines on top of existing zoning designations.&lt;SEP&gt;Overlay Zones refer to specific areas defined under the Zoning Code that impose additional regulations on land use.&lt;SEP&gt;Overlay Zones are additional zoning regulations that apply over existing base zones, often for specific land use purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eda537024724fbc12582034b555f1424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f06b0977a1322293e0781ce406d337f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95bbc1bcc87570cccffede2c40cb383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec40727e0d8bf940e01c40131ec7d220</data>
