    <node id="Detention Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Detention Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Detention Facilities are defined as secured locations specifically designed for holding individuals, often in relation to legal matters such as judicial detainment or incarceration. These facilities are characterized by their use within the framework of governmental regulations and legal supervision, operated under the oversight of peace officers. 

In the context of zoning laws, Detention Facilities are identified as prohibited uses within Single-Dwelling Zones, indicating that their establishment is restricted in certain residential areas. Despite this prohibition, they are recognized within broader zone guidelines that allow for conditional use under specified regulations. This regulatory framework outlines the criteria that must be met for a Detention Facility to be established, which may include considerations for facility size and parking requirements.

The infrastructure of Detention Facilities is designed to accommodate unique needs, including requirements for specialized parking arrangements that are often conditional based on the net building area. These considerations reflect the nature of the facilities as correctional institutions, which serve the purpose of detaining individuals under judicial authority while ensuring compliance with legal and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb0a8fdf55836bf22ae8a840cfbe18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b2323b48f41f87137658c4c38c98ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cc02978e3319b39c1038d83f233d71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34de9e34b3c0011d322a8520a1091e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e255ad4213c8ff69b61a260e064f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930256b3bb4008d11b0886f29973ea67</data>
