    <node id="Historic Resources">
      <data key="d0">Historic Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic Resources are buildings, sites, structures, and features of historical significance that are protected under various regulations and standards. These resources are subject to specific regulations during demolition and are often recognized for their importance in conservation efforts. They may include landmarks, conservation landmarks, and historic districts, all of which require adherence to preservation standards, particularly when modifications or developments are proposed.

In many cases, Historic Resources are recognized under planning and zoning laws, which help ensure their protection. They may be open to the public under certain conditions, contributing to cultural and historical preservation in the community. The significance of these resources often prompts regulatory measures to maintain their integrity and safeguard them against detrimental changes.

Overall, Historic Resources play a crucial role in preserving the cultural heritage and history of communities, thereby necessitating special recognition and protection to ensure their survival for future generations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495efc01559ae21a68e9da3b57998769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4271bb9cc0287dcb0b401b760eb4864e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157f892dc3db1b7d5113b58ec80ccd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11fb000daddf2f11413b9c98892fc17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49385b6cdb2ddda6bb336746708e24c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2df84aea0e28175d739f9e39d7ac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5348591467a41c77d858f5dbd717c172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f349daac2faae66ee44d1e97329f22b</data>
