    <node id="Chapter 33.920">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.920</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.920 is a specific chapter within Title 33 that addresses various use categories and regulations pertinent to planning and zoning. This chapter plays a crucial role in delineating the appropriate use categories for different zones, including Single-Dwelling Zones and Campus Institutional Zones. 

Within the context of these zones, Chapter 33.920 describes the regulations and criteria that govern land use and development. It provides comprehensive guidelines for nonconforming situations, which assist in determining legal uses of property that may not conform to current zoning laws. Additionally, the chapter includes detailed descriptions of use categories relevant to the Commercial/Mixed Use Zone, outlining specific regulations for various types of storage and service operations.

Overall, Chapter 33.920 serves as an important regulatory framework aimed at ensuring orderly land use and development across multiple zones, while addressing both conforming and nonconforming use scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb0a8fdf55836bf22ae8a840cfbe18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f6c68627201b6a0d63e0a73012b8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76f0e466ee927633a830eb76da6e9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1548cc5d56ac0b8d2ab93d83d89c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7777fdca5bcbd3670723d206cd8f5757</data>
