    <node id="Environmental Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Environmental Overlay Zone is a designated area that includes various regulations and restrictions aimed at protecting natural resources and managing the impacts of development activities. These zones are established for conservation purposes and impose special criteria that influence land use, particularly regarding setbacks for buildings and entrances, which must adhere to environmental considerations.

The Environmental Overlay Zone serves to preserve critical environmental features, such as streams and wetlands, and establishes specific review requirements for development projects. Within these zones, special protections are mandated to mitigate environmental impacts and ensure compliance with regulations designed to safeguard natural habitats and resources.

Furthermore, the Environmental Overlay Zone outlines areas that require heightened scrutiny regarding environmental codes, meaning that any violations must be addressed with particular care to conform to the established environmental standards. Overall, these zones reflect a commitment to responsible land management practices, emphasizing the importance of integrating environmental protection within urban planning and development strategies.</data>
