    <node id="Central City Scenic Resources Protection Plan">
      <data key="d0">Central City Scenic Resources Protection Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Central City Scenic Resources Protection Plan is a comprehensive framework established to safeguard scenic resources in urban areas, specifically within Central City. Originally created in 2018, this plan designates essential view corridors and includes regulations relevant to wind turbine placements to preserve the visual integrity of the environment.

This plan encompasses a variety of standards and guidelines aiming to protect scenic vistas, maintain public viewing areas, and uphold the overall aesthetic of the urban landscape. It delineates specific height restrictions on buildings and detailed regulations pertaining to view corridors, ensuring that new developments do not obstruct significant scenic views. The guidelines serve as a mechanism to carefully manage urban landscaping in a way that enhances and protects the scenic value of the area.

Moreover, previous references exist indicating that the plan was established as early as 2017, highlighting its evolving nature and the ongoing efforts to address issues of urban scenery in the context of development pressures. The Central City Scenic Resources Protection Plan thus plays a vital role in balancing urban growth with the preservation of visual and environmental resources, creating a sustainable and aesthetically pleasing urban environment for residents and visitors alike.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65b28885692c418064f133f06efd688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9b97086444d872e3bea48cd8e3ed5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-221d1ae9cf50b3236ae14ae949934120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40d1cf5d1a59a47e32100e78eb27cf84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-659ec42acd09493cb815e59e2193d7bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b0b9956e9369e20a5f76498419272b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fbbf35a5a5146ae4034375e7576374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad866e29e441289a8f35f6617f6b3691</data>
