    <node id="Chapter 33.910">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.910</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.910 is a crucial component of the Title 33 Planning and Zoning regulations, serving primarily to provide definitions for various terms related to nonconforming situations and land use. This chapter encompasses a comprehensive array of definitions that are integral to understanding the regulations concerning planning and zoning.

In particular, Chapter 33.910 focuses on nonconforming situations, outlining specific definitions that clarify the meanings of terms utilized in the zoning code. Among these definitions, the chapter addresses regulations pertaining to short-term shelters, mass shelters, and outdoor shelters, ensuring that these terms are well-understood within the context of local governance and zoning laws.

Furthermore, Chapter 33.910 elaborates on definitions relevant to historic resources, detailing the specific characteristics and classifications of various types of resources mentioned in planning and zoning regulations. This is significant for ensuring that historical designations are appropriately considered in land use planning.

The chapter also provides definitions related to different lot types and their characteristics, contributing to a more nuanced understanding of land use planning. Overall, Chapter 33.910 plays an essential role in clarifying the terminologies and regulations that inform land use decisions within the framework of planning and zoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6bbc03052089bd83b779b573dbdac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9400bf4e5a50bd8a9d73707eb530e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2b2cd34a3e56fc1d7de2b3a42826d7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
