    <node id="River Environmental Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">River Environmental Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The River Environmental Overlay Zone is a designated area with comprehensive regulations aimed at preserving the environmental integrity of river ecosystems and adjacent lands. This zoning classification is crucial for regulating land use and development, especially in areas directly adjacent to waterways, ensuring that such activities align with ecological preservation efforts.

The River Environmental Overlay Zone imposes specific standards and limitations on construction and disturbances to minimize impacts on natural resources. These regulations are particularly focused on hazardous substances, managing their removal or remediation to prevent contamination of river environments. Furthermore, the zone allows for certain developments while simultaneously emphasizing the importance of enhancing and protecting the natural resource functions of riverine ecosystems.

One of the key objectives of the River Environmental Overlay Zone is to guide development practices that respect ecological balances. Regulations cover various aspects, including the placement and management of dredged materials, the removal of structures like dolphins, and the preservation of tree resources near rivers. The zone also requires developers to adhere to ecological criteria when planning projects to ensure that downstream effects on wildlife and natural habitats are mitigated.

Additionally, the River Environmental Overlay Zone plays a pivotal role in safeguarding the scenic and natural resources of river environments, combining environmental protection objectives with regulated development practices. Through its established guidelines, the zone aims to foster sensitive development that aligns with environmental goals, thereby ensuring the long-term health and sustainability of river ecosystems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0008239cd0cc57b5042bb7a02ab19c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a7652f0b0b380d8dc6c5c8262a6ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65b28885692c418064f133f06efd688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c3e12ec08ee12d0c625c3b66e539b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b715d8f3b52a84d0efa1e1daabf8956b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40d1cf5d1a59a47e32100e78eb27cf84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfece86ae05751fbebb6324df767074f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2f9d38007eada5085a52ba7956a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacf586128716bb40a914b64e071f666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a5816615430d9b588c4adaf4aa3131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ef9b400f3f8eaf84f03bdff42a7221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e28ba6f352cf461311b1a12b892a5ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7623c76eb73dcf7a97d644a7c57616d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c81af569271dc0e96af33c5eb99f9dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc5679c2a480cf928223a40dfabf825d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8304e315438268768f83d85e05fcf463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2653802c982b64f8a7af01800f4406b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5045146aa70a167fd48292faecd8ea6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644152b6276c54299003f76b5630241f</data>
