    <node id="Bicycle Parking">
      <data key="d0">Bicycle Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bicycle Parking refers to areas specifically designed for the secure parking and storage of bicycles. These designated areas play a crucial role in promoting cycling by providing both short-term and long-term parking options. Bicycle Parking facilities can be located in hard-surfaced zones, typically situated between buildings and street lot lines, ensuring they are accessible and integrated into pedestrian circulation systems.

Bicycle Parking is not merely a suggestion but a regulatory requirement aimed at encouraging the use of bicycles. Regulations dictate the proper placement of bike parking facilities to comply with planning applications and to facilitate ease of access for cyclists. Additionally, Bicycle Parking is relevant to specific regions, such as within the Marquam Hill Plan District, where certain requirements must be met according to established regulations.

Overall, Bicycle Parking encompasses various designated spaces and facilities for bicycles, emphasizing the importance of secure parking options to promote cycling as a viable and sustainable mode of transportation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a32afcc972f576bfde371e6d61bdfb76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9c74456e021e6800b45f3d57ae1aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e75a7e001ab5c6a45155cc2595b9e77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4328dc69e2d2b9998d2666c8193b0245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2474dfd41e2575d0e3e9c1417c737dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5981b497cbbe74619a5ea1cae750089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8a638cacad1df6f7e7b142a2867c220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e317f6dbe5f15015c8e4149009a9021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ab6bd54c89f86d004823d37a33255e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bcd05068dc776f6a4ff3953570df7a</data>
