    <node id="Setback">
      <data key="d0">Setback</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Setback refers to the required distance from property lines for building structures, ensuring compliance with zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Setback is a zoning requirement that dictates the minimum distance a building must be from the property line or street lot line.&lt;SEP&gt;Setback is a regulatory requirement specifying the minimum distance a building must be from a street lot line.&lt;SEP&gt;Setback refers to the minimum distance required between a specified object, such as a building, and another point, typically measured from lot lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eded02aea3f115ba99e1a14dd25ad585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8491ef6a94a83bd06029a3a52c0a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad3df252c10f7d3d9869375a3dd70b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781036</data>
