    </node>
    <node id="Eastern Pattern Area">
      <data key="d0">Eastern Pattern Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Eastern Pattern Area refers to a geographic area with specific building setback requirements outlined in planning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eastern Pattern Area is a designated zone with specific building setback requirements and exemptions for certain properties within an area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eastern Pattern Area is a designated zone in zoning regulations with specific building and setback requirements for structures located within it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eastern Pattern Area is a specific zone with additional development restrictions concerning landscaping and building setbacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Eastern Pattern Area is a defined zone with specific regulations regarding landscaping and building setbacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Eastern Pattern Area is a section outlined in zoning regulations pertaining to site usage and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eded02aea3f115ba99e1a14dd25ad585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c86bea48b8b39caf895ea538d23c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e596f70f1bcab1802ff190bf7807a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8dedd6570aca440bb011dbffebca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0081003d43e7b772e5a8d3dfae39548</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inner Pattern Area">
      <data key="d0">Inner Pattern Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inner Pattern Area is a zoning designation influencing setback requirements specifically in residential zones adjacent to civic corridors.&lt;SEP&gt;Inner Pattern Area refers to a designated space within a site that adheres to specific zoning guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eded02aea3f115ba99e1a14dd25ad585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8dedd6570aca440bb011dbffebca8f0</data>
