    <node id="Civic or Neighborhood Corridor">
      <data key="d0">Civic or Neighborhood Corridor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Civic or Neighborhood Corridor is a designated street or pathway serving as a vital link in a community, often influencing local zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Civic or Neighborhood Corridors are designated pathways or streets that influence zoning regulations for adjacent properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Civic or Neighborhood Corridor refers to streets designated for public accessibility and community engagement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eded02aea3f115ba99e1a14dd25ad585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207bdd149614a77764e1c1161b9089e5</data>
