    <node id="Planned Development">
      <data key="d0">Planned Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Planned Development is a regulatory framework within urban planning that allows for specific building standards tailored to residential and institutional uses. This concept encompasses a variety of aspects related to land development and zoning regulations, facilitating flexibility in the construction and modification of projects in designated zones. It enables increased building heights and floor area ratios (FAR) under certain conditions, which is particularly significant for accommodating diverse growth needs within urban areas.

The Planned Development process is guided by Title 33, which outlines the rules governing development procedures. This includes the scheduled implementation of developments that must conform to established zoning and planning regulations. It emphasizes the importance of factors such as accessibility and energy efficiency in housing developments, ensuring that these projects meet modern environmental and social standards.

Additionally, Planned Development involves a comprehensive planning process for the design of specific areas, facilitating the reorganization of land use and zoning processes. This allows for the integration of various housing types and the adjustment of density regulations, fostering mixed-use zones that contribute to urban vitality. The framework also mandates the construction of public amenities, such as major public trails, as integral components of development projects.

Furthermore, Planned Development serves as a zoning approval mechanism that provides a structured approach to land use. It focuses on specified land utilization criteria and infrastructure requirements. The overarching goal of this approach is to implement a comprehensive review and establish approval criteria that cater to various zoning projects, thereby enhancing coordinated and sustainable urban growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1dfee1abb6388294ddd10d180ea3f102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c8009e101b1c5acef3b9262a76129e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a962491a7cd2c102b96a01ffc8d4cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4749d2209607255edbe985025b727249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63c21c957d68787ba4fea52897f3a3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ffc992b5e373540a3ee78f16308e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13c24553d0786fad8dd03e98ef27205d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80424e1fdfc525e03fb931cf5e6d14ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67111441a3c9d2875734e7bedb42d3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68e1edc738fe00a1738dc12a945ce96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Affordable Commercial Space Fund">
      <data key="d0">Affordable Commercial Space Fund</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Affordable Commercial Space Fund is designed to provide financial support for the incorporation of affordable commercial space in developments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Affordable Commercial Space Fund is a financial resource that may allow for increased maximum height and floor area ratio in development projects under specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86af9727766ff2222007c054fe1ec5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c8009e101b1c5acef3b9262a76129e</data>
