    <node id="Nonconforming Situations">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Situations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming situations relate to properties that differ from current zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Situations refer to instances where existing uses, density, or development may not comply with current zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Situations refers to zoning cases where a land use does not conform to current zoning regulations but may continue to operate under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Situations involve developments that do not conform to current zoning regulations but are allowed under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Situations refers to exterior display and storage areas that do not comply with zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ab6bd54c89f86d004823d37a33255e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e13bc554ddbf7ad8cfa41b1e6d467181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
