    <node id="Nonconforming Lots">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Lots</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming Lots include lots that do not meet current zoning requirements but were legally established under previous regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming lots refer to parcels of land that do not conform to current zoning regulations but may continue to exist under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nonconforming Development">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming development refers to existing buildings or structures that do not comply with current zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Development refers to properties that do not comply with current zoning laws but were legally established before their adoption.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Development relates to existing structures or uses that do not comply with current zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Development refers to existing developments that do not meet current zoning regulations, which may have legal status if maintained.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming development refers to elements that were previously compliant with regulations but became non-compliant due to zoning changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Development refers to developments that once conformed to regulations but no longer do due to zoning changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ffecc9f384562fe6c27c733b40f0f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495efc01559ae21a68e9da3b57998769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Trees">
      <data key="d0">Trees</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Trees refer to a set of regulations aimed at the preservation and maintenance of vegetation, particularly within development projects and urban environments. These regulations encompass aspects such as planting, maintaining, and protecting trees, ensuring that specific density requirements are met for various development initiatives. 

In zoning regulations, the term 'trees' includes provisions for tree planting and preservation within designated development areas, aligning with broader landscaping objectives. These regulations outline the essential requirements for the size and spacing of trees, which are critical for achieving aesthetically pleasing and environmentally sustainable landscapes, as reflected in standards such as the P1 Standard.

Trees are also described as natural living organisms characterized by a single trunk that supports branches and leaves. They play a significant role in environmental studies and land management due to their impact on local ecosystems. Additionally, regulations governing trees stipulate certain exemptions and conditions regarding their removal, underscoring the importance of protecting these vital organisms in urban and suburban settings.

Together, these elements highlight the multifaceted approach to tree regulation, emphasizing their ecological value and the need for thoughtful integration into development planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-235ba1708a9c48c75daf3faeec3e194d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70e49b32e27402af67173acaf34a3c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6638b6f4daad5d15b558bf7e5689cbbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e6e17bef16281bee8b4ad57adae456d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="City Designation">
      <data key="d0">City Designation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">City Designation refers to the official recognition of a resource as a Conservation Landmark, which entails certain protections and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;City designation refers to the local authority's process of designating or redesignating areas as historic districts through specific procedural guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;City designation refers to the classification of a property as a Historic Landmark, Conservation Landmark, Historic District, or Conservation District based on its significance and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;City designation refers to the classification of areas or buildings as Historic Landmark, Conservation Landmark, Historic District, or Conservation District based on their significance and integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b56b9fdbb25d0d73793d586c98486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d4fb6204c8defda427d1f8fff2f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059f078c9e0b5ea778bd163f9c511685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9157cebcd51ea7cec9c5bd83c0f3df47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Section 29.40.030">
      <data key="d0">Section 29.40.030</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 29.40.030 includes regulations concerning immediate demolition requirements for structures deemed dangerous.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 29.40.030 outlines the regulations related to Property Maintenance and specifies conditions under which demolition may be required.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b56b9fdbb25d0d73793d586c98486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fed5b9206a5c4a294b3284cd70adcb</data>
