    <node id="East Corridor Plan District">
      <data key="d0">East Corridor Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The East Corridor Plan District is a designated area in Portland that focuses on the planning and zoning of regions along the city's east corridor. It is governed by specific regulations as outlined in Title 33, specifically in Chapter 33.521, which establishes zoning and planning standards for land use and development within the district.

This area includes regulations that dictate building heights and floor area ratios, aimed at promoting urban development near light rail stations. Additionally, the East Corridor Plan District emphasizes enhancing connectivity, pedestrian access, and the creation of pedestrian amenities. These urban planning efforts are designed to encourage transit use and support development initiatives that align with the district's regulatory framework.

The East Corridor Plan District serves as a critical component of the city's overall urban planning strategy, with specific zoning regulations aimed at controlling development patterns and ensuring that the expansion of infrastructure is in line with transit-oriented goals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e32e03486b757e08e3d165c5c60acde4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e32407319712c8e952f9496e61eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7afd4cd98781a0f8a75a7fa3cd365098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-956eaa56417e66522506a103f450e0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f602644bfe17db01e93dfc05f1ddad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03d74d6b9596dd3ca6ee9b83679d2f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bce80dce3f6e46fbf15b845bbded504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78575afc304e77ddac795549d18c014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a043b4f466e82f380e009054fb98e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9a71f6df15462ffc6cb82fb99547c8</data>
