    </node>
    <node id="Building Setback Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Building Setback Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Building setback regulations are guidelines that serve various purposes including maintaining light, air, and fire protection as well as ensuring compatibility with neighborhood characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Building setback regulations dictate the distance structures must be from property lines, affecting architectural design and urban planning.</data>
