    <node id="Temporary Activities">
      <data key="d0">Temporary Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Temporary Activities refer to regulations surrounding short-term events and uses of land.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary Activities refer to events or installations that are not permanent and are established for a limited time.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary Activities refer to short-term events or uses of land that are regulated under Title 33, with specific conditions and limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary activities are defined as activities that are short-term or seasonal, without permanent improvements to the site.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary activities are short-term operations permissible under specific regulations, often in response to emergencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary Activities refer to events or uses of sites that are limited in duration, such as fairs, carnivals, and construction activities.</data>
