    <node id="St. Johns Plan District">
      <data key="d0">St. Johns Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The St. Johns Plan District is a designated urban area located in North Portland that focuses on planning processes and land use specific to the St. Johns neighborhood. This district is governed by particular zoning regulations and standards, which are detailed under Title 33, including Chapter 33.583. 

Within the St. Johns Plan District, there are specific guidelines regarding construction materials and building design to ensure that development aligns with the overarching vision for the area. These regulations encompass a range of planning and zoning standards that pertain to both commercial and civic development, emphasizing mixed-use projects. The St. Johns Plan District serves not only as a framework for maintaining the aesthetic and functional aspects of the community but also positions itself as a commercial and civic center in the region.

Overall, the St. Johns Plan District plays a crucial role in shaping the future of land use and development in St. Johns, guiding how new constructions are approached while adhering to established standards and promoting a vibrant community atmosphere.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e32e03486b757e08e3d165c5c60acde4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84bdf4402c70c4d4ae69283e01b9ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92185d9fe6c20f7172332a56db23c66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8275cc3c3a913fa46276d690bac66384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1ec40ef0c834d42a666a80a8223118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37ff07ffa7013303eef3ff22ca4c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b729b503408753bfb450541d299ca7</data>
