    <node id="Ground Floor Active Use">
      <data key="d0">Ground Floor Active Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ground Floor Active Use refers to regulations that require certain types of active uses on the ground floor of buildings in specified zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground Floor Active Use refers to a zoning standard requiring buildings to be listed on the City’s Historic Resources Inventory.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground Floor Active Use is a requirement that mandates active uses in commercial/mixed-use zones within close proximity to commercial corridors or streets.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground Floor Active Use denotes requirements for active use spaces in certain subdistricts of the York Plan District, fostering pedestrian interaction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff526385a57c5befe6ca7788e86d560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d95b223ce551df4ebded5324da87138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ce54762dd350a2baa6b3563a59fff3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd57b33ee4fb90b8e15b4036d8b2f9e3</data>
