    </node>
    <node id="Planning and Zoning Chapter 33.420">
      <data key="d0">Planning and Zoning Chapter 33.420</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Planning and Zoning Chapter 33.420 is a regulatory chapter within Title 33 that outlines specific requirements for building alterations, particularly regarding transmission facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Planning and Zoning Chapter 33.420 outlines specific design overlay zone requirements for new building constructions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff526385a57c5befe6ca7788e86d560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f19e6435928fe4a325e8a1a4cc5dd1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zoning Code">
      <data key="d0">Zoning Code</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Zoning Code is a comprehensive set of regulations governing land use and zoning classifications within a specific jurisdiction, particularly in Portland. It serves as the legal framework that dictates how land can be utilized and developed, encompassing various regulations, guidelines, and standards that apply to specific areas.

Specifically, the Zoning Code regulates all land and water use within Portland, ensuring that any development complies with established requirements. It consists of chapters and symbols represented in zoning maps, which detail the different zoning classifications and the corresponding development standards applicable to each zone. The code includes provisions for temporary activities, ensuring that all forms of land use are adequately managed.

In addition to standard regulations, the Zoning Code includes procedural requirements for obtaining building permits and planning approvals. These regulations encompass detailed steps for community agreements, including the Good Neighbor Agreement, and stipulations for appeals against land use decisions. The code is also designed to adapt automatically to specified dollar thresholds, ensuring that regulations remain relevant to economic changes.

The Zoning Code is vital for urban planning, as it sets forth guidelines for development while incorporating considerations for environmental protection. It may also intersect with development standards outlined in specific plans, such as the Northwest Master Plan and the PIR Master Plan, reflecting a coordinated approach to land use and community growth. 

Overall, the Zoning Code is essential for maintaining an organized and sustainable urban environment, providing a clearly defined framework for land use decisions within the city.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eda537024724fbc12582034b555f1424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb991309bb84fc2868a6a6763b75b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d751359bacfc149fb7266cc12789b1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2b2cd34a3e56fc1d7de2b3a42826d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f313ee8f50d5cdb880e71ed5eab739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d42b3010c15664b1fb208cc57e4facc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e362e6c3818ce32276e136b8d6e3bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8275cc3c3a913fa46276d690bac66384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47812462d7ccc96ffd0025a366f98586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa5d2c57a95ae65f663a55f78fa3c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95bbc1bcc87570cccffede2c40cb383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76f0e466ee927633a830eb76da6e9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c25a4b5dcdfc23b3bd64f8c6d4bbc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16970d294fd2c64906945840f8f4c3ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8e06f7fcece5e199a44dcbdcbf9d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc5679c2a480cf928223a40dfabf825d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f5cbe651ea348ef1311d4a24a92253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9daedca8ce38c66f76f89f5342070ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3ca6674563552f618f0433e3c4016a</data>
