    <node id="Transportation Impact Review">
      <data key="d0">Transportation Impact Review</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Transportation Impact Review is a comprehensive assessment process designed to analyze the effects of land-use changes and proposed developments on transportation systems. It focuses on understanding how such changes impact local infrastructure and transportation networks, particularly in relation to parking needs and overall transportation demand.

This review is especially crucial in campus institutional zones, where developments may significantly influence transportation requirements. The Transportation Impact Review process enables developers to assess how well the existing multimodal transportation system can accommodate new projects and to identify necessary mitigation measures to address any identified impacts. 

In addition to examining individual proposed developments, the Transportation Impact Review serves as a mechanism to approve maximum Floor Area Ratios (FAR) in specific subdistricts, thereby influencing planning and zoning regulations. Furthermore, the results of this assessment are relevant for a period of up to ten years, providing a framework for ongoing evaluation of transportation impacts in relation to new projects and developments in the area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e038f4d3687c0baca987d663a82852cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b2323b48f41f87137658c4c38c98ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79270fc3c081d0e0b0a71f05624d0eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80cb4c4524db16a443cea9724f5fd6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8cd0a693bdee1928f1f0600d5193c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbee049dd9c661ea5a90ad39db328689</data>
