    <node id="Severability">
      <data key="d0">Severability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Severability refers to the legal principle stipulating that if a part of the zoning code is deemed invalid, it can be severed without affecting the validity of the remaining code.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb991309bb84fc2868a6a6763b75b4e</data>
