    <node id="Open Space Zone">
      <data key="d0">Open Space Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Open Space Zone is a zoning classification aimed at preserving and enhancing public and private recreational areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Open Space Zone refers to designated areas intended for preservation and public use under specific zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Open Space Zone is a designated area outlined in Title 33, planning and zoning regulations, with specific use categories and regulations for land use.&lt;SEP&gt;Open Space Zone is a designated area within planning frameworks aimed at preserving open spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Open Space Zone designates areas where additional uses are permitted to enhance urban experiences in Central City.&lt;SEP&gt;The Open Space Zone is a land designation that aims to preserve land for recreational, natural, or agricultural uses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Open Space Zone is a designated area meant to preserve natural spaces and public uses while maintaining environmental resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb991309bb84fc2868a6a6763b75b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e1459a3e9df8bdd44292209ab034270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b31593c6056a4c4b7b5e1b873010f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7707c48b1e017649ebd08fb25641c1ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa7a4d254279e02d605594ebe069be0</data>
