    <node id="Gateway Plan District">
      <data key="d0">Gateway Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Gateway Plan District is a designated area within Portland, Oregon, that focuses on land use and development in conjunction with key access points into the city. It is governed by specific planning and zoning guidelines aimed at facilitating urban redevelopment and growth. As part of the Central City planning regulations, the Gateway Plan District encompasses superblock regulations that apply to developments, including the management of vacated streets.

This urban planning area is notable for its emphasis on mixed-use developments, promoting a variety of residential, commercial, and recreational spaces. In pursuit of enhancing urban environments, the Gateway Plan District includes regulations that enforce specific height requirements for buildings, as well as building floor area ratios. Open area and connectivity are also key aspects of the district’s development regulations, encouraging pedestrian-friendly designs and improved urban character along designated Enhanced Pedestrian Streets.

The Gateway Plan District operates under the regulations of Title 33, which dictates a strategic approach to urban planning. It is classified as a regional center, indicative of its importance in promoting further urban development and connectivity within Portland. With a planned transition from a suburban low-density space to a denser mixed-use environment, the Gateway Plan District reflects a shift in urban planning objectives that affects zoning and development decisions.

Furthermore, this district is set to establish updated zoning and development regulations starting January 1, 2025, aimed at enhancing both the existing urban fabric and the overall livability of the area. The Gateway Plan District exemplifies a comprehensive approach to urban planning that balances development with community needs and environmental considerations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e32e03486b757e08e3d165c5c60acde4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1f1b130f7e5afceced958bf6e3d52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8f030c470408395d5811f58b93edb14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b28b182d587540c8cdc8788f751c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e3be3ac7b6ba5960122bfee8047a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d46523b43ad78784d5fd13052c9870a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-956eaa56417e66522506a103f450e0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48080692bc899a8f3606cd61bb319bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b4c57adc2cf94d9a0a99114828453df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeb1ca82658d21ff2c231993f9597a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e317f6dbe5f15015c8e4149009a9021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd915bc95a0b87e710beaeeee303a655</data>
