    <node id="Structured Parking">
      <data key="d0">Structured Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Structured Parking refers to organized parking facilities that are specifically designed to accommodate vehicles in a structured manner, typically within constructed environments. These facilities must comply with various building and setback standards for exits and entrances, ensuring they are integrated into residential developments or urban layouts effectively. 

Structured Parking usually involves multi-level parking structures, which differentiate themselves from traditional open surface lots by maximizing the use of vertical space. This design approach not only increases the number of vehicles that can be parked within a limited footprint but also often includes features such as covered areas that protect vehicles from the elements. 

Generally defined, Structured Parking is characterized by its adherence to specific standards and regulations, ensuring that these facilities are both functional and efficient. Their design aims to organize parking spaces compactly, enhancing spatial utilization while providing ease of access for users. As such, Structured Parking plays a vital role in modern urban planning, addressing the growing demand for efficient vehicle accommodation in increasingly populated spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-84efb40ac49907b061aeb00bb2d08948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2cc6a137a6b419b9a37152153b673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d46c43c9570caf791239d0c34502c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7a46ce2a41072cf8f503e930128f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44467970b01c8dde6cd5f9a7210f332e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ab64be803cdc30ed89433c92047a024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92d544a559cce4659ea9ffd7dad0732c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde</data>
