    <node id="Table 120-4">
      <data key="d0">Table 120-4</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 120-4 is a comprehensive summary of development standards specifically tailored for multi-dwelling zones. It serves as a critical reference for various zoning metrics and requirements that govern developmental activities within these zones. The table delineates the maximum Floor Area Ratio (FAR) applicable to all developments and uses, ensuring compliance with established zoning regulations.

In addition to delineating FAR, Table 120-4 specifies minimum density requirements essential for maintaining the appropriate balance of residential units within multi-dwelling zones. It further outlines required minimum building setbacks for different building categories, which plays a vital role in ensuring adequate space and access around structures.

The table also addresses maximum density and building coverage standards particularly relevant to specific zones, such as the Residential Mixed Use (RMP) zone and other multi-dwelling zones. By including regulations on building setbacks associated with transit streets and Pedestrian Districts, Table 120-4 highlights its influence on building design and placement, fostering an environment considerate of both urban planning and community needs.

Moreover, it incorporates detailed standards related to building coverage and setbacks for various zones, ensuring a cohesive framework for development in multi-dwelling areas. This synthesis of information makes Table 120-4 an essential guideline for stakeholders involved in urban planning and zoning compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eded02aea3f115ba99e1a14dd25ad585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c86bea48b8b39caf895ea538d23c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2cc6a137a6b419b9a37152153b673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-903ef5f8da50cf2a59819dcb0eda03b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd85ebb9182c99ebc70e5ecbfe9d7ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3901520644b000ca953e813d65ccc92</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781049</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Household Living">
      <data key="d0">Household Living</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Household Living is a term that encompasses a range of residential arrangements within designated living spaces. This category pertains specifically to residential uses allowed under regulatory frameworks, such as Title 33. Household Living typically involves individual housing units that are fully dedicated to living purposes, where all floor areas are utilized for residential living.

The concept of Household Living primarily focuses on land use associated with residential living arrangements. It includes not only single-family dwellings but also other structures designed for these purposes. The regulations governing Household Living ensure that such uses maintain appropriate building and circulation standards and are protected from potential disruptions caused by the introduction of non-residential uses.

Household Living is characterized as a type of land use that accommodates residential dwellings, specifically noting occupancy limits, which commonly include dwelling units with eight or fewer bedrooms. In these settings, tenancy is often on a month-to-month basis, catering to individuals or families who typically reside within these units. Overall, Household Living embodies various forms of residential occupancy, ensuring orderly living arrangements in accordance with specific regulatory criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fee202a5a178704f7fab97145229db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5a24cd6c84e70b31e0e64f3773ddd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930256b3bb4008d11b0886f29973ea67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78b8d8f5df1d607fc21562bc53c145e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcf2b390429bc7c420c7c4a2aa0cb76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4cc500f0cf6ffd63a8f594c9055457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e7feaddec557941c697fec7b2e2763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781050</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone is a designated area aimed at the protection and management of critical natural resources within Pleasant Valley. This zone is subject to specific regulations that govern natural resource management and development practices, ensuring both preservation and careful consideration during site planning and evaluations.

The regulations associated with the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone include development standards that are designed to minimize any potential impact on the area's natural resources. These standards emphasize restricted land development and particularly focus on enhancing and safeguarding the functional values of the environment.

In addition to preservation efforts, the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone also allows for limited new development, provided that such activities adhere to the established environmental regulations. The zone facilitates a careful balance between development needs and environmental integrity, including provisions for the transfer of development rights to further protect the natural landscape.

Overall, the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone represents a concerted effort to integrate environmental protection with land use planning, enforcing specific zoning practices that directly relate to both resource conservation and sustainable development within its geographical limits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a427590c6154215eabffa8c6cfc3461e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a10cf031f788aa8206369e4c6c630d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2762500c7c689febd52ecacda4e0e39d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370bd3a55fe045150292fe6445463a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28182b619a9a912d117b6795858e20f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-088fe9a8bf4c7d50c85bec432d0ca5c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90974c5207e30c3839f91710f5169ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca9af7fb86386b5d8e07a8895278701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ef9b400f3f8eaf84f03bdff42a7221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ff3afda2034b66968957b4926a887c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616a6925a0ab31d5e3e594ef74a2e21d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feff08f8742feb2b38fee34824605dc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9fa7bda2d110e7a4636f9b2c3016a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ade629e2e0020483f573660fbe8416a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51dc10f7cf6f3ff9bea2eb170cf1c4dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31394699e4c236c5efd0bec39e7a8ab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
