    <node id="Nuisance Plants List">
      <data key="d0">Nuisance Plants List</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Nuisance Plants List is an official inventory detailing plant species that are prohibited from being planted or propagated in specific areas due to their undesirable or invasive nature. The list includes plants that are banned from city-required landscaped areas, mitigation areas, and Environmental Zones, with the primary goal of protecting native vegetation and adhering to environmental regulations.

This list categorizes certain plant species as problematic, which may lead to their removal under specific regulatory guidelines. The Nuisance Plants List is particularly relevant within designated zones such as the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone and the Rocky Butte plan district. In these locations, the list outlines which species may not be planted and may necessitate removal if found within the specified areas.

Additionally, the Nuisance Plants List encompasses groundcovers and shrubs, as well as trees identified as invasive or harmful. Removal of these plants can occur during construction activities for trails or recreational facilities, irrespective of standard diameter restrictions. The document serves as a critical component of local landscaping regulations, impacting land use and development by specifying undesirable tree species and those exempt from tree preservation laws.

Overall, the Nuisance Plants List is a regulatory resource managed by the Bureau of Planning and Sustainability, aiming to mitigate the impact of invasive species on local ecosystems and promote the health of native plant communities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00a7652f0b0b380d8dc6c5c8262a6ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9af1918e6e2060f112e9e0fc6b76a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277acf18eaddbd1593ad5f3cfa3a6cab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9b97086444d872e3bea48cd8e3ed5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370bd3a55fe045150292fe6445463a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a079f6fb5c8d245b04e7b9c62fbfa8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-899c4b9a2ac9d3d9713b5cef39a863b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356d9265a5791545fa23fa54dee260f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90974c5207e30c3839f91710f5169ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2fc1b73b6e1ae4e82cbaf205ce719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82ef9b400f3f8eaf84f03bdff42a7221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77c0e594bc319fd143848146f9ea56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ff3afda2034b66968957b4926a887c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feff08f8742feb2b38fee34824605dc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9fa7bda2d110e7a4636f9b2c3016a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285f052019746f5b49b63ae041c898aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99992d12911944db6172dcc6b2ae4ab5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059e173ef884a58e8cd223998e6158d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d11d225e5566d1ff994f2025b1378ec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8e044b1fd94ca567e1458bbd0323ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa149f451b6af62929512ddc6383e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbcf1c43cb59d25662f5af1b9ac994a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fbbf35a5a5146ae4034375e7576374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d54757bbd8eb99b2b0cd39a957603d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbf464d578679736d29b0ac61c4cd5d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad866e29e441289a8f35f6617f6b3691</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IH Zone">
      <data key="d0">IH Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The IH Zone is a specific zoning classification designed primarily for industrial uses, allowing for a high degree of developmental flexibility without imposing coverage limits. This flexibility is coupled with certain regulations to ensure compatibility within the industrial context. The IH Zone shares characteristics with other zones, particularly the IG and EG2 zones, specifically regarding height limitations and setback requirements.

Within the IH Zone, certain environmental development standards are exempted, marking it as a unique area where industrial activities can thrive with fewer restrictions compared to other zoning designations. However, to mitigate potential conflicts with nonindustrial activities, specific prohibitions are enforced against nonindustrial uses. This zoning area is strategically located within the Guild's Lake Industrial Sanctuary, an area predominantly dedicated to industrial purposes.

The IH Zone has specific parking regulations allowing for accessory parking under defined conditions, which facilitates access and usability for businesses operating in this area. To qualify for the zoning regulations outlined in Chapter 33.664, sites classified under the IH Zone must meet a minimum lot size of at least 340,000 square feet. The zone places an emphasis on adherence to minimum lot dimension standards, further aligning with the industrial focus of the area.

Additionally, the IH Zone may apply alternative regulations concerning land divisions, contingent upon site size. Overall, the IH Zone is well-defined for heavy industrial usage, ensuring that its regulations are conducive to the intended industrial development while aiming to minimize conflicts with surrounding environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdb0ed86328221b3f3b4bc1f84ed339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-221d1ae9cf50b3236ae14ae949934120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebeee1e9a6fdc5e2eb02bb6563ce14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d1801c38b4789f81c89f16cc033283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbed3d0d9f1ce8f7b4b9d7df85935cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0147b437f8af7c9b75d571f1f8e2392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retail Sales And Service">
      <data key="d0">Retail Sales And Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Retail Sales And Service refers to a category of businesses that provide goods or services directly to consumers, encompassing various commercial activities. This category includes retail establishments, personal service providers, and repair-oriented services. Retail Sales And Service is subject to specific zoning regulations that govern their operations, particularly in designated areas like Single-Dwelling Zones and Open Space Zones.

In the context of zoning regulations, Retail Sales And Service is recognized as a specific land use category with conditional regulations, especially concerning outdoor seating, exterior display, storage, and overall business footprint. These regulations aim to mitigate the impact on surrounding properties and ensure compatibility with the existing environment, particularly in industrial areas like the IH Zone, where business activities are limited to reduce interference with industrial operations.

Furthermore, Retail Sales And Service is associated with businesses that may include transient lodging options, such as hotels or motels, designed for short stays. The category encompasses sizes of developments that must adhere to specific approval criteria, particularly those exceeding 10,000 square feet. It is also noted that these businesses are encouraged to enhance pedestrian environments, reflecting a broader urban planning objective.

Overall, Retail Sales And Service integrates a variety of commercial uses, emphasizing the direct sale of goods and personal services, while adhering to local zoning laws to support orderly growth and development in communities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b2cc8f6a45d17941e977fde3debc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5a24cd6c84e70b31e0e64f3773ddd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d67d6ae3fefc0ae11f57c206f31b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930256b3bb4008d11b0886f29973ea67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b98f4030f1ba695567caadac80f6cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379809e916e9cfdca408ec201f1ff1c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d735bdaad55969341cee3cca65a09caf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ce319f7fcb7893676edd6b489a8b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b01451771b358c77494f198e0c0a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfa11b893b09fc1fb7d6655be073aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157f892dc3db1b7d5113b58ec80ccd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d1801c38b4789f81c89f16cc033283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78575afc304e77ddac795549d18c014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9a71f6df15462ffc6cb82fb99547c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49a157902a76856c95e4e3a050a0ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3</data>
