    <node id="Land Division">
      <data key="d0">Land Division</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Land Division is a procedural term that encompasses the process of subdividing a larger parcel of land into smaller plots for various purposes, such as development, sale, or as part of planned development proposals. This process must align with specific zoning regulations and is governed by regulations outlined in Section 33.564, which stipulates the necessary compliance and ethical considerations.

The primary function of Land Division is to prepare land for development by ensuring that all newly created lots can accommodate essential infrastructure services. It involves not only the mechanical act of splitting land into smaller parcels but also navigating the regulatory landscape to secure the necessary approvals for such actions. Among its various applications, Land Division is particularly relevant in the context of manufactured dwelling parks and similarly categorized developments.

Moreover, the Land Division process is subject to zoning codes, and it is often necessary to make adjustments based on local considerations and regulatory requirements. Successful navigation of these requirements ensures that the division aligns with the overarching land use policies and contributes to the orderly development of the area involved. 

In summary, Land Division is an essential element of land management, facilitating the establishment of new lots or the reconfiguration of existing ones while adhering to regulatory standards and zoning laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6bcfb59e4095f5b02abc8ac31213ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32beb3a9e96c3d41cc526d4dbd0b1f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41abaceb8097519bba26a5ccb4274c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ffc992b5e373540a3ee78f16308e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f5ada1bd73ae6d3ab8a5bb43ff6e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2546da1b6188ab781e1777780334eb3</data>
