    <node id="CM2">
      <data key="d0">CM2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CM2 is a zoning designation that governs building heights and density in urban planning contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;CM2 is a commercial zoning classification with specific height limits and projections for buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;CM2 is a zoning designation categorized under Mixed Use which allows for specific development types according to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a966c4eaabe25aca0a1be25bd188299e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb053937b4fd6958f885edbd491a92e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8dedd6570aca440bb011dbffebca8f0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CM3">
      <data key="d0">CM3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CM3 is a zoning category with defined regulations for maximum heights and density in city planning.&lt;SEP&gt;CM3 is a commercial zoning classification that has particular regulations for height and structure features.&lt;SEP&gt;CM3 refers to another type of Mixed Use zoning classification that includes particular development guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a966c4eaabe25aca0a1be25bd188299e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb053937b4fd6958f885edbd491a92e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8dedd6570aca440bb011dbffebca8f0</data>
