    </node>
    <node id="Parking Demand Management">
      <data key="d0">Parking Demand Management</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking Demand Management refers to strategies aimed at optimizing parking availability and usage in urban areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management refers to strategies enacted to regulate and optimize parking facilities and transportation impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management refers to the strategies aimed at limiting parking spaces to promote efficient land use and alternative transportation modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management refers to strategies and practices aimed at optimizing parking utilization and managing parking needs within urban environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management is a facet of Transportation Demand Management aimed at managing the demand for parking facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management involves strategies and practices aimed at optimizing parking resources and reducing demand for parking in urban areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking Demand Management encompasses strategies designed to control and optimize parking availability and usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d771f61eac49b01fc5796204c75025ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b430ca141ad0936b7b20ef5f23780667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46af1a858cb150fbd0c6e6b2b602464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78b8d8f5df1d607fc21562bc53c145e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79270fc3c081d0e0b0a71f05624d0eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67111441a3c9d2875734e7bedb42d3af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Level 2 Electric Vehicle Charger">
      <data key="d0">Level 2 Electric Vehicle Charger</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Level 2 electric vehicle chargers are specific charging stations that must be located within 5 feet of a vehicle area if held by a detached structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A Level 2 Electric Vehicle Charger is a type of charger designed for electric vehicles, capable of faster charging compared to standard chargers.&lt;SEP&gt;A Level 2 electric vehicle charger is a charging unit designed to provide faster charging services for electric vehicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 Electric Vehicle Charger is a type of charger for electric vehicles that provides a faster charging option.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e452b9ec8a9af12b429462d8859d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b20838d5c5f56512690b976a12ae34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbed3d0d9f1ce8f7b4b9d7df85935cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 191942">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 191942</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 191942 is a legislative order that amends the zoning code and is set to become effective on January 1, 2025. It functions as a crucial regulation within the broader spectrum of zoning laws, specifically related to planning and zoning regulations. This ordinance is referred to in various contexts, emphasizing its role in modifying existing local regulations.

The effective date of January 1, 2025, is consistently noted across multiple descriptions, affirming the ordinance's significance as a legal measure that will influence zoning frameworks once implemented. Ord. No. 191942 also reflects amendments made to Title 33, which indicates its specific focus on local governance and land use planning.

Overall, Ord. No. 191942 represents an important step in the evolution of legislative measures pertaining to zoning, aligning with a structured approach to managing land use in the community it governs. Its uniform effective date across all descriptions highlights its impending relevance in the legal landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb991309bb84fc2868a6a6763b75b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3ac296609c32cc7de194b33256a6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c4f9e9e16adccaf92b860a8f225b4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92185d9fe6c20f7172332a56db23c66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23f6f27b8a490522d8ea471d51807cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2046790125dcdbb2805d0592a8edd3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 179980">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 179980</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 179980 is an ordinance that became effective on April 22, 2006. This legislative measure plays a significant role in amending existing planning and zoning regulations. Specifically, Ord. No. 179980 pertains to zoning-related issues, including modifications to the Central City Plan District and contributing to regulations about tree preservation plans.

The ordinance has been referenced in various contexts, all indicating that its amendments and legal measures were formalized and took effect on the aforementioned date, consistently noted across the descriptions as 4/22/06. It is classified as a legal document involved in local governance, aimed at enhancing the regulatory framework concerning urban planning.

In summary, Ord. No. 179980 serves as an important legislative tool that shapes the planning and zoning landscape, marking its relevance with a specific effective date that underscores its implementation in legal protocols.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19a2393681785537b2d0f83af94a363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8537f80e77714b5b0188914023a593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0352df0641b29208d29e9ef4be447b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98ccf18b3f007cbd17c7784ea27d4cca</data>
