      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Right-of-Way">
      <data key="d0">Right-of-Way</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Right-of-way is a legal right to pass through property and can influence the regulations regarding fences.&lt;SEP&gt;Right-of-way standards dictate the maximum widths permitted for various types of roadways and streets according to specified tables.&lt;SEP&gt;A right-of-way is a legal right to pass through ground or property owned by another party, particularly relevant to the placement of utility lines and road networks in the overlay zone.&lt;SEP&gt;A right-of-way is a legal right for a party to pass through property owned by another party, requiring maintenance agreements to ensure upkeep by the owner.&lt;SEP&gt;Right-of-way refers to portions of land that contain development, including various structures and traffic areas, excluding natural geologic forms or unimproved land.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ead15b7371d315a50edc3463b2359a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ade629e2e0020483f573660fbe8416a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4271bb9cc0287dcb0b401b760eb4864e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8263d3660b494322f6b2d93ee1245f2d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781057</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="120-Day Delay Procedure">
      <data key="d0">120-Day Delay Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The 120-Day Delay Procedure is a legal protocol that prohibits issuing building permits for demolition or exterior alteration of a significant resource during the delay period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781057</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Resource">
      <data key="d0">Significant Resource</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Significant Resource is a resource recognized for its historic value within a National Register District, relevant to the regulations regarding demolition and alterations.&lt;SEP&gt;Significant Resource refers to a valued item or structure recognized in the Historic Resource Inventory, which undergoes special procedures for demolition or relocation.&lt;SEP&gt;A Significant Resource refers to a building or structure proposed for demolition, which may undergo review processes before any alterations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Significant Resource is a building, structure, or landscape deemed valuable for its archaeological, architectural, cultural, or historical significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4fed5b9206a5c4a294b3284cd70adcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="State Historic Preservation Office">
      <data key="d0">State Historic Preservation Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The State Historic Preservation Office is an organization that ensures the protection and preservation of historic resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The State Historic Preservation Office is the authority that identifies and protects archaeological resources and historical sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The State Historic Preservation Office (SHPO) is responsible for maintaining records and permits related to archaeological resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The State Historic Preservation Office is responsible for notifying the Bureau of Planning and Sustainability about listings and removals from the National Register of Historic Places.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4395c057e21d1b49701c5d6e444bef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-721ec91bd394c742ab66be71cc2391f1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 186639">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 186639</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 186639 is an ordinance that became effective on July 11, 2014. This ordinance specifically pertains to regulations within the framework of planning and zoning. It was amended prior to its effective date and has significant implications for land use and zoning systems, particularly influencing the development regulations and the Central City Plan District.

The regulations outlined in Ord. No. 186639 have been described as a legislative measure that amends existing rules related to planning and zoning. This ordinance has been referenced multiple times in the context of regulatory changes and has been noted as essential in shaping local governance concerning these topics. Overall, Ord. No. 186639 represents a crucial update in the legal framework governing urban planning within its jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3ac296609c32cc7de194b33256a6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d39d3e5dc5ac990b049b748fa4e96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19a2393681785537b2d0f83af94a363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e362e6c3818ce32276e136b8d6e3bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616a6925a0ab31d5e3e594ef74a2e21d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76f0e466ee927633a830eb76da6e9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23f6f27b8a490522d8ea471d51807cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3f9ffb1d8c7f041a89cac2f7df9d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f525a8329ffe0f200c2898df08550d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bce80dce3f6e46fbf15b845bbded504</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Historic Preservation Incentives">
      <data key="d0">Historic Preservation Incentives</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Historic Preservation Incentives are benefits designed to encourage the preservation, rehabilitation, and reuse of historic resources, making them more appealing to owners and tenants.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a971b09f4393ef1136ed16b956179c6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot Dimension Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Lot Dimension Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot Dimension Regulations outline the standards and requirements for lot sizes and shapes in specific zoning areas to facilitate proper development.</data>
