      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 185915 is an ordinance that became effective on May 1, 2013. This ordinance is significant in its role as it amends various regulations, particularly related to zoning and planning, under the Central City Plan District. It modifies planning and zoning regulations, shapes land use policies, and adjusts design review frameworks, emphasizing its comprehensive impact on development regulations.

The ordinance has been described in multiple instances as specifically relating to zoning amendments, highlighting its importance in the regulatory landscape that governs land use and development. It is categorized as a legal ordinance, reasserting its formal standing within the regulatory framework. The effective date of May 1, 2013, provided in various formats, consistently underscores the ordinance's timeline and application to ongoing planning and zoning processes. 

In summary, Ord. No. 185915 serves as a crucial ordinance that amended and updated several regulatory aspects, with its effects continuing to influence land use policies since its inception.</data>
