    <node id="Ord. No. 188259">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 188259</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 188259 is an ordinance that became effective on March 31, 2017. This ordinance plays a significant role in regulating various aspects of urban planning and zoning. It specifically contributes to the establishment of regulations concerning tree preservation plans, which are essential for maintaining ecological balance and urban greenery.

Additionally, Ord. No. 188259 is associated with design review processes, ensuring that new developments are consistent with the broader planning objectives of the community. The amendments introduced by this ordinance represent a concerted effort to enhance the planning and zoning framework, providing clear guidelines for both preservation and development initiatives.

Overall, Ord. No. 188259 is an essential legislative action that addresses important environmental and urban planning concerns, reflecting the local government's commitment to sustainable development practices.</data>
