      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 189000</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 189000 is a municipal ordinance that became effective on July 9, 2018. This legal ordinance specifically addresses planning and zoning regulations, making significant amendments within the Central City Plan District. Additionally, it introduced changes to design review regulations and is associated with the River Review process. 

The ordinance was added to Chapter 33.840 and reflects a legislative effort to update municipal regulations relevant to urban planning. The effective date of July 9, 2018, marks a crucial point for the implementation of these amendments, illustrating the city's ongoing commitment to manage its development and zoning frameworks more effectively. 

Overall, Ord. No. 189000 serves as a record of the regulatory updates established to improve urban planning and zoning within the jurisdiction it governs.</data>
