      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 187216</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 187216 is a legislative ordinance that became effective on July 24, 2015. This ordinance amends existing regulations specifically related to drive-through facilities, planning and zoning regulations, and the Central City Plan District. It falls within the framework of Title 33, which governs land use and development regulations.

The ordinance has provisions that influence various aspects of development regulations, including design review and tree preservation plans. It serves to update and improve regulatory guidelines pertaining to zoning in the respective areas mentioned. Throughout its descriptions, Ord. No. 187216 is consistently noted as a legal ordinance, confirming its formal standing in the legislative process.

Overall, Ord. No. 187216 plays a critical role in shaping the regulatory landscape of urban development as of its effective date, impacting multiple dimensions of land use and planning.</data>
