    <node id="Quick Vehicle Servicing">
      <data key="d0">Quick Vehicle Servicing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Quick Vehicle Servicing refers to a category of uses allowed to have associated drive-through facilities within certain zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Vehicle Servicing is a type of facility that includes fueling positions, with a maximum number defined for simultaneous use.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick vehicle servicing includes automotive services that are sometimes restricted depending on the subdistrict regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Vehicle Servicing is categorized as an industrial use that may require documentation if previously existing on a site.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Vehicle Servicing encompasses services for vehicles where drivers typically wait while the service is performed.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Vehicle Servicing provides direct services for vehicles, typically with the driver waiting in the car during the service.&lt;SEP&gt;Quick Vehicle Servicing is an automotive service category allowing quick maintenance or repairs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a373581b2a74183e9eed060dd888030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49a157902a76856c95e4e3a050a0ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5a24cd6c84e70b31e0e64f3773ddd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a901459905390cbd8ce9c02b74a9fd1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652d83d3265624b311b9bf8c778fdd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc617f6f881f3f98f97136cfa84f2ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3</data>
