    <node id="Land Division Site">
      <data key="d0">Land Division Site</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Land Division Site refers to a designated area for the development and allocation of rights-of-way to facilitate transportation and access.&lt;SEP&gt;The Land Division Site refers to a specified area that may undergo division for development purposes, including zoning considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;A land division site refers to a designated area where new lots are developed, including private streets, shared courts, and common greens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-382ea5f9bd1d1962a9c0ded6051b139a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc4ad1e18166e18f3ffc6869780387e3</data>
