    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 190687">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 190687</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 190687 is a legal ordinance that became effective on March 1, 2022. This ordinance is primarily associated with planning and zoning regulations, and it includes amendments relevant to the Central City Plan District. It also touches upon regulations concerning conditional uses and design review processes.

The ordinance aims to update and clarify existing regulations to improve city planning and land use management. Its effective date, March 1, 2022, marks the commencement of these updated guidelines, signaling a significant step in the legal frameworks governing urban development within the affected areas. Ord. No. 190687 serves as a crucial regulatory document that influences various administrative procedures related to zoning and planning within the jurisdiction it governs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b2c3f3b605bc9f877b7485abc23364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98ccf18b3f007cbd17c7784ea27d4cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22f515f37bfa2d9c859d1b9c66c32763</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OS, R, C, E, CI, IR Zones">
      <data key="d0">OS, R, C, E, CI, IR Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">OS, R, C, E, CI, and IR Zones are classifications of land use that determine the applicable standards for land division proposals.&lt;SEP&gt;OS, R, C, E, CI, and IR Zones refer to various zoning classifications that dictate land use and development guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-382ea5f9bd1d1962a9c0ded6051b139a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pleasant Valley Natural Resource">
      <data key="d0">Pleasant Valley Natural Resource</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pleasant Valley Natural Resource refers to environmental regions designated under zoning laws that impact development and land use decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pleasant Valley Natural Resource refers to the natural resources specific to the Pleasant Valley area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49961939512caa6917f2206eb92e7d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tree Groves">
      <data key="d0">Tree Groves</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Tree groves are areas of grouped trees within a site that may have protective regulations affecting land use and development.&lt;SEP&gt;Tree Groves are groupings of trees that may hold ecological or aesthetic significance and need to be identified during planning and zoning evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f65e5459208816c049f71f8dc6ffc84e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Streams">
      <data key="d0">Streams</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Streams are bodies of flowing water that can influence zoning decisions and development requirements in adjacent sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Streams are natural watercourses that must be preserved in easements if located outside of Environmental Overlay Zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dc64b571fc1e4051ea286aa94de68c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wetlands">
      <data key="d0">Wetlands</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Wetlands are ecosystems that require specific setbacks and protections in the River Water Quality overlay zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Wetlands are environmentally sensitive areas that require protection under state and federal regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Wetlands are ecologically sensitive areas that may impose restrictions on development due to their environmental importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Wetlands are areas where water is present, which must be preserved in easements if located outside of Environmental Overlay Zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Wetlands are areas saturated by water, supporting vegetation adapted to such conditions, including swamps and bogs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7014f2d99071dd5f926719c5b91b21ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed32ffcf90280c2cd045c39203b18c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0271e8b27cedc9b0b135f529688a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dc64b571fc1e4051ea286aa94de68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a187157e908115a4998c100f65fb8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacf586128716bb40a914b64e071f666</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Building Coverage Standards">
      <data key="d0">Building Coverage Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Building Coverage Standards define the maximum footprint of buildings on a lot to control overall bulk and ensure compatibility with surrounding structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Coverage Standards outline the maximum allowed building coverage for dwelling units and accessory structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Coverage Standards regulate the footprint of buildings to maintain desired urban density and aesthetic coherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Building coverage standards regulate the overall bulk of structures and their footprint in specific zoning areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Building coverage standards limit the area covered by structures to maintain the character of a zone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c54aa01b8a84d0bf5d8975d9c8cc8b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dce4a7be57273a9865cad046f69ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58aaae1598e79c7b72066b698da3a9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 110-5">
      <data key="d0">Table 110-5</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 110-5 specifies the maximum building coverage allowed based on lot size in various residential zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Main Entrances">
      <data key="d0">Main Entrances</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Main entrances must adhere to specific standards to ensure accessibility and aesthetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Main Entrances standards ensure that residential structures have visible and accessible pedestrian entrances that connect effectively to the street.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R10 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R10 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The R10 Zone is a designation for single-dwelling residential areas characterized by specific zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The R10 zone is a zoning classification that mandates specific standards for cottage cluster sites, including minimum area and density.&lt;SEP&gt;The R10 Zone requires a minimum lot area of 6,000 square feet for dwellings.&lt;SEP&gt;The R10 zone is another residential zoning classification with specific minimum lot area requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The R10 Zone is a residential zoning classification permitting a higher density of dwellings compared to the R20 Zone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65a020b68966aec020e3367f56ac854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e889d237f01a5093e629880a38d5a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fee5077b9b5bae2a7dec413478071a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimum Building Setbacks">
      <data key="d0">Minimum Building Setbacks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimum Building Setbacks refer to the regulations specifying how far back a building must be set from property lines based on height.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimum Landscaped Area">
      <data key="d0">Minimum Landscaped Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimum Landscaped Area refers to the requirement for a specified percentage of site area to be dedicated to landscaping, set at 25% for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Minimum Landscaped Area refers to the regulation requiring at least 20% of the site area to be landscaped.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Buffering Standards">
      <data key="d0">Buffering Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Buffering Standards refer to the regulations detailing the distance requirements for buffering from residential zones, including a 10 ft. buffer to L1 and L3 standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 191310">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 191310</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 191310 is an ordinance that became effective on June 30, 2023. This legal measure encompasses planning and zoning regulations, addressing changes in these areas. The ordinance has been described as a legislative order or measure, signifying its formal status within a legal framework.

Additionally, Ord. No. 191310 also refers to a set of regulations that pertain to planning and zoning, specifically highlighting its relevance to conditional uses. The ordinance not only outlines the new regulations but also includes amendments, ensuring its applicability to evolving community needs.

In summary, Ord. No. 191310 is a comprehensive legislative measure intended to update and regulate planning and zoning practices, officially taking effect on June 30, 2023.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3ac296609c32cc7de194b33256a6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f525a8329ffe0f200c2898df08550d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b2c3f3b605bc9f877b7485abc23364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bce80dce3f6e46fbf15b845bbded504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f0a7e50ec5c262cdb4140ddc318c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22f515f37bfa2d9c859d1b9c66c32763</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parking and Loading">
      <data key="d0">Parking and Loading</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking and loading regulations define requirements for vehicle accommodation in developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking and Loading regulations outline requirements for parking facilities and vehicle loading areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking and Loading includes regulations related to vehicle parking provisions and loading zones at a property.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking and Loading pertains to guidelines described in Chapter 33.266 related to the management of vehicle parking and loading areas in developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking and Loading concerns spaces allocated for vehicle parking and areas designated for loading and unloading of goods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Detached Accessory Structures Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Detached Accessory Structures Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Detached Accessory Structures Regulations outline the specific rules governing the placement and construction of accessory structures on a property.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="School Use">
      <data key="d0">School Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">School use refers to the operational status of a school on a site, which can be discontinued or may require a conditional use review.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C and E Zones">
      <data key="d0">C and E Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">C and E zones are zones where schools are generally allowed by right, according to the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;C and E zones are designated areas where specific regulations apply for institutional uses, including schools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30acaad3495315145b81fed5d7cb9158</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Park">
      <data key="d0">Public Park</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Public parks are areas contiguous with school sites that can influence development standards and agreements.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Park is an outdoor space designated for community use, often characterized by recreational areas and facilities for children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a9d69b412438d9027f85a2c39c69e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 191609">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 191609</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 191609 is a legal ordinance that will become effective on March 1, 2024. This ordinance specifically amends Title 33 and relates to planning and zoning regulations, including land use and building permits. It addresses various aspects of planning, including conditional uses and design review processes, establishing new regulations and adjustments to existing standards.

The ordinance is designed to implement amendments affecting zoning matters, reflecting changes in regulatory frameworks to accommodate evolving land use needs. In particular, Ord. No. 191609 introduces new procedures and guidelines aimed at improving the effectiveness of planning and zoning practices. All changes stipulated by this ordinance will take effect on the specified date, reinforcing the importance of timely compliance with updated legal requirements in the realm of urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23f6f27b8a490522d8ea471d51807cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b2c3f3b605bc9f877b7485abc23364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94f04c4574ac8473fb645f2bd083c638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22f515f37bfa2d9c859d1b9c66c32763</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781061</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Joint Use Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Joint Use Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A joint use agreement is a formal arrangement that allows shared use of facilities, such as a park by a school.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781062</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Schools and School Sites">
      <data key="d0">Schools and School Sites</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Schools and School Sites cover the planning and development of educational institutions and their infrastructures.&lt;SEP&gt;Schools and School Sites are locations designated for educational institutions and related facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Schools and School Sites encompasses the regulations related to the establishment and operation of educational institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Schools and School Sites refers to regulations concerning the use and development of school properties, emphasizing community integration and recreational activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Schools and school sites relate to the guidelines and regulations concerning educational facilities and their operational conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd57b33ee4fb90b8e15b4036d8b2f9e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ff07d99a0c758d3b51f7e05d950738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781062</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metro Urban Growth Boundary">
      <data key="d0">Metro Urban Growth Boundary</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Metro Urban Growth Boundary (UGB) defines the limits for urban development, impacting planning and zoning decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781062</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Future Urban Zone">
      <data key="d0">Future Urban Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Future Urban Zone designates regions planned for future urban development.&lt;SEP&gt;The Future Urban Zone is a regulatory designation that limits development and prohibits the creation of new lots with an area less than 20 acres to prevent environmental harm.&lt;SEP&gt;The Future Urban Zone limits development in specified urban areas according to the framework for land use planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9916243fd6ec8d5d7a01e1c0d8f2bd77</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781062</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
