    <node id="Chapter 33.120">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.120</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.120 is a regulatory framework within the Portland City Code that delineates planning and zoning regulations specifically for Multi-Dwelling Zones. This chapter encompasses a wide range of provisions that address various aspects of multi-dwelling development, including lot size, development standards, and the types of housing permissible within these zones.

The chapter specifies standards related to development features such as building setbacks, coverage, entrance requirements, and the characteristics specific to street-facing facades. It also outlines regulations regarding landscaping, fencing, and the inclusion of detached covered accessory structures, ensuring that development within these zones adheres to defined aesthetic and functional guidelines.

In summary, Chapter 33.120 serves as a comprehensive set of rules that governs the planning and zoning of multi-dwelling zones in Portland, aiming to create orderly and sustainable residential environments while establishing clear standards for developers and architects involved in these projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0db595deea447329ffb950dc6a8bf8b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2cc6a137a6b419b9a37152153b673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd49cb12bde2e181e43e4b3ea44c114c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586262724750ed4bbb098ac0aed41049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97c549f439b335c735e299563e1e4c63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd85ebb9182c99ebc70e5ecbfe9d7ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b659477574fcf7f35453f172163de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d67d6ae3fefc0ae11f57c206f31b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e596f70f1bcab1802ff190bf7807a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13fbd22ccb86e669dc7d330d54f31def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae5a6d220ddce8db9baaa910a116b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9ce8abdb14d484f7e951e27e2fec56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4271bb9cc0287dcb0b401b760eb4864e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a</data>
