      <data key="d5">1768781064</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.630">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.630</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.630 outlines regulations for tree preservation in conjunction with land divisions to promote ecological benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.630 provides regulations for tree preservation with specific density standards and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.630 pertains to tree preservation regulations that must be complied with for land division approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.630 outlines the regulations for tree preservation related to land divisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1918e6e2060f112e9e0fc6b76a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8537f80e77714b5b0188914023a593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f464bb6caf4196f9f098e5debb9f7fc4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781064</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mechanical Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Mechanical Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mechanical Equipment encompasses a variety of devices and systems critical for building operations, including heating and cooling systems, air conditioners, and generators. These installations often require specific screening standards to minimize visual and noise impacts, particularly in residential and commercial/mixed-use developments. 

In residential zones, mechanical equipment must be screened from view to comply with zoning regulations, which aim to enhance aesthetic appeal and reduce disturbances. This entails placing heating and cooling units in ways that are not visible from the street and ensuring they adhere to specified screening criteria. 

Moreover, Mechanical Equipment must meet certain dimensional criteria concerning placement on properties, reflecting regulations intended to govern the compatibility of these systems with their surroundings. This includes considerations for housing and access related to the devices necessary for efficient building operations. Compliance with these standards is essential to maintain the structural integrity and visual harmony of the surrounding environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e58a4abdc96df0823cedabefcc94943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b2cc8f6a45d17941e977fde3debc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7aa0bae5c7fef30a568af91c0f05e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77775bfe50a48aa700ab96a9ab1c440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f72437166c353de768d234823279f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f45e86d97574f9fac5d7d012bcae97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14a3fd9ec346cf135da2b0299cad1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71ef8e763b48167f014ebc29d2564293</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781064</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Facility or Service">
      <data key="d0">Public Facility or Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
