    <node id="Ord. No. 175965">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 175965</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 175965 is an ordinance that became effective on July 1, 2002. This regulation establishes a series of provisions related to planning and zoning regulations, specifically addressing changes that impact the Columbia South Shore Plan District and the Kenton Plan District. The ordinance also includes amendments to zoning regulations and contributes to design review processes and tree preservation plans.

Additionally, Ord. No. 175965 has been identified as a legislative order that adds provisions to Title 33, further detailing its role in the development regulations that govern these specific districts. The consistent effective date underscores its significance in coordinating and updating local regulations related to urban planning and development.</data>
