    <node id="Medical Centers">
      <data key="d0">Medical Centers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical Centers are healthcare facilities recognized under institutional use categories and are permitted within Single-Dwelling Zones. They serve as vital institutions that provide a range of medical services, contributing to community health and well-being. These centers may develop as institutional campuses in alignment with specific regulations, particularly those governing Institutional and Residential (IR) Zones.

In terms of operational requirements, Medical Centers must comply with defined zoning regulations, which include specific parking requirements. These requirements may vary based on the net building area of the facilities, ensuring that adequate space is available for both staff and visitors. Furthermore, Medical Centers are classified as an active use in zoning regulations, affirming their role in delivering essential health services within the community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33d0f030f285a86371b78f7278eb5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cc02978e3319b39c1038d83f233d71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaed07dc46c4dea3061745b8e0750d03</data>
