    <node id="IG1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">IG1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The IG1 Zone is a designated zoning classification that regulates land use primarily for Retail Sales and Service or Office purposes. This specific zone encompasses various restrictions and guidelines governing property use, particularly regarding allowable building types and areas. 

The IG1 Zone is characterized by its designation for industrial sites, which necessitate compliance with minimum size requirements. Specifically, all parcels within this zoning category must be at least 200,000 square feet in area to qualify for the related regulations outlined in Chapter 33.664. Moreover, the IG1 Zone mandates adherence to minimum lot dimension standards, which are classified under Standard B.

In addition to these regulations, the IG1 Zone permits surface parking, contingent upon specific conditions relating to industrial activities. It is situated within the Lower Albina Subdistrict, suggesting that it is intended for both industrial and mixed-use developments. Overall, the IG1 Zone serves as a critical framework for managing land use and development in designated areas, ensuring that both commercial and industrial activities are appropriately accommodated while adhering to established standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bcdb0ed86328221b3f3b4bc1f84ed339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b54ec38d3cb1a3d30f391fc1b147316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157f892dc3db1b7d5113b58ec80ccd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4cc500f0cf6ffd63a8f594c9055457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbed3d0d9f1ce8f7b4b9d7df85935cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc62df021ba5cb939053361288e0352a</data>
