    <node id="Setbacks">
      <data key="d0">Setbacks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Setback requirements determine the minimum distance buildings must be from property lines.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks are required distances that structures must maintain from property lines, which apply to various types of detached structures outlined in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks are regulations that dictate the minimum distance structures must be from property lines.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks refer to regulatory requirements concerning the distance structures must be from property boundaries or streets.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks are the required distances that structures must be set back from property lines as defined by zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks are zoning regulations that specify the minimum distance a building must be from property lines.&lt;SEP&gt;Setbacks are minimum distances that helicopter landing facilities must maintain from residential zones to mitigate potential impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e452b9ec8a9af12b429462d8859d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21fff4b96769197d29b5065fb50894e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5555f01efc47b9ad220ce985153f9292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf1cc9b5437586cfb484233e2286c341</data>
