    <node id="Nonconforming Residential Density">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Residential Density</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming residential density refers to the rights related to residential density that may be maintained or lost based on damage and repairs to structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Residential Density is a lawful residential use that exceeds allowed density due to zoning changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 176333">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 176333</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 176333 is an ordinance that became effective on July 1, 2002. This ordinance includes various amendments specifically related to zoning regulations and planning within the jurisdiction it governs. It notably amended Title 33 and contributed to the development regulations associated with the Columbia South Shore Plan District. Furthermore, it is relevant to the Kenton Plan District regulations, highlighting its significance in urban planning.

In addition to its regulatory aspects, Ord. No. 176333 includes provisions related to tree preservation and influences design review regulations as part of its broader impact on planning and zoning. There are mentions of further amendments that extended certain regulations effective August 30, 2003. 

Overall, Ord. No. 176333 serves as a significant legal framework intended to govern and guide development practices and urban planning policies within the specified districts, reflecting a comprehensive approach to managing zoning and related regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bcdb0ed86328221b3f3b4bc1f84ed339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2e828d0ef40701ea87d62c0b01bd2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8537f80e77714b5b0188914023a593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c26e370406e01072c5a2f986aca90fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd51482e13f3b991071675a0ea850c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f9cce1f67d8125895ea396b1acc241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bce80dce3f6e46fbf15b845bbded504</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lots of Record">
      <data key="d0">Lots of Record</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lots of record are parcels of land that are recognized and documented within legal frameworks for development purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lots of record are legally recognized parcels of land that existed before current zoning regulations and may have nonconforming status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd85ebb9182c99ebc70e5ecbfe9d7ae0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Colleges">
      <data key="d0">Colleges</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Colleges refer to a category of post-secondary educational institutions that are primarily focused on providing degree programs and specialized studies. They are recognized as institutional entities that facilitate higher education by offering a variety of academic programs aligned with education policies.

In terms of zoning and land use, colleges have specific regulations that allow them to operate in certain areas, including Single-Dwelling Zones, where they can utilize spaces for educational purposes. Additionally, they are permitted to develop as institutional campuses within designated Institutional Reserve (IR) Zones, ensuring compliance with local development regulations.

Colleges are also associated with outdoor sports facilities, which are included in the permitted uses under certain zoning regulations. Furthermore, there are explicit parking requirements for colleges, which take into account the size of their buildings and the presence of dormitory accommodations. This includes specified parking space requirements that correlate with the net building area of college facilities, ensuring adequate infrastructure to support their operational needs.

Overall, colleges are institutions of higher learning that occupy a crucial role in the educational landscape, governed by specific guidelines that influence their establishment, use of space, and operational logistics in various residential and commercial zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34de9e34b3c0011d322a8520a1091e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaed07dc46c4dea3061745b8e0750d03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e2adfc473177ee34daf0edf44e9fab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Preliminary Plan">
      <data key="d0">Preliminary Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Preliminary Plan is a critical proposal that serves as the initial outline and design for land division. This document is essential for the land division process, as it sets the basic layout while ensuring compliance with certain standards and criteria necessary for future development. The Preliminary Plan must go through a review and approval process, requiring adherence to specific regulations, including zoning laws.

This plan includes detailed proposals for land divisions, providing legal descriptions and site layouts integral to the development process. Its primary purpose is to present a comprehensive outline of intended developments, thereby facilitating the necessary evaluations for land use approvals. It is also noted that the Preliminary Plan is a foundational document that does not expire unless particular conditions are met, emphasizing its importance in the approval chain.

Before advancing to the Final Plat approval process, the Preliminary Plan must be affirmed, reflecting the proposed land divisions and compliance with all pertinent regulations. As such, it plays a crucial role not only in initiating the land division requests but also in shaping the regulatory landscape that guides future development activities. Overall, the Preliminary Plan is an indispensable component of land management, ensuring organized and regulated growth in accordance with established planning frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bcdb0ed86328221b3f3b4bc1f84ed339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d7961ce66e26136990bb4bb54c838e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0017e9ee882283347e4f97cb10636de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c866b4b0736bc538364f76d18bd9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2bdb61444de27eb1c904251335348f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f464bb6caf4196f9f098e5debb9f7fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32beb3a9e96c3d41cc526d4dbd0b1f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41abaceb8097519bba26a5ccb4274c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594964a698a9063f34a66127a99f84d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2546da1b6188ab781e1777780334eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87b7eb1267fcd08cc2e4395c933546a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot Remnants">
      <data key="d0">Lot Remnants</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot remnants are portions of lots that remain after a portion has been removed or developed, subject to specific regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot remnants refer to portions of land that remain after the creation of new lots and are subject to specific development regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot remnants are small pieces of land left over after a larger parcel has been split or developed, often facing specific zoning challenges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd85ebb9182c99ebc70e5ecbfe9d7ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Willamette Greenway Design Guidelines">
      <data key="d0">Willamette Greenway Design Guidelines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Willamette Greenway Design Guidelines provide standards for development along the Willamette River to protect its ecological and aesthetic qualities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Willamette Greenway Design Guidelines provide standards that must be met for all greenway review applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11138328735cf87d245bb64f2a57f4d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Type Ix Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Type Ix Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Type Ix Procedure is a multifaceted regulatory and administrative process that primarily addresses specific land use reviews, particularly those involving land divisions that do not fit into the more established Type IIx or Type III categories. It serves as an alternative review option for certain development applications, notably those related to affordable housing.

The Type Ix Procedure encompasses the handling of various enhancements, including public recreational trails and interpretative facilities. It specifically includes a review process for replat applications, allowing local jurisdictions to evaluate requests in a structured manner. Additionally, the procedure facilitates the assessment of Final Plats, ensuring that they meet regulatory standards before approval.

Administratively, the Type Ix Procedure is designed to streamline processes by allowing for public notice without necessitating a hearing, thus expediting decision-making for less complex land use cases. It allows for local decisions on limited design reviews and reviews concerning historic resources. Moreover, it includes provisions for requests related to Preservation Parking, defined under specific circumstances.

Overall, the Type Ix Procedure serves as a crucial instrument in land management, providing a framework for efficient handling of select applications while maintaining regulatory oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d855fbf99c0d0379fc75e502d7bd623a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c232ce107cc5a0bd00a23892d69d0561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200b9b34fa908e42e599f92db53639cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0352df0641b29208d29e9ef4be447b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f464bb6caf4196f9f098e5debb9f7fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ca5b72e1693d958a1e3c385272e963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f976aff1b8a931aa89584cca89b6bd36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23bdb6b78c43cbe3cee1a2bacbb57a5f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.266">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.266</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.266 is a comprehensive section within the planning and zoning regulations that addresses various standards and requirements related to parking, loading, landscaping, and transportation management for developments, particularly within the Commercial Employment (CE) zone. This chapter outlines specific regulations concerning the provision of vehicle and bicycle parking, loading areas, and transportation demand management.

The regulations specified in Chapter 33.266 encompass requirements for landscaping and screening within parking areas and loading zones, ensuring that such developments meet aesthetic and environmental standards. Furthermore, the chapter delineates the regulatory framework for transportation management, emphasizing the need for effective planning in parking and loading to cater to both residential structures—such as houses, duplexes, triplexes, and fourplexes—as well as commercial properties.

Additionally, Chapter 33.266 incorporates stipulations for transportation management practices that are critical to urban planning, including specific guidelines for bicycle parking and other transportation modalities. Overall, this chapter aims to create a balanced and orderly development approach that adheres to established zoning standards while addressing the functional needs of various properties within affected zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8966d01e665f9cb17191db9bb5912d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c04f82ed495a847d38cb7549bbc8ce4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fdd35be330bba709b87457f05729af8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b2323b48f41f87137658c4c38c98ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145c2e6cf2a3147235dc3027efb2fd6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc01e5a62a9dbd8bf10a560a6ed844cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72db2074515977339664a4c6fb188af1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b31593c6056a4c4b7b5e1b873010f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deccf49edc8456f9e632a30209a8e62a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e75a7e001ab5c6a45155cc2595b9e77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfa9c8fb1cdec53d0022f9be528e80a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78b8d8f5df1d607fc21562bc53c145e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79270fc3c081d0e0b0a71f05624d0eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c95bddb922c68491a627c84908a1149&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-250f22c8b2433134e7522ccaf4bb55d8</data>
