    <node id="Chapter 33.700">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.700</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.700 outlines the administration and enforcement processes related to land use actions within the Title 33 framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.700 is a section of the planning and zoning regulations that outlines the administration and enforcement of land use approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.700 outlines the regulations for Planning and Zoning Administration and Enforcement including conditional uses and land divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.700 outlines the review criteria and procedures for processing Comprehensive Plan Map amendments, including distinctions between quasi-judicial and legislative processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47812462d7ccc96ffd0025a366f98586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cebb99c668ae3666c0d99752b2945f3c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transportation Demand Management Plan">
      <data key="d0">Transportation Demand Management Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transportation Demand Management Plan is a strategy aimed at reducing transportation-related impacts on land use developments.&lt;SEP&gt;A Transportation Demand Management Plan is a strategy aimed at reducing vehicle trips and improving transportation systems, particularly in sites with a College or Medical Center.&lt;SEP&gt;Transportation Demand Management Plan outlines strategies to manage transportation and parking demands related to proposed developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbee049dd9c661ea5a90ad39db328689</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="College">
      <data key="d0">College</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A College is an educational institution that may exist within designated land use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Colleges are educational institutions that must conduct at least one community meeting per year to inform the community regarding future development and changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A College is an educational institution that offers higher education degrees and is recognized as a primary use in specific campus zones.&lt;SEP&gt;College is a category of land use that does not fall under the regulations specified in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A College is an educational institution that may influence regulations concerning conditional uses and land developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fe28a6c33ecbcbe2396156e4ee10e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1548cc5d56ac0b8d2ab93d83d89c89</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Center">
      <data key="d0">Medical Center</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Medical Center provides health services and may be subject to land use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical Centers are healthcare facilities required to hold annual community meetings to discuss potential impacts and updates on their operations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Medical Center is a type of facility that provides healthcare services, included as a use category in the Campus Institutional Zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical Center represents a type of land use that is excluded from the application of certain regulations discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical Centers are eligible to apply for Preservation Parking under certain conditions outlined in the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Medical Center is a healthcare facility that can affect land use regulations regarding conditional uses in its vicinity.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical center offers medical and surgical care to patients, including overnight care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fe28a6c33ecbcbe2396156e4ee10e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1548cc5d56ac0b8d2ab93d83d89c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-701c3f15dff43f3530bb018f9bae2909</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tree Preservation Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Tree Preservation Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tree Preservation Requirements are guidelines intended to protect trees during land use reviews or developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd54e5b638113595ce88bbc6ccf94bc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="City Limits">
      <data key="d0">City Limits</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">City Limits delineate the geographical boundaries of a municipality.&lt;SEP&gt;City Limits denotes the geographic boundaries within which specific land use regulations apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356d9265a5791545fa23fa54dee260f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
