    <node id="Public Safety Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Public Safety Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Public safety facilities are structures that are exempt from height limitations under zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Public safety facilities are structures that are exempt from height limitations set for detached uncovered vertical structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Safety Facilities refer to structures or improvements intended to enhance safety within the urban environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Safety Facilities are developments that must minimize impacts on water quality resource areas and follow specific guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Safety Facilities are locations identified as necessary for public health and safety, subject to approval criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Public safety facilities are establishments responsible for ensuring public safety, including police and fire stations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2e452b9ec8a9af12b429462d8859d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f013869c1ec32a0acb630a40f63c4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad1968bb57e3baa2ecd3350abe6caf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fec75523a13dc705f1116777ea0ce94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-632a46b796dd8e7e5beca816ac0c1138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
