      <data key="d0">Middle Housing Land Division</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Middle Housing Land Division refers to a regulatory framework for dividing land to create housing units, such as fourplexes, while prohibiting certain dwelling types.&lt;SEP&gt;Middle Housing Land Division refers to a specific type of land division application process governed by Title 33.&lt;SEP&gt;Middle Housing Land Division is a process for dividing land to allow for the construction of multiple dwelling units on a single site.&lt;SEP&gt;Middle Housing Land Division refers to a specific type of land division governed by regulations under ORS 92.031.</data>
