      <data key="d0">Figures 258-2</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Figures 258-2 shows the area of possible expansion in C, E, and I zones for nonconforming uses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781072</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="E Zone">
      <data key="d0">E Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The E zone represents an area with designated standards for commercial or mixed-use buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;The E Zone is a zoning classification that pertains to specific development standards for residential and other structures.&lt;SEP&gt;The E Zone is a zoning classification that regulates development based on established community standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The E zone signifies an employment zone where specific nonconforming use standards apply.&lt;SEP&gt;The E Zone refers to an area where specific zoning rules apply, potentially affecting development rights.&lt;SEP&gt;The E Zone is a designated area referenced for specific regulations related to wind turbine installations.&lt;SEP&gt;The E zone indicates Employment zones designed to support job-related activities and businesses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-221d1ae9cf50b3236ae14ae949934120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5814020534bf1fbc0a6e4c64746ca31d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b58865c473bfa9835169ceac4d038b1d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781072</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nonconforming Use">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming use refers to a type of property use that does not comply with current zoning regulations but continues to exist under specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming use describes a property use that does not conform to current zoning regulations due to changes in the law or other factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Use refers to a use of land that does not conform to the zoning regulations of the area.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Use describes a land use that does not comply with current zoning regulations but existed before those regulations were implemented.&lt;SEP&gt;A Nonconforming Use is a type of property use that does not comply with the current zoning regulations, which may be impacted by Property Line Adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Use pertains to uses that were once allowed but now violate current zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781072</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nonconforming Situation Review">
      <data key="d0">Nonconforming Situation Review</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonconforming Situation Review is a process through which changes and expansions of nonconforming uses are evaluated and approved by governing bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The nonconforming situation review is a procedural method to evaluate and potentially approve expansions of nonconforming uses.&lt;SEP&gt;Nonconforming Situation Review is a Type II procedure for assessing compliance with approval criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e13bc554ddbf7ad8cfa41b1e6d467181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781072</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conditional Use">
      <data key="d0">Conditional Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Conditional Use denotes a zoning classification that allows specific types of land use which are not normally permitted within a defined zoning district, provided they meet certain conditions established by zoning regulations. It involves a special permission process that often requires additional scrutiny or approval from local authorities to ensure compliance with zoning laws. 

The Conditional Use permits are allocated to various categories of land uses, such as educational institutions, mass shelters, and other specific uses that may necessitate alterations in parking requirements or other standard zoning stipulations. The conditions under which these uses are allowed can vary, depending on the type of use, the time of use, and any changes in regulations that may take effect. 

This zoning term encompasses the permissions granted to uses that may not align with existing zoning rules, indicating the need for special considerations and a review process to assess the implications of such uses within the community. Conditional Use thus serves as a vital mechanism by which local governments can manage land use flexibly while ensuring that community standards and regional planning goals are upheld.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afe903e400770e09111a01b6ada75d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b2323b48f41f87137658c4c38c98ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e13bc554ddbf7ad8cfa41b1e6d467181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30acaad3495315145b81fed5d7cb9158&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157f892dc3db1b7d5113b58ec80ccd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d1801c38b4789f81c89f16cc033283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa7a4d254279e02d605594ebe069be0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1548cc5d56ac0b8d2ab93d83d89c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781072</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Three Continuous Years">
      <data key="d0">Three Continuous Years</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The requirement stating that nonconforming use rights are lost if the use is discontinued for three continuous years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781073</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="75 Percent of Assessed Value">
      <data key="d0">75 Percent of Assessed Value</data>
