    <node id="Type II Review">
      <data key="d0">Type II Review</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Type II Review refers to a regulatory process designed for evaluating specific alterations proposed to a site. This review is characterized by its requirements for addressing particular conditions and limitations, particularly when correcting environmental code violations. Unlike a Type III Review, a Type II Review does not demand the same level of scrutiny and is applicable to instances that involve minor changes and less significant implications.

Within the context of environmental assessments, the Type II Review process is mandated for correcting violations of regulations in Pleasant Valley resource reviews. It primarily focuses on adjustments that do not significantly involve large water bodies, thereby streamlining the review process for minor changes. It also serves as a procedural requirement for changes of occupancy and conditional uses in designated zoning areas.

This review captures proposals that do not qualify for a Type I Review and includes non-exempt proposals, thereby ensuring that various minor adjustments to urban plans, such as those in the Central City Master Plan, can be reviewed without the rigorous procedures required for more extensive changes. Type II Review is critical for maintaining compliance with local regulations while facilitating necessary developments across specified areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65c927885cd8918e2dccfdeeb204f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8f7b7f798d73271c022ea233a96a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1347219a19de2480f10b4ab0d1cc91d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-185d37e595bd772f81423b42b3193eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e1d49f86df4a02f01af7661478e4005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dfa716b92fafe3e0c5a60967fdfe220</data>
