    <node id="Site Plan">
      <data key="d0">Site Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Site Plan is a comprehensive document that serves as a detailed drawing illustrating the arrangement of structures, landscaping, and other elements in relation to land use. It plays a crucial role during the application process for building or development permits, ensuring that proposed developments are accurately documented and adhere to relevant regulations.

In particular, the Site Plan is essential for confirming that the proposed development conforms to applicable development standards necessary for obtaining building permits. This document not only showcases the layout and dimensions of both existing and proposed structures but also includes details regarding the infrastructure and circulation systems within the property. Furthermore, it acts as a mapped representation of the building layout and associated ground disturbance activities on the development site.

The Site Plan is particularly important within designated planning areas, such as the Central City Master Plan area, where it outlines the proposed development's layout, including specific measurements and placement on the property. Overall, the Site Plan provides a vital framework for visualizing the development's impact and compliance with planning guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1b829449e430ca472af4da987d81a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cd2a226a2530256c685d499d90fe0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df192280c989d3e1d2bc59bf520124ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f5ada1bd73ae6d3ab8a5bb43ff6e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73cef7ee88bf3469ada732d2e4209747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92124b64bdb5812f3a81c72fd6334a86</data>
