    <node id="Ord. No. 174263">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 174263</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 174263 is a legislative ordinance that became effective on April 15, 2000. The ordinance amends various regulations, particularly concerning zoning and planning. It specifically impacts drive-through facilities and incorporates changes within the Title 33 framework, which deals with land use regulations.

In addition to addressing drive-through facilities, Ord. No. 174263 also pertains to regulations associated with the Columbia South Shore Plan District and the Central City Plan District, as well as the South Auditorium Plan District. It plays a significant role in the development regulations and land use review framework, indicating its broad implications on urban planning in the affected areas.

Overall, Ord. No. 174263 represents a comprehensive legislative attempt to adjust and enhance zoning and development standards effective from April 15, 2000, with specific relevance to various planning districts and regulatory frameworks in the jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d26bbdcc0a02b98a788e69d178237a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d39d3e5dc5ac990b049b748fa4e96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19a2393681785537b2d0f83af94a363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d771f61eac49b01fc5796204c75025ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2e828d0ef40701ea87d62c0b01bd2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7f584fe857b5fce6394c52a4277eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c26e370406e01072c5a2f986aca90fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-616a6925a0ab31d5e3e594ef74a2e21d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd51482e13f3b991071675a0ea850c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52cd6f75c0ef15f81f473a7fd946bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f9cce1f67d8125895ea396b1acc241</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Business Association">
      <data key="d0">Business Association</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Business associations are entities that represent local businesses and also receive notifications regarding meetings held by colleges and medical centers.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Associations represent local businesses and must also be notified regarding proposed developments in their area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Business Association represents local businesses and may be involved in the land use review process.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Association is a local group that receives meeting notes prior to land use reviews or building permit applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Association is an organization that represents the interests of business owners in a community and may engage in neighborhood contact processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3ac296609c32cc7de194b33256a6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1b829449e430ca472af4da987d81a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7e7d1e624354524b6833b6427f9866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fe28a6c33ecbcbe2396156e4ee10e6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="School District">
      <data key="d0">School District</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The School District is responsible for educational services in the area and may be consulted during land use reviews.&lt;SEP&gt;School District is a local education organization that receives meeting notes prior to land use reviews or building permit applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7e7d1e624354524b6833b6427f9866</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Waste Related Uses">
      <data key="d0">Waste Related Uses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Waste Related Uses refer to categories of uses that involve the disposal or utilization of energy-generating processes not categorized as Small Scale Energy Production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Railroad Yards">
      <data key="d0">Railroad Yards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Railroad Yards are listed under industrial primary uses in Single-Dwelling Zones, typically marked as a prohibited use.&lt;SEP&gt;Railroad Yards are locations where trains are assembled, loaded, unloaded, and serviced.&lt;SEP&gt;Railroad Yards are designated areas containing multiple tracks for switching, assembling trains, and transshipment of goods.&lt;SEP&gt;Railroad Yards are areas containing multiple railroad tracks used for rail car switching, assembling of trains, and transshipment of goods.&lt;SEP&gt;Railroad Yards are industrial facilities used for managing railroad operations and logistics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Warehouse And Freight Movement">
      <data key="d0">Warehouse And Freight Movement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Warehouse And Freight Movement includes operations related to the storage and transportation of goods.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse And Freight Movement involves the storage and transport of goods and materials as part of industrial operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse And Freight Movement firms focus on the storage and movement of goods on behalf of themselves or other businesses.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse And Freight Movement category includes businesses that deal primarily with the transfer and storage of goods without individual storage areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse And Freight Movement involves firms that store or move goods for themselves or others with limited customer presence during delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse and freight movement refers to services related to the storage and transportation of goods.&lt;SEP&gt;Warehouse And Freight Movement refers to facilities that handle storage and transportation of goods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f6c68627201b6a0d63e0a73012b8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b01451771b358c77494f198e0c0a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Waste-Related Uses">
      <data key="d0">Waste-Related Uses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Waste-Related Uses refer to land uses associated with managing waste and are subject to specific regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste-Related Uses are defined as activities that manage solid or liquid wastes, including collection, disposal, or production of goods from organic materials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31a92cc8ee690c44538d0568e543e8a7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Scale Energy Production">
      <data key="d0">Small Scale Energy Production</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small Scale Energy Production refers to localized energy generation, which may be considered an accessory use.&lt;SEP&gt;Small Scale Energy Production pertains to the generation of energy that operates under defined limits that distinguish it from utility scale energy production.&lt;SEP&gt;Small scale energy production refers to energy generated through various means like solar, small wind turbines, and hydroelectric systems producing up to 100 kW.&lt;SEP&gt;Small Scale Energy Production refers to energy-generating processes that do not meet certain definitions set by regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Small Scale Energy Production refers to the generation of energy on a smaller scale, often using renewable sources, typically for local use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7a46ce2a41072cf8f503e930128f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad3df252c10f7d3d9869375a3dd70b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wholesale Sales">
      <data key="d0">Wholesale Sales</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Wholesale Sales refer to the sale of goods in large quantities to be resold by retailers.&lt;SEP&gt;Wholesale Sales is a sector that involves selling goods in large quantities for resale.&lt;SEP&gt;Wholesale Sales is recognized as an active use that can occupy ground floor spaces within specified zoning classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Wholesale Sales refer to businesses involved in the sale, lease, or rent of products intended for industrial or commercial entities.&lt;SEP&gt;Wholesale sales refer to the sale of goods in large quantities to retailers, industrial, commercial, institutional, or other business users.&lt;SEP&gt;Wholesale Sales pertains to businesses that sell goods in bulk to retailers or other businesses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8720ae6e86b5d5b7120bdfbb3c9a2cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 177422">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 177422</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 177422 is an ordinance that became effective on June 7, 2003. This ordinance is associated with various amendments and regulations impacting multiple plan districts, particularly the Columbia South Shore Plan District and the Central City Plan District. 

The ordinance has been recognized as a legislative measure amending Title 33 and involves regulations concerned with residential structure types. It serves as a key regulatory framework within municipal guidelines and development regulations, reflecting updates in planning and zoning laws effective from the stated date. 

Overall, Ord. No. 177422 encapsulates a variety of modifications aimed at enhancing the regulatory landscape within specific urban areas, ensuring compliance with updated development standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d39d3e5dc5ac990b049b748fa4e96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fee202a5a178704f7fab97145229db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f525a8329ffe0f200c2898df08550d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6aad1106b110b0d7d16c1115383897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f9cce1f67d8125895ea396b1acc241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bce80dce3f6e46fbf15b845bbded504</data>
