      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Review">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Review</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Environmental Review is a critical evaluative process mandated for proposals that fail to meet established development standards within Environmental Zones. Its primary aim is to evaluate potential environmental impacts, thereby ensuring that any proposed actions align with environmental regulations and standards. 

This process serves multiple purposes, including the prevention of harm to natural resources, the success of mitigation strategies, and the potential modification of development standards based on thorough assessment outcomes. As a comprehensive evaluation, it requires adherence to specific approval criteria and procedures that assess compliance with environmental standards.

Environmental Review also specifically addresses the impacts of proposed developments on various natural resources, ensuring concerns related to wildlife hazards are adequately considered, particularly in contexts involving airport regulations. Moreover, it pertains to land proposals that must satisfy specific environmental regulations, such as those delineated in Chapter 33.630.

Overall, Environmental Review is an essential mechanism for assessing the environmental impacts of proposed developments, ensuring that they meet established criteria and comply with overarching environmental impact guidelines established under relevant resource plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1918e6e2060f112e9e0fc6b76a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a90d16f519debce0d1b06def34f6932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285f052019746f5b49b63ae041c898aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8f7b7f798d73271c022ea233a96a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490cb02a9aa37ab5ed0231106009cb20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9baf563ec9df2a33ac29db9f4fc53fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a4fda2a7ebb04a6a59cff745526b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1226a7075ba7d150a3b769bb492b29a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a187157e908115a4998c100f65fb8a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
