    </node>
    <node id="Two-Way Antenna">
      <data key="d0">Two-Way Antenna</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Two-Way Antenna is a type of antenna required for towers, specified to be provided for every certain height of the structure in the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e0d3aa49a8c3edf6ae58238049a8d3b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781074</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Greenway Goal Exception">
      <data key="d0">Greenway Goal Exception</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Greenway Goal Exception allows certain developments located within the greenway setback that are not river-dependent or river-related to bypass standard review processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Goal Exception is a regulatory provision that allows for specific development activities around greenway zones.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Goal Exception is a provision allowing certain developments outside of normal regulations if approved.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Goal Exception allows certain developments near the Willamette River to bypass typical planning goals under specific criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Goal Exception allows development not dependent on rivers within specified setback areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6638b6f4daad5d15b558bf7e5689cbbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e88e3e2ec290b90a147566b3c2e07270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165b18aa9a1d81892edc1c295c96b243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fce67d5a707ef7b953fc44e3ab5449b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Greenway Setback">
      <data key="d0">Greenway Setback</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Greenway Setback refers to the required buffer area from the riverbank for development activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Setback is a designated area along a river where certain development activities are subject to review and regulations to protect the river environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Setback is a designated area near the riverbank which has specific regulations regarding development to protect wildlife habitat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greenway Setback is a buffer zone along riverbanks where development is restricted to protect habitats and water quality resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Greenway Setback refers to the requirement for landscaping between developed property and the riverbank to enhance environmental aesthetics and access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad1968bb57e3baa2ecd3350abe6caf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ec46b8cc5650199d033fa9573b44034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0271e8b27cedc9b0b135f529688a98</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planning and Zoning Title 33">
      <data key="d0">Planning and Zoning Title 33</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 33 is a regulatory framework that encompasses various planning and zoning laws, including those related to greenway management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Section 33.440.320">
      <data key="d0">Section 33.440.320</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.440.320 outlines specific exemptions applicable to certain developments and alterations in relation to the Greenway regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Figure 440-3">
      <data key="d0">Figure 440-3</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Figure 440-3 illustrates the Greenway Goal Exception in the River Water Quality Zone, serving as a visual aid for understanding regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c968440bc0fba466f64f33dd21b85e63</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Type III Review">
      <data key="d0">Type III Review</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Type III Review is a comprehensive assessment process that applies to various development alterations on a site, particularly those not covered by other review categories. It serves as a regulatory mechanism for specific proposals related to new recreational fields and modifications to existing ones, ensuring that these changes meet community and environmental standards.

This review is designated for situations that require a more stringent scrutiny for environmental compliance. It is mandated for activities such as tree removal that exceeds certain thresholds and development actions within sensitive ecological zones, including wetlands, stream channels, and other water bodies. The Type III Review thus plays a critical role in safeguarding environmental integrity while allowing for necessary development.

In addition to environmental considerations, the Type III Review is also essential for evaluating significant changes to planning instruments, such as amendments to the Central City Master Plan. This ensures thorough examination and community input on proposed alterations to important civic frameworks.

The review process encompasses broader impacts of proposals situated within institutional contexts, particularly for substantial projects or alterations that involve complex developments, such as multi-dwelling structures. In summary, the Type III Review is a vital procedure to ensure that various developments undergo a detailed evaluation in order to balance growth with environmental sustainability and community welfare.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65c927885cd8918e2dccfdeeb204f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555b254650c4e6bcde7e85291a2480b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8f7b7f798d73271c022ea233a96a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1347219a19de2480f10b4ab0d1cc91d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4670488f256f231024de0291feeec277&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-185d37e595bd772f81423b42b3193eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80424e1fdfc525e03fb931cf5e6d14ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e1d49f86df4a02f01af7661478e4005</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
