    <node id="Development Standards">
      <data key="d0">Development Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Development Standards refer to the comprehensive set of guidelines and regulations that govern building practices and land use, particularly in residential zones. These standards serve to ensure that construction projects adhere to specific characteristics and requirements, which include but are not limited to lot size, floor area ratios (FAR), building setbacks, and overall building coverage within various zoning codes.

These regulations are crucial for maintaining compliance with zoning laws and for the approval of building and development permits. Development Standards detail the criteria that proposals must satisfy to ensure compatibility with surrounding uses, thereby promoting a harmonious integration of structures within their environments. This includes regulations that manage the visual impact of developments, such as Radio Frequency Transmission Facilities, and requirements for recreational fields and their accessory structures.

Furthermore, Development Standards encompass guidelines that enhance urban design and pedestrian-friendly environments, fostering mixed-use developments and maintaining the aesthetic appeal of neighborhoods. They also play a role in environmental protection, ensuring that development activities do not compromise natural resources, such as those found in the Pleasant Valley area.

These standards are not static; they evolve through master planning efforts that propose specific criteria, such as height limits, landscaping needs, and parking requirements, which aim to control future land uses and ensure coherent urban development. Overall, Development Standards are integral to guiding how land is developed and modified, ensuring that all projects conform to local regulations and are aligned with community goals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d220a61d92d1c965d2882acdcd160d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155b41dabaadf0c9869e8d0f00d94360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-182c8d04df8eca72ac077fcd7a5564f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdee8c33d0d52a7455e70087137ca492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90974c5207e30c3839f91710f5169ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0271e8b27cedc9b0b135f529688a98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555b254650c4e6bcde7e85291a2480b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52cbe23eb8de6a4318808cef3ac4f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-546f125167252089bdfedd0eae022ba2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2eeace7e4e8bfbd79b4cab85b0af9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f5238f416f69c282caa09bc226ffbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ace73fe9057e3e9a8fa2fac920590272&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30acaad3495315145b81fed5d7cb9158&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78755af7dcf0cbd31bb8a59f246d601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd9adaf9df20165e7a81ed8dcfe84163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133e0d785413e64759688100094b7c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cad83ae88a9187d47c9acf881162cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5eb17d84fb94bd8bf31df2d43873e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2001ba277158737c9b888248e680d7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e28ba6f352cf461311b1a12b892a5ff</data>
