    <node id="Affordable Housing">
      <data key="d0">Affordable Housing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Affordable Housing refers to residential buildings designed to be accessible to individuals with low to moderate incomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Affordable housing refers to housing units that are affordable to individuals or families with low to moderate incomes, as required by certain development bonuses.&lt;SEP&gt;Affordable Housing refers to residential units that meet specified criteria, allowing for exemptions in development regulations under certain programs, such as the Title 30 System Development Charges Exemption Program.&lt;SEP&gt;Affordable Housing pertains to housing development initiatives aimed at providing economically accessible housing options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f57fb6953e9769254bb5d2a323550c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ffc992b5e373540a3ee78f16308e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14dcd96a6f149344a7f8451f7533b386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80424e1fdfc525e03fb931cf5e6d14ed</data>
