    <node id="Accessory Dwelling Unit">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Dwelling Unit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessory dwelling units are secondary housing units that provide flexible living space on residential properties and have specific development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;An accessory dwelling unit is a secondary living space on a property, allowed under specific zoning conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;An accessory dwelling unit is a secondary housing unit on a single-family property, which can be added under specific zoning provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;An Accessory Dwelling Unit is a secondary housing structure that can be added to a primary residence in specified zoning areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Unit refers to a secondary housing unit located on the same property as a single-family home, often regulated under zoning laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Dwelling Unit refers to a residential structure type associated with larger primary residences.&lt;SEP&gt;An Accessory Dwelling Unit is a smaller dwelling unit created on a lot with a primary dwelling, designed for independent living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f3d3dc1f275b21f3a0c1622695839a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7777fdca5bcbd3670723d206cd8f5757&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924adce58a3a3a8622d21ee99005b5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fee5077b9b5bae2a7dec413478071a4</data>
