    <node id="Option Two">
      <data key="d0">Option Two</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Option Two is an alternative method for correcting environmental violations under specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Two is an alternative method for correcting violations if specific conditions regarding tree removal are met.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Two refers to a process of legalizing illegal development while mitigating any environmental damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Two is an alternative method for correcting environmental violations that cannot meet the criteria for Option One.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Two refers to the second process for handling violations, which allows legalizing illegal developments and mitigating damage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-370bd3a55fe045150292fe6445463a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-088fe9a8bf4c7d50c85bec432d0ca5c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a5816615430d9b588c4adaf4aa3131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b95c123bc42f5e9142018f60381ac37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c77c0e594bc319fd143848146f9ea56</data>
