    <node id="Option Three">
      <data key="d0">Option Three</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Option Three is a method that must be used if the applicant cannot meet the requirements of Options One or Two.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Three is the required method for correcting violations when Options One or Two cannot be met.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Three requires a Pleasant Valley resource review based on specified approval criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Option Three is the final method available for correcting violations when neither Option One nor Option Two can be used.</data>
