    <node id="Building Coverage">
      <data key="d0">Building Coverage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Building Coverage refers to the proportion of a land lot that can be occupied by buildings and structures. It is defined as the percentage of the total area of a site that can be utilized for construction, which is subject to specific regulations dictated by zoning laws. These regulations often establish limits not only for the primary structures but also for accessory structures, ensuring that there is an appropriate balance between built and open spaces.

The concept of Building Coverage plays a significant role in zoning compliance, impacting the allowable density of development on a property. This factor is crucial for urban planning, as it influences the amount of open space available on a site. Additionally, specific requirements may apply to different types of developments, such as cottage clusters, and to arrangements like shared courts and common greens, where functional and aesthetic considerations become vital.

In summary, Building Coverage is a critical measurement in real estate and urban development that dictates how much of a property can be constructed upon, thereby affecting the overall density and livability of the area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40b451e83bd236d5610bd2be4f5e2e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85949d3f78909228a152d02b0d54f684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a48525044c3c1bf75799ef0954937b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c858bb23efe67cb70612c0464f3e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2574af8787db7883bc15da7cbabd3a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781077</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
