    <node id="Temporary Erosion Control Measures">
      <data key="d0">Temporary Erosion Control Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Temporary erosion control measures are short-term strategies employed to protect against erosion until permanent solutions are implemented.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary erosion control measures are implemented to stabilize soil and prevent erosion during construction or land disturbance activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary Erosion Control Measures are practices implemented to prevent soil erosion during construction or until vegetation is established.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5ea5fe5eea40eab34623aa7e60f482&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planting Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Planting Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Planting requirements detail specifications for planting trees, shrubs, and groundcovers, including size and species diversity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Archaeological Resources">
      <data key="d0">Archaeological Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Archaeological resources refer to historical remnants and artifacts significant to understanding early human activity, especially related to Native American tribes.&lt;SEP&gt;Archaeological resources refer to historical and cultural artifacts and sites, particularly associated with American Indians, and are protected under zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Archaeological resources are significant historical artifacts that must be protected during development projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4395c057e21d1b49701c5d6e444bef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f349daac2faae66ee44d1e97329f22b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972d6f8b824b76de1c4e754f5d9f3110</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Subarea 1">
      <data key="d0">Subarea 1</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Subarea 1 is a zoning area extending from the ordinary high water mark to the top of bank of the Willamette River, with specific landscaping regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Subarea 1 is a designated area within the context of planting regulations that has specific characteristics related to slope and soil requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Subarea 1 refers to a specific section defined in the overall development plan where particular regulations and improvements apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e88e3e2ec290b90a147566b3c2e07270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a2edce75cc1c84e8d78d82be31fd43b</data>
