    <node id="Property Line Adjustment">
      <data key="d0">Property Line Adjustment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Property Line Adjustment describes the process and regulations for relocating common property lines between abutting properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Property Line Adjustment refers to the process of modifying the common property line between two properties, requiring conformance to various regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Property Line Adjustment is a procedural method used for reconfiguring property lines while adhering to specified zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Property Line Adjustment is a process required to relocate a common property line between two properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Property Line Adjustment refers to the process of conveying land from one property to another, which may involve multiple exchange parcels.&lt;SEP&gt;Property Line Adjustment involves relocating a property line between adjacent properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e6483ee1a0cf1415621eb7ccf6224b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1548067bb4833113c6a54b4a7e87fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfe18720ad9b5bf5dadab610a40b064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219169bf18bf9f73b3370be8bd44ed1d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.677">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.677</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.677 specifies the requirements for property line adjustments in land division processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.677 details the regulations for Property Line Adjustments, including purpose, prohibited actions, and application requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.677 outlines regulations and procedures for Property Line Adjustments under Title 33, Planning and Zoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1548067bb4833113c6a54b4a7e87fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0017e9ee882283347e4f97cb10636de7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Common Property Line">
      <data key="d0">Common Property Line</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A common property line refers to the boundary between two adjacent properties that may be adjusted through legal processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Description">
      <data key="d0">Legal Description</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Legal Description involves the formal, accurate description of property boundaries and ownership details necessary for Property Line Adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;The legal description provides detailed information identifying the boundaries and location of the property in question.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0de2e33b17c8bed0fb16624ad72fab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f5ada1bd73ae6d3ab8a5bb43ff6e2b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781078</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R5 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R5 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The R5 Zone is a zoning classification that governs residential development by establishing specific requirements for density and lot size. It mandates a minimum of two dwelling units on sites measuring 10,000 square feet or larger, while also outlining minimum size requirements for adjusted lots and lot remnants, specifying that they must be at least 36 feet wide and 1,600 square feet in area.

Additionally, the R5 Zone requires a minimum lot area of 3,000 square feet for dwellings, which supports a higher density of residential units compared to the R7 Zone. This residential zoning classification includes designated regulations affecting property configurations and development guidelines, thereby influencing property line adjustments for parcels within the zone.

Overall, the R5 Zone serves to regulate residential development effectively, ensuring that projects meet predefined density and area requirements that promote organized growth and optimal land use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e889d237f01a5093e629880a38d5a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e6483ee1a0cf1415621eb7ccf6224b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8e38ccecc8aee043d4f983d468a91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fee5077b9b5bae2a7dec413478071a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
