    <node id="R7 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R7 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The R7 Zone is a residential zoning classification that mandates specific requirements for land use and development focused on housing variety. This zoning designation requires a minimum of two dwelling units on sites that are 14,000 square feet or larger and specifies that individual lot areas must be at least 4,200 square feet for each dwelling. 

The R7 Zone particularly emphasizes standards for residential density, which allows for more units and increased floor area compared to the R10 Zone, facilitating higher density living solutions. This zoning classification is applicable in diverse scenarios, enabling diverse housing types, including cottage clusters and accessory dwelling units, adhering to the stipulated density and site dimension standards.

In summary, the R7 Zone serves as an important regulatory framework governing the development and organization of residential properties, promoting efficient land use while addressing community housing needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a18871dd80f2b9b263d128e9803fd70d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e889d237f01a5093e629880a38d5a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8e38ccecc8aee043d4f983d468a91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fee5077b9b5bae2a7dec413478071a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781079</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
