    <node id="Transportation Impact Analysis (TIA)">
      <data key="d0">Transportation Impact Analysis (TIA)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transportation Impact Analysis (TIA) is a method used to assess the impact of proposed developments on transportation systems, particularly when they exceed allocation limits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4cac4e6c1ba756a5bcff3c73c0fac10d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781079</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Development Capacity">
      <data key="d0">Development Capacity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Development capacity relates to the potential amount of building floor area and usage allowed within specific zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4cac4e6c1ba756a5bcff3c73c0fac10d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781079</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Combined Flood Hazard Area">
      <data key="d0">Combined Flood Hazard Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Combined Flood Hazard Area encompasses designated regions identified as being at risk of flooding. These areas are subject to specific regulations aimed at managing flood risks effectively, ensuring both safety and environmental protection. The regulations governing these zones dictate development standards, stipulating limitations on construction, land use, and vegetation management, including guidelines for tree removal.

In addition to safety regulations during development, the Combined Flood Hazard Area includes rules that aim to protect natural resources and minimize the impact of potential flooding. Proposed building sites within these areas must adhere to strategic placement guidelines intended to mitigate flood risks. Furthermore, these zones may provide exemptions from certain development standards, reflecting an approach that balances development ambitions and environmental safety.

Overall, the designation of the Combined Flood Hazard Area serves as a crucial measure for risk management, delineating specific regions where regulatory frameworks are established to promote safety and sustainability in the face of flooding threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20addac2bd7bf67d0c780bffff45e581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-148b4481af37fbad429e170e0527ee60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bda12d4c6ac60dd023d2422e670f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacf586128716bb40a914b64e071f666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8537f80e77714b5b0188914023a593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f464bb6caf4196f9f098e5debb9f7fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c35c570b66abd053c37dd3812df90d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9ce8abdb14d484f7e951e27e2fec56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11738f034d5f65fb344c5bf37019ca51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1b5dababc725aeec628685254c591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fbbf35a5a5146ae4034375e7576374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2653802c982b64f8a7af01800f4406b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5045146aa70a167fd48292faecd8ea6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68e1edc738fe00a1738dc12a945ce96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781079</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Trip Generation">
      <data key="d0">Trip Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Trip generation is a metric regarding the estimated number of trips produced by developments in relation to their size and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4cac4e6c1ba756a5bcff3c73c0fac10d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
