    <node id="Residential Facility">
      <data key="d0">Residential Facility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Residential Facility is designed to accommodate a small number of disabled persons alongside support staff.&lt;SEP&gt;A Residential Facility is a residence for 6 to 15 physically or mentally disabled persons, may provide care along with training or treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfe18720ad9b5bf5dadab610a40b064</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Residential Home">
      <data key="d0">Residential Home</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Residential Home is a residence for five or fewer physically or mentally disabled persons, offering care and possible training or treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Attached Duplex">
      <data key="d0">Attached Duplex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An Attached Duplex is a type of residential structure consisting of two dwelling units connected by a shared wall.&lt;SEP&gt;An Attached Duplex is a duplex on its own lot that shares walls with other units, with shared walls covering at least 25 percent of the length.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c858bb23efe67cb70612c0464f3e80</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Attached House">
      <data key="d0">Attached House</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An Attached House refers to a residential structure that shares walls with adjacent houses.&lt;SEP&gt;An Attached House is a dwelling unit located on its own lot that shares walls with other units, not sharing common floor/ceilings with them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c858bb23efe67cb70612c0464f3e80</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Congregate Housing Facility">
      <data key="d0">Congregate Housing Facility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A congregate housing facility pertains to a type of residential structure catering to shared living arrangements.&lt;SEP&gt;A Congregate Housing Facility includes separate bedrooms and bathrooms but typically does not have a kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11738f034d5f65fb344c5bf37019ca51</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cottage Cluster">
      <data key="d0">Cottage Cluster</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cottage clusters are residential structures allowed under specific guidelines, focusing on site dimensions, density, and building coverage.&lt;SEP&gt;Cottage Cluster is a housing type that consists of multiple small homes grouped together, allowed under specific conditions in the RM1 zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Cottage clusters refer to a type of housing development that allows multiple manufactured homes to be grouped together within a designated area.&lt;SEP&gt;A Cottage Cluster consists of 3 to 16 individual detached dwelling units located on one lot.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b659477574fcf7f35453f172163de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc6ceed3be738324a1eb3f18282ffbd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="House">
      <data key="d0">House</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A House is a detached dwelling unit located on its own lot, not created through a middle housing land division.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Houseboat Moorage">
      <data key="d0">Houseboat Moorage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Houseboat Moorage is a facility providing moorings for houseboats.&lt;SEP&gt;Houseboat moorage refers to facilities that provide docking and mooring services for houseboats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Application Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Application Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Application Requirements are a comprehensive set of documents and information that must be collected and submitted when applying for various land division and use review processes, specifically concerning manufactured dwelling parks and middle housing land divisions. These requirements specify the necessary materials needed for a complete application, ensuring that applicants are equipped with the correct information to facilitate the review process.

The Application Requirements encompass the materials and information essential for several specific requests, including Lot Confirmation requests and Property Line Adjustments. They serve as a guide for applicants, detailing the complete criteria that must be satisfied as outlined in legal provisions, particularly in Section 33.730.060, which governs land use review applications.

Furthermore, Application Requirements include fees and additional documentation necessary for applications processed under the Type III Procedure. They establish a framework for the necessary components involved in submitting a Comprehensive Natural Resource Plan to the governing body. Each aspect of the Application Requirements aims to ensure thoroughness and compliance with applicable laws, ultimately leading to efficient processing of land-related applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f69badbdc0a01b4a234db008584a915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b235ce896bb310db6bf647fb59f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b56454c04ddb2d2d976f1d6f6ebbd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d7961ce66e26136990bb4bb54c838e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47812462d7ccc96ffd0025a366f98586&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4263b41e43a7e8a83f6017fb2cf1c50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32beb3a9e96c3d41cc526d4dbd0b1f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a4fda2a7ebb04a6a59cff745526b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a43129b93ff8ead9df972bce81ecbb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manufactured Dwelling">
      <data key="d0">Manufactured Dwelling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Manufactured dwellings are prefabricated homes that can be replaced under certain conditions related to damage or destruction.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufactured Dwellings are prefabricated homes built in factories and transported to the site.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufactured Dwellings are dwelling units constructed off-site that can be moved on public roadways, including trailers and mobile homes.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufactured dwelling encompasses units constructed off-site that can be transported on public roadways, including trailers and mobile homes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194988951f77d654ea0875ebdb6acdde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6e3473a810a12fa40e385deedea49f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bus Loading">
      <data key="d0">Bus Loading</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bus Loading refers to the requirements and standards for safe and efficient loading areas for buses, particularly at schools.&lt;SEP&gt;Bus Loading regulations ensure safe and efficient loading and unloading of students at school locations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd57b33ee4fb90b8e15b4036d8b2f9e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30acaad3495315145b81fed5d7cb9158</data>
