    <node id="Main Entrance">
      <data key="d0">Main Entrance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Main Entrance is defined as the primary entry point of a residential structure that must meet specific standards for safety and accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The main entrance is designated for pedestrian access and should be more prominent than the garage to enhance accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Entrance refers to the primary entry point of a structure, which must adhere to specific proximity and design standards outlined in the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The main entrance is the primary access point of a building, oriented towards the street, with requirements for porches and access.&lt;SEP&gt;The main entrance is the primary access point of a structure that must face the street lot line under community design standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The main entrance is the entry point most commonly used by pedestrians to access a building, often the widest point of entry.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06ffebbe5f5a48ace7018e8814873e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90656f21118fd0ad7c0ee7822eac4d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-606354f765e28b95d29b753fc9fe43fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b58865c473bfa9835169ceac4d038b1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9ce8abdb14d484f7e951e27e2fec56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3994dbc2c6f464ef189000d5ce6654c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781081</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
