    <node id="Seep">
      <data key="d0">Seep</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A Seep is a natural hydrological feature where water flows out of the ground and must be preserved in development planning.&lt;SEP&gt;A seep is an area where water is discharged through the ground surface, relevant for determining tract boundaries and easements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04cb5d072ac6b2a3e906facf4052c5aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe16dacd4c0cb29ef445c2340ee2812</data>
