    <node id="Disturbance Area">
      <data key="d0">Disturbance Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Disturbance Area is a designated zone that encompasses regions where development and construction activities may occur, necessitating specific regulations and setback requirements to protect the environment. This area is particularly governed by rules that aim to minimize environmental impact during activities like landscaping, construction, and utility line installation. 

Within the context of environmental protection, the Disturbance Area serves as a critical framework for regulating alterations. It includes not only the sites directly affected by such activities but also adjacent regions, ensuring that surrounding ecosystems and resources are preserved. The activities within this area are categorized into Permanent and Temporary disturbances, each with distinct management strategies.

In particular, the Disturbance Area is identified within the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone, indicating its importance in maintaining local ecological balance amid development pressures. This zone may involve pre-existing structures, as well as areas where vegetation management is essential to facilitate utility installations or other developments. Ultimately, the Disturbance Area plays a vital role in coordinating land use while prioritizing environmental sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f39dddebb1be94c3bd4cfa1ac35ccac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40d1cf5d1a59a47e32100e78eb27cf84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebeee1e9a6fdc5e2eb02bb6563ce14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d11d225e5566d1ff994f2025b1378ec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ade629e2e0020483f573660fbe8416a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8263d3660b494322f6b2d93ee1245f2d</data>
