    <node id="Street Lot Line">
      <data key="d0">Street Lot Line</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Street lot lines are the boundaries of a property that adjoin a street, affecting zoning and setback requirements for buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;The street lot line is the boundary line of a lot that abuts a street, inclusive of various configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Street lot lines refer to the boundaries along the edges of street lots, which can include front and side lot lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Residential Zone">
      <data key="d0">Residential Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential zones are designated areas where rules regarding building setbacks and other zoning regulations apply, specifically for residential use.&lt;SEP&gt;A residential zone is a land use classification primarily intended for housing development, which imposes specific regulations to maintain the character of areas intended for living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.130 Title 33">
      <data key="d0">33.130 Title 33</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">33.130 Title 33 refers to the specific section of planning and zoning regulations governing building setbacks and related requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6</data>
