    <node id="Electric Vehicle Chargers">
      <data key="d0">Electric Vehicle Chargers</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">Electric vehicle chargers are detached structures that are mentioned as part of the standards for uncovered vertical structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric Vehicle Chargers are devices that supply electric energy to electric vehicles, including standards for detachments and location in architectural plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric Vehicle Chargers are devices for charging electric vehicles, which may be located within service areas of drive-through facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric vehicle chargers are devices installed to provide charging facilities for electric vehicles as part of development requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric vehicle chargers are devices located in parking areas, designed for charging electric vehicles and accompanied by necessary protective equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric vehicle chargers are facilities that allow electric cars to recharge, exempt from certain regulations regarding site area modifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05ab6bd54c89f86d004823d37a33255e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77775bfe50a48aa700ab96a9ab1c440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a48525044c3c1bf75799ef0954937b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52cbe23eb8de6a4318808cef3ac4f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46af1a858cb150fbd0c6e6b2b602464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52cd6f75c0ef15f81f473a7fd946bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Landscaping">
      <data key="d0">Landscaping</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Landscaping is the practice of designing and maintaining outdoor spaces to improve aesthetics and environment, including cooling air and managing stormwater.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaping involves the planning and implementation of vegetation and design elements to enhance urban environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaping involves the design and arrangement of plants and outdoor space features, particularly in urban and residential areas to enhance appearance and functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaping regulations provide guidelines for the design and maintenance of green spaces around school sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Landscaping involves the design and maintenance of outdoor areas, although its significance is tied to historic attributes as noted in landmark documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46af1a858cb150fbd0c6e6b2b602464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30acaad3495315145b81fed5d7cb9158&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b45e62181c08d6aef102ffa4458a5226</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paths">
      <data key="d0">Paths</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Paths are walkways that may or may not contribute to a resource's historic significance, depending on documentation identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fabric Awnings">
      <data key="d0">Fabric Awnings</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Fabric awnings are coverings made of fabric that can be replaced or altered while maintaining existing dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric Awnings are used for shading and aesthetic purposes, and alterations to them must adhere to specific guidelines regarding size and configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric awnings are coverings used on buildings that can be replaced or altered without increasing the total fabric area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08792af032c7577571c2943db7371a28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f72437166c353de768d234823279f24</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Plaques">
      <data key="d0">Plaques</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Plaques are small flat markers attached to materials, typically containing information, and must meet specified dimensions and components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ground Mounted Mechanical Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Ground Mounted Mechanical Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Ground mounted mechanical equipment refers to installations that satisfy specified size and placement criteria in relation to street-facing facades.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
