    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.430">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.430</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.430 is a comprehensive regulatory framework that establishes regulations and standards related to Environmental Zones within city planning. It delineates various requirements and prohibitions that govern development activities in these zones, ensuring that such activities align with specified environmental standards and practices.

The chapter provides specific criteria concerning the construction and implementation of septic systems, land divisions, and other relevant infrastructure, making it essential for compliance during the development review process. Additionally, Chapter 33.430 details the necessary procedures for obtaining permits related to environmental zones, facilitating oversight and adherence to environmental governance.

This chapter also highlights the interaction of its regulations with other local regulations, such as those outlined in the Portland International Airport Plan District, which may influence or interact with the stipulated environmental standards. It explicitly mentions the Environmental Overlay Zones that need to be followed within the Portland International Airport Master Plan, reinforcing the importance of these regulations in comprehensive urban planning initiatives. 

Overall, Chapter 33.430 serves as a vital reference point for ensuring that developments within its jurisdiction comply with overarching environmental standards while promoting sustainable land use in urban environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f39dddebb1be94c3bd4cfa1ac35ccac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2325c884efc6a13f1b84583326ff8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e460c58e359f4aa61eae2678eeb2a806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cd2a226a2530256c685d499d90fe0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34a0bcc2ef40b300fb0774b97f4e1e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c25a4b5dcdfc23b3bd64f8c6d4bbc00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285f052019746f5b49b63ae041c898aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490cb02a9aa37ab5ed0231106009cb20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1226a7075ba7d150a3b769bb492b29a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Light Wells">
      <data key="d0">Light Wells</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Light wells are architectural features designed to bring natural light into buildings, fully surrounded by existing walls.&lt;SEP&gt;Light wells are architectural features that allow light into a building, with placement restrictions related to surrounding walls.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rooftop Vents">
      <data key="d0">Rooftop Vents</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Rooftop vents are openings on roofs for ventilation purposes, regulated by height and pitch specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Rooftop vents are outlets installed on a roof for ventilation, subject to height and setback regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Solar Energy Systems">
      <data key="d0">Solar Energy Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Rooftop solar energy systems are methods for harnessing solar power, subject to specific installation guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems installed on detached accessory buildings must comply with the same standards as new primary structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems are technologies that capture and convert sunlight into usable energy, with restrictions on installation on conservation landmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems are installations for harnessing solar power, which must be installed with specific dimensions and screening from the street.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems harness solar power and have specific installation standards based on roofing conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems are installations that convert solar power into usable energy and have specific mounting requirements based on roof type.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar energy systems are installations placed on specific types of roofs under distinct conditions to ensure compliance with outlined standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62277f559200167b441652bb61e8226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f72437166c353de768d234823279f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af58e78814991f9a5ecdccb7e8088e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7643c0f4d3b8e865b2421a8cf1882d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Residential Docks Standard">
      <data key="d0">Residential Docks Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Residential Docks Standard is intended to minimize environmental impacts from new floating boat docking structures on aquatic habitats.&lt;SEP&gt;The Residential Docks Standard aims to limit impacts on shallow water habitat and protect aquatic species.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873d10749dbc15173a36fece7c83683d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Endangered Species Act">
      <data key="d0">Endangered Species Act</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Endangered Species Act is a law aimed at protecting threatened and endangered species from extinction and preserving their habitats.&lt;SEP&gt;The Endangered Species Act is a law aimed at protecting species that are at risk of extinction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Endangered Species Act is a law aimed at protecting threatened and endangered animals and plants, impacting River Review evaluations and requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873d10749dbc15173a36fece7c83683d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8304e315438268768f83d85e05fcf463</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Floating Boat Docking Structure">
      <data key="d0">Floating Boat Docking Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Floating Boat Docking Structure is a new type of docking structure subject to specific standards regarding size and location.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exterior Lighting Standards">
      <data key="d0">Exterior Lighting Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Exterior Lighting Standards are regulations intended to minimize light glare and improve safety and security in public areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Exterior Lighting Standards outline requirements to minimize light pollution, maintain public safety, and improve ecological impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165b18aa9a1d81892edc1c295c96b243</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bird-Safe Glazing Standards">
      <data key="d0">Bird-Safe Glazing Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bird-Safe Glazing Standards are guidelines designed to reduce bird-to-building collisions by modifying window reflectivity and transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Bird-safe glazing standards are designed to reduce bird-to-building collisions by improving the visibility of exterior glazed surfaces to birds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91db399b32e598af5683382ecc53fa6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
