    <node id="Portland Bird Safe Windows List">
      <data key="d0">Portland Bird Safe Windows List</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Portland Bird Safe Windows List provides standards for exterior glazing treatments to minimize bird collisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Portland Bird Safe Windows List is a reference for treatment patterns and application techniques to enhance bird safety in building designs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Portland Bird Safe Windows List includes treatment patterns and application techniques to be used for bird-safe exterior glazing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60b9ffdb955ab3944250655ae5423afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc3fc3ad91ea490a2f8ffb98e83e2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91db399b32e598af5683382ecc53fa6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OS Zone">
      <data key="d0">OS Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The OS Zone, or Open Space zoning, refers to specific zoning areas typically designated for parks, recreation, and preserving natural landscapes while allowing certain developments. It encompasses various guidelines aimed at regulating land use and ensuring the area's functionality and aesthetic appeal.

Within the OS Zone, there are particular zoning classifications that impose standards relevant to both conforming and nonconforming uses. This area is also known for accommodating recreational fields, thereby permitting organized sports activities to take place within its boundaries. However, the zoning regulations specifically prohibit outdoor shelters, indicating restrictions on their establishment in this area for purposes of maintaining the intended open-space character.

Moreover, the OS Zone includes specific provisions in districts such as the Marquam Hill Plan District, where additional regulations and utilities—such as a suspended cable system—are integrated. Furthermore, the OS Zone mandates compliance with certain regulations for facilities like helicopter landing sites, which must adhere to impact standards to minimize disruption in these designated spaces.

In summary, the OS Zone serves multiple functions, balancing the need for recreational use with the preservation of natural areas, while imposing specific constraints and regulations to manage development within these open spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0bbb62dc601b56a2d362f9a82f2ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52cbe23eb8de6a4318808cef3ac4f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2474dfd41e2575d0e3e9c1417c737dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78755af7dcf0cbd31bb8a59f246d601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5814020534bf1fbc0a6e4c64746ca31d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Affordable Dwelling Units">
      <data key="d0">Affordable Dwelling Units</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Affordable Dwelling Units refer to housing units that are priced for individuals earning no more than 60 percent of the area median family income, as stipulated by Title 33.&lt;SEP&gt;Affordable dwelling units refer to housing that is made available to individuals or families at a reduced cost based on their income levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Affordable dwelling units refer to residential units that are priced to be affordable for individuals earning no more than 60 percent of the area median family income.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5adc4cb7aae3d0001c977968b8799a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4cc500f0cf6ffd63a8f594c9055457</data>
