    <node id="C Zone">
      <data key="d0">C Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The C Zone refers to a commercial zoning designation that encompasses specific planning and design standards applicable to development. This zoning classification is significant for regulating various commercial uses and facilitating appropriate development within defined areas. It serves a dual purpose, addressing both conforming and nonconforming uses, which allows for flexibility in the types of businesses that can operate within the zone.

In addition to its primary function as a commercial zone, the C Zone permits certain developments such as new mass shelters or alterations, provided they adhere to specific conditions set forth by the zoning regulations. These regulations also extend to outdoor shelters, where guidelines dictate construction and alteration practices to ensure compatibility with the surrounding area. 

Parking site standards are another critical focus within the C Zone, as the designation includes specific regulations governing the layout and requirements for parking facilities associated with commercial establishments. Furthermore, the C Zone is relevant in discussions about boundary features in areas like Rocky Butte, highlighting its geographical implications and relevance in urban planning.

Overall, the C Zone represents an essential framework for balancing commercial development with community standards, ensuring businesses can thrive while maintaining the character of adjacent residential neighborhoods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0471cd3f359b7c1de83040290a16c652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13c2d06abd310f2993f5dbfa38449c5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5814020534bf1fbc0a6e4c64746ca31d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Functional Values">
      <data key="d0">Functional Values</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Functional values refer to the benefits or services provided by natural resources, which are considered during evaluations and planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values refer to the essential attributes and benefits provided by natural resources, which must be preserved during development.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values refer to the ecological benefits provided by a habitat, which should not be significantly impacted by development activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values are characteristics related to the ecological functions of a water quality resource area that are evaluated during impact assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values refer to the benefits provided by natural resources, affecting the decisions regarding development and resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values refer to the roles and benefits provided by natural resources, crucial for assessing mitigation success.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional Values refer to the benefits provided by resources, which may include physical, aesthetic, educational, or other nonphysical functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9149bc1dda22c4352a0aaff8decd7425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad1968bb57e3baa2ecd3350abe6caf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f1a17fa78cd57a59c10407c2e49631f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d06cb95ab17fc909ffe773dee0f0a731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5045146aa70a167fd48292faecd8ea6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Recreational Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Public Recreational Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Recreational Facilities include trails, rest points, and other amenities designed to benefit the community while minimizing environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Recreational Facilities include trails and interpretative sites that must adhere to development criteria to ensure environmental protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Recreational Facilities encompass trails, viewpoints, and interpretative sites that provide community access to natural resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9149bc1dda22c4352a0aaff8decd7425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad1968bb57e3baa2ecd3350abe6caf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fec75523a13dc705f1116777ea0ce94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Impact Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Impact Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Impact Evaluation is a process used to assess the effects of a proposed development on site resources and to evaluate alternatives to minimize detrimental impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Impact Evaluation is a required assessment that demonstrates compliance with environmental standards and criteria for proposed developments in designated zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact Evaluation is the process through which the effects of proposed developments on functional values are assessed and reported.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact Evaluation is a process to assess compliance with approval criteria and evaluate development alternatives based on their impact on water quality resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The Impact Evaluation assesses potential negative effects of development on resources and functional values.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact evaluation is a process used to assess compliance with approval criteria and evaluate development alternatives for a site, particularly in the case of violations.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact Evaluation is a process used to determine compliance with approval criteria and assess practicable development alternatives for a specific site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9149bc1dda22c4352a0aaff8decd7425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9914c8cd6c5cbc27ea6f25de34c9dfa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51dc10f7cf6f3ff9bea2eb170cf1c4dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b0bd3b13a0c05d569d6126ad180bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3010f7a799b5930226f765522b860fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca</data>
