    <node id="Quick Vehicle Service">
      <data key="d0">Quick Vehicle Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Quick Vehicle Service is a type of service use in buildings within Subdistrict A that has specific regulatory exemptions under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2858436e5d48fb58437de44d9334763</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Convention and Conference Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Convention and Conference Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Convention and Conference Facilities are types of uses in buildings that are exempt from specific design regulations under certain circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2858436e5d48fb58437de44d9334763</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Development Rights">
      <data key="d0">Development Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Development rights refer to the potential dwelling units permissible on a site, which can be transferred under specific regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Development rights represent potential dwelling units that can be allocated between sending and receiving sites in regulatory contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Development Rights refer to the potential dwelling units permitted on a site, influencing housing development opportunities.&lt;SEP&gt;Development rights refer to the allocated potential dwelling units that may be permitted on a specific site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11ed8622a96da6b6be60b2a25c56017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31394699e4c236c5efd0bec39e7a8ab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d54757bbd8eb99b2b0cd39a957603d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Section 33.564">
      <data key="d0">Section 33.564</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.564 outlines regulations and procedures for land division and Planned Developments in designated areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimum Site Size">
      <data key="d0">Minimum Site Size</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimum Site Size refers to the regulatory requirement that land divisions or Planned Developments must be on sites of at least a certain acreage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47f51b4fbd4dac0a144b2d3f573a4dd9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Land Suitability Standards">
      <data key="d0">Land Suitability Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Land Suitability Standards outline the requirements for proposals for land divisions in residential zones and other areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38a0672dd2aa59189e1e13c242175d7b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Approval Criterion">
      <data key="d0">Approval Criterion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Approval Criterion refers to the guidelines that must be followed when vehicle access standards cannot be met.&lt;SEP&gt;Approval Criterion refers to the criteria that must be met for land division proposals, as stated in various sections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38a0672dd2aa59189e1e13c242175d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fe4540439f409de13002eb40172d2d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Preliminary Clearing and Grading Plan">
      <data key="d0">Preliminary Clearing and Grading Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Preliminary Clearing and Grading Plan is a required document that outlines clearing and grading standards for construction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Preliminary Clearing and Grading Plan outlines the requirements for clearing and grading activities on a development site, including mapping and proposed modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Preliminary Clearing and Grading Plan details limits of disturbance and tree protection measures for construction activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38a0672dd2aa59189e1e13c242175d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dc64b571fc1e4051ea286aa94de68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189a3579e304a7efcf0f543eaaad1a8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Geologic Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Geologic Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Geologic Conditions refer to the natural geological features of a site that may affect land divisions and suitability for development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38a0672dd2aa59189e1e13c242175d7b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781084</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.635.150">
      <data key="d0">33.635.150</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.635.150 outlines the Land Suitability Standards applicable to proposals for land divisions in residential zones.</data>
