    </node>
    <node id="Residential Densities">
      <data key="d0">Residential Densities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential densities pertain to the regulations governing the number of dwelling units allowed on a property, which can affect property development and zoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Base Zone Development Standards">
      <data key="d0">Base Zone Development Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Base zone development standards are regulations that apply when accessory dwelling units are not specifically addressed, serving as foundational guidelines for property development.&lt;SEP&gt;Base zone development standards are guidelines that dictate the allowable building practices within a specified zoning area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924adce58a3a3a8622d21ee99005b5a7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Landslide Hazard Area">
      <data key="d0">Landslide Hazard Area</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The landslide hazard area is a designated region at risk of landslides, affecting property use and development choices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Landslide Hazard Area is a designated region where regulations aim to limit development in order to minimize risks associated with landslides.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c35c570b66abd053c37dd3812df90d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intentional Destruction">
      <data key="d0">Intentional Destruction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Intentional destruction refers to the act of deliberately damaging a structure, which influences the rules governing the re-establishment of nonconforming uses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Accidental Damage">
      <data key="d0">Accidental Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accidental damage refers to unintentional harm to a structure that can complicate the status of nonconforming residential density rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maximum Residential Density Standard">
      <data key="d0">Maximum Residential Density Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum residential density standard establishes the upper limit on the number of dwelling units allowed per site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimum Residential Density Standard">
      <data key="d0">Minimum Residential Density Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimum residential density standard sets the lower limit on the number of dwelling units that must be maintained on a site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b33894864a61e3795f8a49e185ee7bcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Utility Scale Energy Production">
      <data key="d0">Utility Scale Energy Production</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Utility Scale Energy Production refers to the large-scale generation of energy, primarily from renewable resources such as wind turbines, and is typically conducted by utility companies for commercial purposes. This form of energy production is regulated under various zoning laws, including Single-Dwelling Zones and Manufacturing And Production categories in the Open Space Zone. It represents a significant sector of energy generation that is distinct from Small Scale Energy Production, with a focus on producing substantial quantities of electricity or heat for public distribution.

Facilities involved in Utility Scale Energy Production are classified as conditional uses within specific zoning regulations, indicating that they may be subject to certain environmental and operational standards. These activities often take place in commercial or mixed-use zones, ensuring limited environmental impact while meeting the energy demands of the grid. The methods employed in this category of energy production are diverse, encompassing various technologies aimed at generating notable amounts of electrical power.

Overall, Utility Scale Energy Production is crucial for meeting the energy needs of the public and contributes significantly to the energy landscape, adhering to regulatory frameworks designed to manage its implementation and minimize ecological footprints.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bfe32c70ad9d043f357dc56ff6f9925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7a46ce2a41072cf8f503e930128f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf715f84f913a198debd93fc73ff20b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e934d288b532969001ac5c602e3192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aafe5a7a2907664ceccb93037cc2fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6c39f118dd3cc1984138088ad67005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a773484e51a9cad486454fcfa9ec3959&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Solar Energy System">
      <data key="d0">Solar Energy System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Solar Energy System is a renewable energy installation on rooftops that must meet specific coverage requirements for new buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Solar Energy System refers to arrangements for harnessing solar power, with specific installation guidelines outlined based on roof types.&lt;SEP&gt;The solar energy system refers to photovoltaic technologies used for energy generation on buildings, adhering to specific regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c749708919a67aa6d2facb52ce88c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flat Roof">
      <data key="d0">Flat Roof</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A Flat Roof is a type of roof that is horizontal or nearly horizontal and serves as a suitable location for solar energy systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Flat roofs are surfaces that are horizontally oriented and capable of supporting installations such as skylights and solar energy systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A Flat Roof is a roof type with a pitch of 2 in 12 or less, measured to its highest point or parapet, as per building codes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mansard Roof">
      <data key="d0">Mansard Roof</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A Mansard Roof is a style of roof with a double slope on each of its sides that can accommodate solar energy systems under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mansard roofs are architectural structures with a dual-pitched design, allowing for specific solar energy system installations based on regulatory guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;A Mansard Roof is measured to the deck line, as specified in building measurement regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parapet">
      <data key="d0">Parapet</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A Parapet is a protective wall or railing at the edge of a roof, which must be higher than the solar energy system for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pitched Roof">
      <data key="d0">Pitched Roof</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A Pitched Roof is a roof that has a slope and requires specific guidelines for the installation of solar energy systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Pitched roofs are sloped roof structures that require specific guidelines for mounting solar energy systems without increasing the building's footprint or height.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skylight">
      <data key="d0">Skylight</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Skylight is a window in a roof or ceiling that can be installed under specific conditions concerning roof types and lot lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roof Hatch">
      <data key="d0">Roof Hatch</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Roof Hatch is an access point to a flat or pitched roof that can be installed with guidelines related to its location and type.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
