    <node id="Lot Confirmation">
      <data key="d0">Lot Confirmation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot Confirmation refers to the process of confirming the separation of a lot from abutting lots, finalized before September 11, 2020.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot Confirmation refers to the verification of parcel boundaries and classifications within land use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot Confirmation refers to the approval process for confirming the status of lots as defined by regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot Confirmation is a process defined by regulations for confirming a lot or combination of lots of record.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b56454c04ddb2d2d976f1d6f6ebbd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8e38ccecc8aee043d4f983d468a91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1548067bb4833113c6a54b4a7e87fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Replat">
      <data key="d0">Replat</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Replat involves creating new plat maps for previously subdivided land to reflect changes in boundaries or design.&lt;SEP&gt;Replat refers to the procedure of reconfiguring lot lines within a site to combine multiple lots into one or more configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Replat refers to the process of redefining the boundaries of lots within an existing subdivision without creating new lots.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b56454c04ddb2d2d976f1d6f6ebbd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa0352df0641b29208d29e9ef4be447b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Affordable Housing Fund">
      <data key="d0">Affordable Housing Fund</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Affordable Housing Fund is a financial resource managed by the Portland Housing Bureau aimed at supporting the development and maintenance of affordable housing within the city of Portland. It plays a crucial role in financing housing-related projects through fees collected from developers. These fees are typically incurred when developers opt for additional floor area, known as Bonus Floor Area Ratio (Bonus FAR), which allows them to maximize their building's space in exchange for contributions to the fund.

The Affordable Housing Fund is designed to incentivize development that contributes to affordable housing availability and sustainability. By requiring developers to make payments per square foot when they seek to benefit from the Bonus FAR, the fund generates vital financial resources that can be directed toward various affordable housing initiatives and projects. This mechanism underscores the fund's commitment to increase the stock of affordable housing options in Portland.

In summary, the Affordable Housing Fund serves as both a financial instrument and a catalyst for affordable housing development, ensuring that contributions from developers translate into tangible benefits for the community by enhancing the accessibility and maintenance of affordable housing within Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-586262724750ed4bbb098ac0aed41049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f57fb6953e9769254bb5d2a323550c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c8009e101b1c5acef3b9262a76129e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-916fae91f6b0da087cc62a6bce573a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7525c3c81ec880dec86a378f065ef6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93214ee5c49fbb5384175df60c9eafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04d6cd35d45d8e93ff5e834df187ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2c7926ceca17c4d0d7614d1c8acec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc22ba039a9fe91f1dbd58c1c542c993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26d97abf5771d4460162667c195b262f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7afd4cd98781a0f8a75a7fa3cd365098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-059e05beab69bbb7d4dc82bdd6ddff25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49acd712739227babe51a65cf9f9e8be</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neighborhood Association">
      <data key="d0">Neighborhood Association</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Neighborhood Association is a community organization that represents local residents and plays a vital role in the communication and planning processes related to their areas. These associations are tasked with receiving notifications and notices about significant community meetings, activities, and proposals that may impact their neighborhoods, including those from colleges and medical centers.

One of the key responsibilities of the Neighborhood Association is to be informed about new Type B accessory home occupations, as well as any developments that could affect local properties. This ensures that the interests and concerns of residents are taken into account in local planning and zoning matters. The Neighborhood Association must be contacted regarding proposed developments to adequately assess how these changes may influence the community.

Additionally, the Neighborhood Association is involved in the land use review process, which includes receiving meeting notes before land use reviews or the submission of building permit applications. This involvement is essential for making sure that any proposed alterations to the community are in line with the residents' preferences and the needs of the neighborhood.

Furthermore, Neighborhood Associations may participate in the historic resource review process within their districts, advocating for the preservation of local heritage and historical sites. Overall, the Neighborhood Association serves as a critical conduit between residents and local governance, ensuring that the voices of community members are heard in the decision-making processes that shape their living environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1b829449e430ca472af4da987d81a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7e7d1e624354524b6833b6427f9866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-021df6cb16582b344e89bb48dc23186f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a997e1b200b6816ddf145fba6c1929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fe28a6c33ecbcbe2396156e4ee10e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca333850d886eb6696137e8d84c9908&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe92a3f46b3bfc4baa1f040d200709a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781085</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
