    <node id="Skylights">
      <data key="d0">Skylights</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Skylights are restricted from being on street-facing elevations due to design regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Skylights are architectural elements that must adhere to specific guidelines based on their location on the building.&lt;SEP&gt;Skylights are windows installed in roofs for natural light, governed by specific height and location criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Skylights are windows installed in roofs to allow natural light, which can be subject to installation guidelines based on the roof type.&lt;SEP&gt;Skylights are roof openings covered with transparent material, designed to admit light and are applicable under certain configurations for solar energy systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Skylights are architectural features allowing natural light into buildings and are specified as exceptions in building roof area calculations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9e945a4de0eb93decd93ac5bbc54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af58e78814991f9a5ecdccb7e8088e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71ef8e763b48167f014ebc29d2564293</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Accessory Structure">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An accessory structure is a building or space that can be converted into an accessory dwelling unit if it is at least 5 years old.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory structures are secondary buildings on a property meant for specific purposes, with guidelines for construction provided.&lt;SEP&gt;An accessory structure refers to an additional building that is secondary to a primary structure and has specific regulatory exemptions depending on its size and location.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Structure refers to subordinate buildings or structures that may be subject to demolition reviews and evaluation procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Structure refers to secondary importance structures on a site, such as garages or fences.&lt;SEP&gt;An Accessory Structure is a secondary building that supports the main structure in a site’s usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc8929a3f5f26daf160f30332a927b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b3d78b716894f51a8b9d0830f8f790e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfe18720ad9b5bf5dadab610a40b064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825dcc9caa885b9e5aef8f2ccbaf183d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
