    <node id="Quasi-Judicial Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Quasi-Judicial Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Quasi-Judicial Procedures are processes that resemble judicial proceedings but are conducted in administrative contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Quasi-Judicial Procedures are specific processes outlined for reviewing land use approvals and violations.&lt;SEP&gt;Quasi-Judicial Procedures refer to processes that involve decision-making by a governing body, which requires adherence to specific procedures and standards around land use hearings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c623ec1ba96e21d348f6cf747ed9156</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Land Use Approval">
      <data key="d0">Land Use Approval</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Land Use Approval is a decision granting permission for the use or development of land, subject to certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Land Use Approval is a formal consent for a development or use of land according to zoning codes.&lt;SEP&gt;Land Use Approval is the process by which changes to land are authorized, often involving conditions related to tree preservation and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Land Use Approval denotes a decision regarding the use of land, potentially including conditions or time limits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6359633c178583bad809c59ed226cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd54e5b638113595ce88bbc6ccf94bc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.700.020">
      <data key="d0">33.700.020</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">33.700.020 refers to the section of the Title 33 that outlines uses and developments that are not allowed by right and the requirement for a land use review.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.700.030">
      <data key="d0">33.700.030</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">33.700.030 refers to the section of Title 33 outlining violations and enforcement related to land use decisions and approvals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.700.040">
      <data key="d0">33.700.040</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">33.700.040 outlines the procedures for reconsideration of land use approvals in accordance with Title 33.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e4433ccb8446a4e4dd5e7c31a9daeb3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
