    </node>
    <node id="Bureau of Planning and Sustainability">
      <data key="d0">Bureau of Planning and Sustainability</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bureau of Planning and Sustainability is a city department in Portland tasked with managing various aspects of urban planning and environmental sustainability. This bureau plays a critical role in overseeing zoning maps, planning activities, and sustainability practices, which include establishing and enforcing regulations concerning recycling areas and environmental standards for development.

Specifically, the Bureau of Planning and Sustainability regulates the requirements for recycling areas, ensuring that these regulations align with broader sustainability initiatives. The bureau also monitors compliance with green building certifications, verifying that new developments meet established environmental standards. Additionally, it prepares recommendations on city standards related to new information regarding non-ionizing radiation and its implications for human health.

In the realm of cultural preservation, the Bureau is responsible for maintaining a confidential atlas of identified archaeological resources and overseeing planning and zoning regulations that relate to these archaeological sites. This underscores the bureau's commitment to integrating historical resources into urban planning.

Furthermore, the Bureau of Planning and Sustainability provides vital staff assistance to the Planning Commission and prepares reports and recommendations for legislative matters, aiding the City Council in decision-making. The bureau also has a role in notifying the Land Conservation and Development Commission about relevant hearings, thereby promoting transparency and public involvement in planning processes.

Overall, the Bureau of Planning and Sustainability is integral to fostering an environmentally conscious and forward-thinking urban landscape in Portland, demonstrating a commitment to both sustainable development and the preservation of cultural resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8650a4518ea9b5abb022622589521156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-423bb58a4673879619218c3271a171e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b03bc141c3d781440a712d9c33699f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b659477574fcf7f35453f172163de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b430ca141ad0936b7b20ef5f23780667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495efc01559ae21a68e9da3b57998769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef944d23c9926239972a50df6aac13f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e3be3ac7b6ba5960122bfee8047a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc65f441d5b262a6e985063f42142907&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-250f22c8b2433134e7522ccaf4bb55d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f231106269a74d76750e77d25977faa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71ef8e763b48167f014ebc29d2564293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-721ec91bd394c742ab66be71cc2391f1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manufacturing And Production">
      <data key="d0">Manufacturing And Production</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Manufacturing And Production pertains to activities involved in producing goods and services, with regulated conditional uses in certain zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production outlines industrial land uses that have specific compliance requirements in the Open Space Zone, particularly concerning energy production.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production involves the processes and industries that create goods and products for consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production refers to the activity of producing goods on a site, outlined in the conditional use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production is recognized as an active use within the zoning regulations for the Northwest Plan District.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production firms are involved in the creation and processing of goods, primarily for wholesale and not typically for direct public sale.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing And Production is a use category for facilities engaged in producing goods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b01451771b358c77494f198e0c0a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 100-1">
      <data key="d0">Table 100-1</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 100-1 lists various uses, including conditional and prohibited uses, along with standards and criteria for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 100-1 is a referenced table within the Open Space Zone regulations that lists allowed uses and their classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b31593c6056a4c4b7b5e1b873010f6</data>
