    <node id="Short Term, Mass, And Outdoor Shelters">
      <data key="d0">Short Term, Mass, And Outdoor Shelters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Short Term, Mass, And Outdoor Shelters are community services that are prohibited under specific regulations within the Open Space Zone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pedestrian Connection System">
      <data key="d0">Pedestrian Connection System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pedestrian Connection System establishes necessary walkways connecting dwelling units to streets and outdoor areas, enhancing accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pedestrian Connection System refers to the network that connects dwelling units to the street and outdoor common areas, ensuring accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c54aa01b8a84d0bf5d8975d9c8cc8b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visitability Standard">
      <data key="d0">Visitability Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The visitability standard outlines the necessary accessible features for residences, facilitating ease of access for individuals of all abilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Visitability Standard aims to ensure that residential units are accessible for individuals with mobility challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;The Visitability Standard ensures accessible features in residential units for people of all ages and abilities, promoting community interaction and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The Visitability Standard ensures that housing is accessible for individuals of all ages and abilities, promoting inclusive living conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c54aa01b8a84d0bf5d8975d9c8cc8b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff254476c2742dcdf5c26a1256fd36e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee4ba726d698227e002aae5c6cc82e38</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cottage Cluster Site">
      <data key="d0">Cottage Cluster Site</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cottage Cluster Site is a residential site type that must adhere to specific visitability standards for accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planned Developments">
      <data key="d0">Planned Developments</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Planned Developments refer to large-scale development projects that undergo specific planning processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Developments are a category discussed in the regulations that outlines standards for residential and other uses in designated zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Developments involve the comprehensive planning of land for residential or commercial use as a cohesive unit.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Developments are designed land use plans that integrate different types of development within a defined area.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Developments refer to specific proposals for land development that require adherence to zoning standards and criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24a0dc5a40ce1a7a9401f80aac49c163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cea9dda5872573fde3c02744ac5969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CR Zoning">
      <data key="d0">CR Zoning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CR Zoning refers to a zoning classification where site transfers are prohibited.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CE Zone">
      <data key="d0">CE Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The CE Zone is an area that has defined limits for indoor agriculture and other conditional uses according to zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;CE Zone is a zoning classification within the city that regulates building heights and FAR.&lt;SEP&gt;The CE Zone permits individual industrial uses limited to 40,000 square feet of net building area.&lt;SEP&gt;CE Zone is a zoning classification where exterior display of goods is allowed with some limitations regarding industrial goods.&lt;SEP&gt;The CE Zone is a zoning category that permits various uses and development options, potentially requiring additional specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The CE Zone is a zoning classification with regulations for ground floor active uses that must comply with specific standards.&lt;SEP&gt;CE Zone is a specific zoning designation mentioned in the approval criteria for Planned Developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fab78bf22476f90e50de5d511279727d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Covenants with the City">
      <data key="d0">Covenants with the City</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Covenants with the City are agreements that establish conditions tied to property deeds regarding FAR changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City are agreements required to ensure the installation, maintenance, and replacement of public art under the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City are legal agreements that property owners must execute, outlining compliance with zoning regulations and development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City are stipulations that property owners must comply with regarding public art installations in coordination with the City Arts Program.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City involve agreements that ensure compliance with city regulations regarding property maintenance and usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City are required agreements to ensure that Preservation Parking is primarily for buildings served by the parking for a certain duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Covenants with the City are agreements ensuring the compliance of long-term bike parking with city standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e6e0a14b42f25e67a43e11831d8486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c127588b3effb62124f2b4367f10741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7282e754cd453819f3e67c09c8e7a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-701c3f15dff43f3530bb018f9bae2909</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paragraphs C.2 and C.3">
      <data key="d0">Paragraphs C.2 and C.3</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraphs C.2 and C.3 detail specific development standards related to FAR.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R Zone">
      <data key="d0">R Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The R Zone is a zoning designation primarily associated with residential areas that include specific regulations and requirements aimed at fostering community living while managing the impacts of developments on neighborhoods. This classification not only addresses the characteristics of the residential zones but also specifies guidelines related to various aspects, including landscaping, building heights, and interactions with recreational facilities.

In the context of R Zone regulations, specific screening requirements are imposed for mechanical equipment, ensuring a maintained aesthetic and functional environment. Furthermore, drive-through facilities are subject to particular landscaping and setback requirements, which contribute to the overall planning and integration of commercial uses within residential areas.

The R Zone designation also applies to nonconforming uses, meaning that certain existing land uses may not comply with the regular zoning requirements but are still allowed under specific conditions. There are also regulations governing the construction of noise-buffering walls, particularly along thoroughfares like Powell Boulevard, highlighting the R Zone's focus on mitigating noise and enhancing residential livability.

Building height regulations are part of the R Zone's framework, with a maximum stipulation of 30 feet for structures, which ensures that developments do not overshadow neighboring properties and maintain a suitable living environment. Additionally, R Zones permit the establishment of outdoor shelters under specific restrictions, including the number of shelters allowed, which emphasizes controlled and community-oriented use of public spaces.

The R Zone also includes provisions for recreational fields and organized sports, indicating its comprehensive approach to integrating leisure activities within residential settings. Overall, the R Zone is dedicated to managing development impacts while promoting harmonious community living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c12d6555e1901995a51aaf68fcae440f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0471cd3f359b7c1de83040290a16c652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52cbe23eb8de6a4318808cef3ac4f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13c2d06abd310f2993f5dbfa38449c5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5814020534bf1fbc0a6e4c64746ca31d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d1779dc70c5faec44a2798d3eb478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52cd6f75c0ef15f81f473a7fd946bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d46523b43ad78784d5fd13052c9870a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.260">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.260</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.260 outlines regulations concerning occupied recreational vehicles and how Title 33 applies to them, effective 8/1/21.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Occupied Recreational Vehicle">
      <data key="d0">Occupied Recreational Vehicle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Occupied Recreational Vehicle refers to the use of recreational vehicles as living spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Occupied Recreational Vehicle involves using RVs as temporary living quarters, often as part of housing solutions in various contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;An occupied recreational vehicle is defined as a vehicle utilized for residential occupancy that does not count as a dwelling unit under Title 33.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.262">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.262</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.262 focuses on off-site impacts and establishes standards to protect various zones from objectionable impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R, C, CI, IR, OS zones">
      <data key="d0">R, C, CI, IR, OS zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The R, C, CI, IR, and OS zones are classifications within the Portland City Code that delineate different types of land use regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3780b9c6c1f1a0194a82434f5bdf402e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781086</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
