    <node id="Environmental Protection Zone">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Protection Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Environmental Protection Zone (EPZ) refers to designated areas specifically created to provide the highest level of protection to important natural resources and functional values in accordance with city regulations. These zones serve to maintain natural resources and prevent environmental degradation by imposing strict restrictions on construction and development activities.

Within an Environmental Protection Zone, specific regulations govern development to ensure that the natural environment is safeguarded from detrimental impacts associated with construction activities. The EPZ aims to strike a balance by minimizing environmental harm while allowing for necessary development, which must undergo rigorous evaluations to assess its compatibility with conservation goals.

Overall, the Environmental Protection Zone is crucial for the preservation of natural resources and functional values, offering a structured approach to environmental conservation within defined boundaries. These areas are vital for protecting ecosystems from the pressures of urbanization and ensuring that future generations can benefit from the ecological services they provide.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c2325c884efc6a13f1b84583326ff8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebeee1e9a6fdc5e2eb02bb6563ce14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fec75523a13dc705f1116777ea0ce94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b463643e19fbf1a7684090d0b63adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a90d16f519debce0d1b06def34f6932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9914c8cd6c5cbc27ea6f25de34c9dfa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d37b0db2824c732a3a9a02ff910d85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbcf1c43cb59d25662f5af1b9ac994a8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
