    <node id="SHPO">
      <data key="d0">SHPO</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The State Historic Preservation Office (SHPO) is responsible for the identification and preservation of historical and cultural sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oregon State Historic Preservation Office (SHPO) is responsible for overseeing archaeological resource recovery projects and ensuring adherence to preservation standards.&lt;SEP&gt;SHPO refers to the State Historic Preservation Office, which is involved in recording archaeological resources and managing reports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc38fc86828ecd90586e33007486e5d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef944d23c9926239972a50df6aac13f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Burial">
      <data key="d0">Burial</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Burial is defined as an archaeological resource with evidence of human remains or funerary objects.&lt;SEP&gt;A burial falls under archaeological resources, enforcing regulations that apply to all identified resources when present.&lt;SEP&gt;A burial is classified as an archaeological resource that demonstrates evidence of human remains or funerary objects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573af662b54921327a93cf7f0c3a073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26cd939550cd7265fc4c8d659c5ff9f9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Village">
      <data key="d0">Village</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A village is characterized as an archaeological resource with evidence of a relatively permanent residential location.&lt;SEP&gt;A village is categorized as an archaeological resource subject to specific regulations when not associated with burials.&lt;SEP&gt;A village is identified as an archaeological resource representing a location traditionally occupied for residential purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573af662b54921327a93cf7f0c3a073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26cd939550cd7265fc4c8d659c5ff9f9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seasonal Campsite">
      <data key="d0">Seasonal Campsite</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Seasonal campsite is an archaeological resource indicating organized activity focused on resource extraction on a seasonal basis.&lt;SEP&gt;A seasonal campsite is a type of archaeological resource that is governed by its own set of regulations during ground disturbance activities.&lt;SEP&gt;A seasonal campsite is an archaeological resource indicating organized activity in harvesting and processing resources periodically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573af662b54921327a93cf7f0c3a073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26cd939550cd7265fc4c8d659c5ff9f9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Activity Area">
      <data key="d0">Activity Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An activity area is defined as an archaeological resource where specific activities took place, such as stone tool making.&lt;SEP&gt;An activity area is classified as an archaeological resource where specific activities, such as tool-making or food preparation, occurred.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26cd939550cd7265fc4c8d659c5ff9f9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Traditional, Sacred, or Cultural Use Site">
      <data key="d0">Traditional, Sacred, or Cultural Use Site</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">This site type is characterized by evidence of sacred or ceremonial locations, including vision quest sites and sweat lodge sites.&lt;SEP&gt;A traditional, sacred, or cultural use site is an archaeological resource linked to ceremonial or spiritual practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0093ccd81e4a4bb0c52f74a13adda6fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26cd939550cd7265fc4c8d659c5ff9f9</data>
