    <node id="U.S. Army Corps of Engineers">
      <data key="d0">U.S. Army Corps of Engineers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is a federal agency responsible for approving dredging and maintenance activities in federal navigation channels.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is a federal agency involved in the approval of channel, slip, and berth maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is responsible for approving channel maintenance and dredging activities in federal navigation channels.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is responsible for managing and regulating development and maintaining resources across waterways and floodplains.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is a federal agency that plays a role in regulating permits related to environmental impacts and mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is a federal agency responsible for public engineering, design, and construction projects, including environmental management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b715d8f3b52a84d0efa1e1daabf8956b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c81af569271dc0e96af33c5eb99f9dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2653802c982b64f8a7af01800f4406b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5045146aa70a167fd48292faecd8ea6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad866e29e441289a8f35f6617f6b3691</data>
