    <node id="Approval Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Approval Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Approval Criteria are the defined standards that must be met for various types of applications and proposals across different contexts, ensuring compliance with established regulations. These criteria serve as benchmarks for various reviews, including environmental, resource, and land development applications.

For development applications, Approval Criteria ensure that projects align with specific guidelines, such as those required for nonconforming situation reviews and environmental review applications. Applications for resource reviews, particularly within the Pleasant Valley Natural Resources Overlay Zone, must also adhere to these standards to gain approval.

In addition, Approval Criteria govern land divisions and related changes, specifying the necessary conditions for preliminary plans and final plats, as well as for modifications, relocations, or demolitions of historic resources. They are also foundational for the evaluation of land use proposals, ensuring that all developments comply with both community needs and regulatory standards.

The criteria specifically address the approval process for various project types, such as community service uses and Planned Developments, where distinct standards apply to facilitate appropriate land use. Furthermore, they encompass the evaluation of resource management plans, rights-of-way regulations, and the review of master plans, solidifying their role in maintaining the integrity of urban planning and resource conservation.

Approval Criteria additionally include guidelines for assessing impact mitigation plans, ensuring that potential environmental and community impacts are addressed adequately. As such, these criteria are instrumental in guiding the approval process across a wide spectrum of land use and development scenarios, thereby promoting orderly growth and sustainable resource management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-382ea5f9bd1d1962a9c0ded6051b139a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdee8c33d0d52a7455e70087137ca492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03672adab686e2724fe4ae10d50293ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd02cf4545f01a8b1a3eabb4ce881c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c866b4b0736bc538364f76d18bd9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2dff9267506b3019f40d39ac0b51e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ca5b72e1693d958a1e3c385272e963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b0bd3b13a0c05d569d6126ad180bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6798d89accc1ff81b347ffdd52d0e6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca9a5a2db627da6f2925010a7a2a42fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a03e87f530e2f281bbac1f0bd2b6049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cad83ae88a9187d47c9acf881162cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9baf563ec9df2a33ac29db9f4fc53fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e988f81291359d27584c02f5af917de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca73cfb027011d4c0e66fe2e055b6280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972d6f8b824b76de1c4e754f5d9f3110&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca333850d886eb6696137e8d84c9908&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d28f6febcf4de65239d0203f2197382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f7d373987e115c5189e0f34f1774910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67111441a3c9d2875734e7bedb42d3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca</data>
