    <node id="Density Calculation">
      <data key="d0">Density Calculation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Density calculation is a method used to determine the number of dwelling units allowed based on site area, considering rounding rules.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fraction">
      <data key="d0">Fraction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fraction is a numerical representation used in density calculations to determine dwelling units based on various rounding thresholds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allowed Dwelling Units">
      <data key="d0">Allowed Dwelling Units</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Allowed dwelling units refer to the number of residential units permissible according to density calculations and site area specifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Site Area">
      <data key="d0">Site Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Site area is the total land area on which development measures, such as density and building coverage, are calculated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Public Rights-of-Way">
      <data key="d0">Public Rights-of-Way</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Public rights-of-way refer to the legal right for public access to transportation routes, which influence site area measurements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Private Rights-of-Way">
      <data key="d0">Private Rights-of-Way</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Private rights-of-way indicate legal permissions for private access to properties, affecting measurements in development standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maximum Density Calculations">
      <data key="d0">Maximum Density Calculations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum density calculations refer to the specific methods used to determine the allowable density of dwelling units based on the area of the site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Measurement of Distances">
      <data key="d0">Measurement of Distances</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Measurement of distances involves specific guidelines for determining required distances for setbacks and structural dimensions in development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Measuring Development Standards">
      <data key="d0">Measuring Development Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Measuring development standards outlines the criteria and methods used in determining standards for building coverage, floor area, and setbacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shortened Distances">
      <data key="d0">Shortened Distances</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Shortened distances pertain to the guideline where distances are measured using the shortest route between two objects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7deb7311917979d720727eeda5b9e8d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Base Zone">
      <data key="d0">Base Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Base Zone refers to designated areas within a planning framework for land use and development regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FAR (Floor Area Ratio)">
      <data key="d0">FAR (Floor Area Ratio)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FAR is a measure used to define the intensity of land use by regulating the ratio of building area to the size of the lot.&lt;SEP&gt;FAR (Floor Area Ratio) is a zoning measurement representing the ratio of a building's total floor area to the size of the land on which it is built.&lt;SEP&gt;FAR, or Floor Area Ratio, is a regulatory measure used to determine the maximum allowable development density on a site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d0e3bbe363516aa161846014338967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2da4d204d050cba040fddbe243ce05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="January 1, 2025">
      <data key="d0">January 1, 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">January 1, 2025 is the effective date noted in relation to the regulations and standards for Multi-Dwelling Zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Short Term Shelters">
      <data key="d0">Short Term Shelters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Short Term Shelters refer to temporary housing facilities regulated under local zoning laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Short term shelters refer to temporary accommodations that operate under specific regulations regarding existing structures and new constructions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d094258a7672d9b9a828426b17e2146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mass Shelters">
      <data key="d0">Mass Shelters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mass Shelters are large-scale temporary housing facilities, subject to specific regulations under zoning laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass shelters are large facilities designed to provide accommodations for many individuals, governed by particular regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass shelters are facilities designed to provide larger accommodations with specific regulations regarding bed occupancy and operational hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass shelters are established facilities to provide temporary accommodation for individuals in need, subject to zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d094258a7672d9b9a828426b17e2146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Outdoor Shelters">
      <data key="d0">Outdoor Shelters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Outdoor Shelters are temporary structures regulated by zoning laws for community services.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor shelters refer to temporary or permanent facilities providing shelter outside traditional buildings, also regulated for community service uses.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor shelters are designated areas for temporary housing that are exempt from certain development standards, subject to specific site and operational requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor shelters refer to temporary shelters regulated under specific zoning laws, with defined limits on the number of individual shelters based on different zoning categories.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor Shelters refer to facilities that provide temporary accommodations and must comply with specific zoning regulations in the I zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d094258a7672d9b9a828426b17e2146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdfe21baa0f0ca21d6a17ac611149488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c1ff44e4a06a65a47b8c351d06d59b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
