    </node>
    <node id="Riparian Buffer Area">
      <data key="d0">Riparian Buffer Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Riparian Buffer Area is a zone adjacent to waterways where vegetation removal or pruning is prohibited during certain times to protect the ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;The Riparian Buffer Area is a vegetated region next to water bodies, crucial for protecting water quality and providing habitat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Riparian Buffer Area is a defined space adjacent to water bodies where specific environmental protections and restrictions apply.&lt;SEP&gt;The Riparian Buffer Area is a transitional zone between land and a river, where proposed developments can impact natural resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40d1cf5d1a59a47e32100e78eb27cf84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5ea5fe5eea40eab34623aa7e60f482&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a5816615430d9b588c4adaf4aa3131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5045146aa70a167fd48292faecd8ea6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Publicly Accessible Outdoor Area">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Outdoor Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The publicly accessible outdoor area is a designated space open to the public, which must meet specific design review and accessibility standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ff630c9a267554d2f1236df690069f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
