    <node id="Outdoor Common Area">
      <data key="d0">Outdoor Common Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Outdoor Common Area is the space adjacent to new buildings that must meet various design requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Outdoor common areas are shared spaces that must meet minimum size and accessibility requirements under city planning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ff630c9a267554d2f1236df690069f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cf98dff4ee5559ad6fd84e90727c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indoor Common Area">
      <data key="d0">Indoor Common Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indoor common areas must be designed as recreational facilities or community rooms for residents.&lt;SEP&gt;Indoor common areas refer to recreational or community spaces within a building, which cannot be substituted with non-recreational facilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ff630c9a267554d2f1236df690069f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59602cfae2cfed1834328c9ad24adf39</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Combination of Outdoor Areas">
      <data key="d0">Combination of Outdoor Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The combination of individual, common, and publicly accessible outdoor areas fulfills city requirements for outdoor space related to development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ff630c9a267554d2f1236df690069f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Portland Bureau of Transportation">
      <data key="d0">Portland Bureau of Transportation</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Portland Bureau of Transportation (PBOT) is the municipal agency in Portland responsible for a wide range of transportation-related activities, including the review and management of transportation policies and impact standards. PBOT oversees the approval and regulation of public rights-of-way and the construction of trails, ensuring that these elements fit within the city’s broader transportation framework.

Additionally, PBOT plays a crucial role in determining street improvements and managing transportation infrastructure throughout the city. This includes the location, dimensions, and specifications of rights-of-way, particularly in designated areas such as the Gateway plan district and Hayden Island. PBOT also administers the multi-modal street plan, aiming to integrate various forms of transportation and cater to diverse community needs.

The agency is involved in transportation impact studies, providing guidelines to assess the implications of proposed developments. Beyond infrastructure, PBOT monitors and permits accessory parking, particularly within the Northwest Plan District. Furthermore, the agency manages and collects funding from the Northwest Transportation Fund, which is utilized for various transportation-related improvements across Portland, thus ensuring a sustainable and efficient transportation network for the city.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd57b33ee4fb90b8e15b4036d8b2f9e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-916fae91f6b0da087cc62a6bce573a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa5d2c57a95ae65f663a55f78fa3c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4749d2209607255edbe985025b727249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79270fc3c081d0e0b0a71f05624d0eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b121eab358b392062623a0c2554b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e3be3ac7b6ba5960122bfee8047a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61687599149060b1e058a26bfd55caee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e317f6dbe5f15015c8e4149009a9021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bc34687798d2c98cb9455da5ca08306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d532a006f3aa47075d5f58cb0d7da4e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd915bc95a0b87e710beaeeee303a655&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-386ae62e0f06be64c345a3fd84815c6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
