    <node id="Ord. No. 175204">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 175204</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 175204 is a legislative ordinance that became effective on March 1, 2001. This ordinance includes various amendments to regulations that relate to zoning, design review, and planning within specific districts, particularly the Columbia South Shore Plan District and the Central City Plan District. 

The ordinance is primarily associated with modifications to the zoning chapter, which outlines how land use is regulated within these areas. Its amendments are aimed at enhancing the effectiveness of existing regulations, ensuring that they align with contemporary planning needs and priorities. Overall, Ord. No. 175204 serves as a critical legislative document impacting the regulatory landscape of zoning and land development as of its effective date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93d39d3e5dc5ac990b049b748fa4e96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19a2393681785537b2d0f83af94a363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3f9ffb1d8c7f041a89cac2f7df9d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f9cce1f67d8125895ea396b1acc241</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CI1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">CI1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CI1 Zone is a zoning classification with specific building height limits and development standards as outlined in the planning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI1 Zone is a designated area that promotes compatible development with surrounding residential zones and open spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI1 Zone is a zoning classification with specific maximum height regulations relative to adjacent zones.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI1 Zone refers to a commercial and industrial zone that influences regulations around drive-through facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI1 zone permits certain outdoor shelters under defined regulations and restrictions related to their establishment and expansion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58aaae1598e79c7b72066b698da3a9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7525c3c81ec880dec86a378f065ef6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52cd6f75c0ef15f81f473a7fd946bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf1cc9b5437586cfb484233e2286c341</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CI2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">CI2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">CI2 Zone is a zoning classification that allows for greater building height limits compared to CI1 and is governed by specific development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI2 Zone allows for urban development with characteristics consistent with adjacent mixed-use areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI2 Zone is a zoning classification that has reduced maximum height standards based on its proximity to other zones.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI2 Zone is a specific zoning area accommodating mass shelters under conditional use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI2 zone has defined procedures for outdoor shelters and their conditional uses based on specific studies.&lt;SEP&gt;The CI2 zone is an industrial zoning classification that accommodates certain types of light industrial and commercial activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58aaae1598e79c7b72066b698da3a9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7525c3c81ec880dec86a378f065ef6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf1cc9b5437586cfb484233e2286c341</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Section 33.285.050">
      <data key="d0">Section 33.285.050</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.285.050 provides the regulations and standards for short term and mass shelters including zoning requirements and review procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 33.285.050 outlines the standards and regulations for mass shelters and their review procedures in certain zoning areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 33.285.050 contains standards that outdoor shelters must meet to remain compliant with regulations in various zoning categories.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ac355b146a97e19880b3790c5ffe83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3caa6629bdef153dada4d72aed50d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
