    <node id="Mitigation Area">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Mitigation Area is an identified space where ecological repairs or improvements are implemented due to disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;A mitigation area is a designated space where certain environmental protections and stormwater discharges must adhere to specific regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation Area refers to the designated location for implementing mitigation activities in place of altered or destroyed natural resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfece86ae05751fbebb6324df767074f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbcf1c43cb59d25662f5af1b9ac994a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca18882d6a8207dec4b469f7a2654fd4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 475-3">
      <data key="d0">Table 475-3</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 475-3 outlines the planting density standards and requirements for different tree sizes and associated planting options.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 475-3 outlines the planting standards that must be adhered to following environmental disturbances.</data>
