    <node id="Lot Area">
      <data key="d0">Lot Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot Area refers to the total area of a property, which must meet specific standards for property line adjustments, particularly regarding minimum and maximum area requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot Area refers to the measured area of a lot of land, which is essential for determining zoning compliance and development standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e6483ee1a0cf1415621eb7ccf6224b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maximum Flag Lot Area">
      <data key="d0">Maximum Flag Lot Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum Flag Lot Area is defined as the upper limit of 3,000 square feet for the total area of a flag lot, including both the flag and pole portions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Front Lot Line">
      <data key="d0">Front Lot Line</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Front Lot Line indicates the boundary at the front of a lot, impacting minimum standards for flag lots where none are specified.&lt;SEP&gt;Front Lot Line is a boundary line that defines the front of a property.&lt;SEP&gt;The front lot line is the shortest lot line abutting a street, particularly in corner lots.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot Width">
      <data key="d0">Lot Width</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot Width refers to the minimum width requirement of a lot, stated as 36 feet at the midpoint of opposite lot lines for flag lots.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot width measurement involves placing a rectangle along the minimum front building setback line in single-dwelling zones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a421dc7c5c5ed797ef20bf18c33cb13c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot Depth">
      <data key="d0">Lot Depth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lot Depth is the required measurement of the depth of a lot, also specified to be at least 36 feet for flag lots.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot depth pertains to the measurement of the length from front to back within a defined parcel of land.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3da64931c37bc8d61d93781cf02db2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a421dc7c5c5ed797ef20bf18c33cb13c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminals">
      <data key="d0">Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminals are facilities for storing and distributing fossil fuels, subject to strict regulations regarding capacity and condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Fossil Fuel Terminals are defined facilities not including those for exclusive use at transportation hubs or reprocessing used petroleum products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c87cd5892944f62fa946209c5e76d09</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ord. No. 179092">
      <data key="d0">Ord. No. 179092</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ord. No. 179092 is a legislative ordinance that underwent amendment, becoming effective on April 1, 2005. This ordinance primarily addresses regulations related to planning and zoning, as well as design review policies. 

Specifically, Ord. No. 179092 amended existing regulations concerning the Central City Plan District, thereby impacting governance and urban planning frameworks within that area. The ordinance serves as a legal measure that modifies previous regulatory structures, and its effective date is consistently noted throughout multiple descriptions as April 1, 2005. 

Overall, Ord. No. 179092 is established as a crucial ordinance within the legislative framework, shaping the planning and zoning landscape by refining existing policies and ensuring their relevance as of the effective date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93d39d3e5dc5ac990b049b748fa4e96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd349cb529fd5cf21e341790c05e4bc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1998ebd13056e67974311eecd3d3c24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11f829729d0020581f29820d44e30308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbde9b26d1da0b6d201fb666deeea1af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599508fe86fb4e6ee4dd67e02ddb8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contractors">
      <data key="d0">Contractors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Contractors provide various services off-site and may fall under specific business categories, depending on their operational characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Contractors perform services off-site and are categorized under the Office category if their equipment is not stored on-site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b98f4030f1ba695567caadac80f6cd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Examples of Industrial Services">
      <data key="d0">Examples of Industrial Services</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Examples of Industrial Services include welding shops, machine shops, tool repair, and janitorial services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Utilities Scale Energy Production">
      <data key="d0">Utilities Scale Energy Production</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Utilities Scale Energy Production refers to the large-scale generation of energy, frequently associated with Manufacturing and Production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f68934562aabb1fc36107a5be06cbfcf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781090</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Department of Environmental Quality">
      <data key="d0">Department of Environmental Quality</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Department of Environmental Quality (DEQ) may assist in the review process of applications for helicopter landing facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Department of Environmental Quality (DEQ) oversees environmental regulations and compliance related to noise, vibration, and other impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Department of Environmental Quality is responsible for overseeing the removal or remediation of hazardous substances in designated areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Department of Environmental Quality oversees vehicle emission testing sites as part of environmental regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Department of Environmental Quality oversees requirements for septic systems in certified child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d771f61eac49b01fc5796204c75025ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0faba42bb95011a11cda5b0c9113041e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a901459905390cbd8ce9c02b74a9fd1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ca5fc3d28aa819abc484b86dc468ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c72a172d251d6504ae739472394027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781565</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Noise Control">
      <data key="d0">Noise Control</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Noise Control standards are outlined in Title 18 and regulate acceptable noise levels from different sources to protect sensitive uses.&lt;SEP&gt;Noise Control involves regulations aimed at limiting noise pollution in designated areas, particularly in relation to the operations within the PIR Master Plan district.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d771f61eac49b01fc5796204c75025ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df361d0b769c8729ae58a7e716789b6e</data>
