    <node id="National Register Landmark">
      <data key="d0">National Register Landmark</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A National Register Landmark is a historic site that is formally recognized for its historical significance and subject to review processes for relocation and demolition.&lt;SEP&gt;A National Register Landmark refers to landmarks recognized for their historical value, which can lose their designation if moved.&lt;SEP&gt;A national register landmark is a building or site listed by the federal Keeper of the National Register of Historic Places without local designation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdaeb46ee0afe6f8cbf449de5ce1578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8034fc51f3b39a89498e8a31263eac35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab68c6faa3af9af6f5cd876312e30c7</data>
