    <node id="Demolition Review">
      <data key="d0">Demolition Review</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Demolition Review refers to a regulatory process that is crucial for evaluating the historic value of structures before permits for demolition are granted. This procedure is particularly significant for Conservation Landmarks and contributing resources within designated historic districts. The Demolition Review assesses not only the necessity of demolition but also the implications such actions may have on historic preservation.

The main aim of the Demolition Review is to protect landmarks and historic resources from unnecessary demolition and loss. By evaluating the significance of a resource, the review helps ensure that any potential impacts are thoroughly considered prior to allowing a structure to be demolished. This assessment is required for certain resources classified as contributing within National Register Districts, where the historical context and value play a pivotal role in the decision-making process concerning demolition.

Overall, the Demolition Review is integral to preserving the heritage of communities, ensuring that any modifications or demolitions respect the historical narrative and contribute to the conservation of significant architectural and cultural resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d31ffd348227ba062bb811bffdbe39bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-851e46c6798be63a5ed200499e9b955d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdaeb46ee0afe6f8cbf449de5ce1578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74ebc7af6a19551e094bffa65ccb3a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-992925c33f931f469018e63e676d862e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972d6f8b824b76de1c4e754f5d9f3110</data>
