    <node id="City Forester">
      <data key="d0">City Forester</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The City Forester is a designated authority within the City of Portland, tasked with overseeing urban forestry and executing tree management regulations. This role encompasses a range of responsibilities, including assessing the condition of trees on specified sites and determining whether they pose an immediate danger. As part of their duties, the City Forester provides essential documentation ensuring that trees preserved for Floor Area Ratio (FAR) transfers do not fall under the category of nuisance or dead trees.

In addition to managing assessments and evaluations of tree health and growth, the City Forester collaborates with the City Engineer to approve plans for street tree preservation and planting. This collaboration ensures that both preservation and removal decisions are made responsibly and in alignment with the city’s vegetation regulations. The City Forester plays a crucial role in maintaining the safety and sustainability of the urban forest, as well as contributing to the environmental health of the city’s landscape through informed tree management practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-992f79974821c7d84a0abe4219c3b2b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-899c4b9a2ac9d3d9713b5cef39a863b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40d1cf5d1a59a47e32100e78eb27cf84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c815f0219b3fa08de12163f428266e23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8e044b1fd94ca567e1458bbd0323ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd54e5b638113595ce88bbc6ccf94bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39fbbf35a5a5146ae4034375e7576374</data>
