    <node id="L2 Standard">
      <data key="d0">L2 Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The L2 Standard is a comprehensive regulation outlined in Chapter 33.248 that governs landscaping and screening requirements for development. This standard establishes minimum requirements that developers must adhere to in order to create aesthetically pleasing and functional landscapes, particularly in urban settings.

Specifically, the L2 Standard focuses on landscaping requirements for areas adjacent to certain zones, ensuring that these spaces are visually appealing and harmonize with surrounding developments. It addresses guidelines for the height and screening methods of mechanical equipment to prevent them from being visually intrusive, thus enhancing the overall appearance of the area.

Additionally, the L2 Standard includes provisions for low screen landscaping methods, which employ a combination of distance and low-level screening techniques. This approach aims to soften developmental impacts, especially in zones adjacent to surface parking or urban development.

Moreover, the L2 Standard outlines guidelines pertaining to tree categories and spatial designs, indicating a thorough consideration for greenery and ecological balance within urban environments. Overall, the L2 Standard serves as a crucial regulatory framework that seeks to improve urban landscapes while maintaining functional and aesthetic integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7b2cc8f6a45d17941e977fde3debc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32085ee92ea490a135a4678599552bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deccf49edc8456f9e632a30209a8e62a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f45e86d97574f9fac5d7d012bcae97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d3c1a461749c2773607b44c831a1a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b58865c473bfa9835169ceac4d038b1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f</data>
