    <node id="Parks And Open Areas">
      <data key="d0">Parks And Open Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parks and Open Areas refer to designated recreational and natural spaces that are integral to community planning and public use. They are generally classified under various zoning regulations, such as Single-Dwelling Zones and Open Space Zones, which facilitate their use for recreational activities. These spaces may encompass a range of settings, including parks, gardens, and golf courses, tailored for public enjoyment and recreational activities.

These areas are often recognized for their contribution to enhancing community space and promoting outdoor engagement among residents. They serve as officially designated green spaces intended for recreational use, prioritizing natural landscapes and facilities designed for community activities. However, while Parks and Open Areas are typically allowed by right, their development or alteration may require conditional use reviews, especially for accessory uses.

Furthermore, the classification of Parks and Open Areas includes specific requirements, such as the necessity for parking spaces based on the area’s intended use and capacity for recreational activities. Overall, Parks and Open Areas play a crucial role in urban planning and development by providing accessible, natural spaces for the public to enjoy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809d9f51e6409fec41d4c184732a13b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34de9e34b3c0011d322a8520a1091e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5a24cd6c84e70b31e0e64f3773ddd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028c3c84ee58774048f304cfbc47c40a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e2adfc473177ee34daf0edf44e9fab</data>
