    <node id="Drive-Through Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Drive-Through Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Drive-Through Facilities are designated areas that allow customers to receive goods and services from their vehicles without needing to exit. These facilities incorporate specific designs, including stacking lanes and service areas, to accommodate vehicle access and enhance customer convenience. They function under specified guidelines and zoning regulations aimed at managing their placement and ensuring proper integration within urban development.

In most contexts, Drive-Through Facilities are bound by regulatory terms that govern their operation, including limitations on their location. Such establishments are generally prohibited in pedestrian-oriented districts and in proximity to light rail alignments to minimize congestion and maintain the pedestrian-friendly environment. Additionally, planning regulations may specify that these facilities cannot be positioned within certain distances from public transit routes, further emphasizing their design for automotive use rather than pedestrian access.

Overall, Drive-Through Facilities represent a pragmatic approach to consumer convenience, enabling efficient transactions while simultaneously adhering to zoning provisions that ensure they contribute to orderly urban development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e7aa0bae5c7fef30a568af91c0f05e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1ec40ef0c834d42a666a80a8223118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652d83d3265624b311b9bf8c778fdd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8233be0787d6dbf29673028851524520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78755af7dcf0cbd31bb8a59f246d601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9bdd0a72bd1cfe3ef9d36a7ad4b1bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e52cd6f75c0ef15f81f473a7fd946bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78575afc304e77ddac795549d18c014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6571cdc55e7ba51879f95332dd75ffd</data>
