    <node id="Title 3">
      <data key="d0">Title 3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 3 refers to a legal framework under which environmental violations may be subject to fines.&lt;SEP&gt;Title 3 relates to regulations that may impose fines on individuals or businesses for violations in the permit process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Conservation Zone">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Conservation Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Environmental Conservation Zone allows for urban development while conserving important resources and functional values in designated areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Environmental Conservation Zone is a designated area focused on conserving resources and limiting development to protect functional values.&lt;SEP&gt;The Environmental Conservation Zone is a designated area aimed at preserving resources and functional values, requiring impact evaluations for developments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Environmental Conservation Zone is designated for land use that requires specific protection standards for environmental resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The Environmental Conservation Zone is a designated area where specific regulations apply for the protection of resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fec75523a13dc705f1116777ea0ce94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b463643e19fbf1a7684090d0b63adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a90d16f519debce0d1b06def34f6932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9914c8cd6c5cbc27ea6f25de34c9dfa5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Development Permit">
      <data key="d0">Development Permit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Development Permit is necessary for proposed developments, particularly those within Environmental Zones, to meet specific standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A Development Permit is required for certain construction projects and is granted based on regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;A Development Permit is required for applications dealing with land development under specified guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;A development permit is an authorization required for construction or development activities within certain regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285f052019746f5b49b63ae041c898aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f5238f416f69c282caa09bc226ffbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af7b62435ab8aaa0e29e89b645a23e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Permit Application Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Permit Application Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Permit Application Requirements refer to the necessary documentation and information needed to apply for a building or development permit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393312325b82278116f59418428cf4e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scenic Resource Zone">
      <data key="d0">Scenic Resource Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Scenic Resource Zone designates areas recognized for their visual beauty that require protection and management.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scenic Resource Zone is an area where specific standards for tree removal and planting are enforced to protect visual and environmental qualities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scenic Resource Zone is a designated area intended to protect significant scenic resources in Portland, enhancing its appearance and economic vitality.&lt;SEP&gt;Scenic Resource Zone outlines guidelines for development and landscaping to preserve scenic character along identified corridors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-659ec42acd09493cb815e59e2193d7bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-877a823bd216070dbe9fd06f8befc552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a90d16f519debce0d1b06def34f6932</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="City Arts Program">
      <data key="d0">City Arts Program</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The City Arts Program is an organized entity responsible for the regulation, approval, and maintenance of public art installations within the city. This program plays a critical role in ensuring that all artworks comply with city regulations and related covenants, fostering a vibrant urban artistic landscape.

The City Arts Program oversees the approval of both artists and specific works of art intended for public display, which includes installation projects associated with urban development. By doing so, the program not only facilitates the presentation of artistic expressions in public spaces but also ensures that these artworks align with community standards and regulations.

Additionally, the City Arts Program is tasked with nominating qualified members to the Design Commission, particularly individuals with experience in public art. This involvement highlights the program's commitment to integrating knowledgeable voices into the regulatory process, thus promoting informed decision-making in the approval of public art installations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b04cb33b3135ed3ccce916cd1c14a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c96a1e5b1eb94f3a586e5986daa73c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2020f8cb9e1e9fff0f2699c2142d64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7282e754cd453819f3e67c09c8e7a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639e5332d0e90ed7ad51bb327c530214</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.480">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.480</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.480 establishes standards for scenic corridors, focusing on preserving scenic vistas and limiting certain types of development.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.480 addresses the Scenic Resource Zone regulations, detailing applications and standards for preserving scenic views in Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-659ec42acd09493cb815e59e2193d7bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-877a823bd216070dbe9fd06f8befc552</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Section 33.430.140">
      <data key="d0">Section 33.430.140</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.430.140 pertains to development standards to which the comments addressed by the Director of PP&amp;D are related.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e362e6c3818ce32276e136b8d6e3bbc</data>
