      <data key="d0">Powell Butte / Mt. Scott Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Powell Butte / Mt. Scott Plan District is another area within city planning that is referenced regarding zoning and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e362e6c3818ce32276e136b8d6e3bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="West Delta Park">
      <data key="d0">West Delta Park</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">West Delta Park is a natural area with a unique character and is part of the PIR plan district that serves multiple purposes, including recreation and environmental protection.&lt;SEP&gt;West Delta Park is a transition area that connects natural environments to developed spaces, providing opportunities for outdoor recreation and preserving environmental qualities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e362e6c3818ce32276e136b8d6e3bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd02a036b3524dda605ba42dd4a99988</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Land Use Hearings Officer">
      <data key="d0">Land Use Hearings Officer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Land Use Hearings Officer reviews applications for the Northwest Master Plan and can approve, deny, or apply conditions to the plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Land Use Hearings Officer conducts quasi-judicial reviews of land use applications, allowing for prompt decision-making on land use issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6848b70101fce6283f62065768fd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa5d2c57a95ae65f663a55f78fa3c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Director of Portland Permitting &amp; Development">
      <data key="d0">Director of Portland Permitting &amp; Development</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Director of PP&amp;D oversees the staff and operations of the Portland Permitting &amp; Development office, ensuring compliance with city regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6848b70101fce6283f62065768fd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="City Auditor">
      <data key="d0">City Auditor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The City Auditor is responsible for filing the revocation decision related to land use approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is responsible for filing and receiving guarantees associated with land use approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is responsible for appointing the Land Use Hearings Officer in conformance with city rules.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is responsible for scheduling public hearings and mailing notices regarding the appeal decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is responsible for mailing the notice of the final decision to relevant parties after the review body’s action.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is a local government official involved in the process of receiving written requests for notice related to land use actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Auditor is responsible for scheduling public hearings in compliance with city regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6848b70101fce6283f62065768fd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6359633c178583bad809c59ed226cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0de2e33b17c8bed0fb16624ad72fab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa32294cb8855f6032b144b5ecb04092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f231106269a74d76750e77d25977faa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bde6fb397c7366841124f779d183b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc65f441d5b262a6e985063f42142907</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Guarantees">
      <data key="d0">Performance Guarantees</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance guarantees are assurances required for compliance with construction project regulations and standards."&lt;SEP&gt;Performance guarantees are requirements that applicants must meet to ensure that improvements are completed as specified in development plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Guarantees are conditions that must be met for construction, monitoring, and maintenance of mitigation sites prior to permit issuance.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Guarantees are requirements that may be imposed on applicants as a condition of land use approval to ensure compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Guarantees are conditions set by the Director of PP&amp;D to ensure compliance with mitigation or remediation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a3e7000b47e86fb0ceb843165c824c66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6359633c178583bad809c59ed226cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7822437163e35b6c56d5560ac87ff1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a2edce75cc1c84e8d78d82be31fd43b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f9cce1f67d8125895ea396b1acc241</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781095</data>
