      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CX Zone">
      <data key="d0">CX Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The CX Zone is a defined commercial/mixed-use zoning classification characterized by specific regulations and limitations affecting land use, development, and architectural standards. This zoning area is subject to height and Floor Area Ratio (FAR) limitations, which can vary based on the specific use and development type, allowing for potential height and FAR adjustments.

Within the CX Zone, certain industrial uses are permitted, aligning closely with limitations found in the CM2 Zone. This classification supports commercial activities and permits the exterior display of goods, albeit under certain restrictions to maintain aesthetic and functional integrity. Additionally, it imposes landscaping requirements during demolition activities, ensuring that development adheres to environmental and visual standards.

The CX Zone also establishes essential guidelines for ground floor window placement and related architectural standards, promoting urban activity and interaction at the street level. It serves as a regulatory framework for new development projects and significant remodeling efforts, clearly defining the parameters within which developers must operate.

As a commercial mixed-use zoning designation, the CX Zone plays a vital role in urban planning and development, facilitating a blend of residential, commercial, and potentially light industrial use, while ensuring that growth occurs in an organized and sustainable manner. It is also notably referenced in the approval criteria for Planned Developments, underscoring its importance in the city’s overall zoning landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aa735bcf86b8023079cfc5ea6f84da6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ceb0639cc3b4b602e0b2c747a13e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247549d54269808af0150d94edb52c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0460f02d0e013f6aa12de53db834a01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f458c7c4b1b1f282fce4511ff8dc00f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b4c57adc2cf94d9a0a99114828453df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9a5a4577f7544b4671be7b0e59a2ab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781096</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prohibited Uses">
      <data key="d0">Prohibited Uses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prohibited Uses are activities or structures that are not allowed under specific zoning regulations and are listed in zoning tables.&lt;SEP&gt;Prohibited uses are activities listed with an "N" in Table 130-1 that are not allowed within certain zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Prohibited Uses are specific activities and services that are not allowed within certain areas of the Marquam Hill Plan District, as defined in the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fab78bf22476f90e50de5d511279727d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2474dfd41e2575d0e3e9c1417c737dbb</data>
