    <node id="Roof-Type Reference Point">
      <data key="d0">Roof-Type Reference Point</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Roof-Type Reference Point is a measurement point used to determine the height of various types of roofs in building regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gabled Roof">
      <data key="d0">Gabled Roof</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Gabled Roof is a type of roof measured to the average height of the gable for building height regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Measuring Height">
      <data key="d0">Measuring Height</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Measuring Height refers to the method of determining the vertical distance of various structures, including buildings and fences, from the ground.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Height of Other Structures">
      <data key="d0">Height of Other Structures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Height of Other Structures is the measurement from ground level to the top of structures like flag poles and fences, excluding exempted portions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Deck Height">
      <data key="d0">Deck Height</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deck Height is determined by measuring the distance from the ground to the top of the deck floor or the railing, depending on specific criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Average Slope">
      <data key="d0">Average Slope</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Average Slope represents the gradient of a lot calculated based on the elevation differences at the corners of the lot.&lt;SEP&gt;Average slope is calculated using the elevations at the corners of a lot, determining the incline of the land.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6feb38e3d4faebf120b7cf1e9165848c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a421dc7c5c5ed797ef20bf18c33cb13c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Structures">
      <data key="d0">Primary Structures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary structures refer to the main buildings allowed to be developed on certain lots based on specific regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-606354f765e28b95d29b753fc9fe43fd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 110-3">
      <data key="d0">Table 110-3</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 110-3 outlines the minimum lot size requirements for different zoning classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adjustments">
      <data key="d0">Adjustments</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Adjustments refer to modifications allowed under specific regulations pertaining to lot sizes and development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjustments refer to modifications allowed regarding requirements such as lot area and height, although certain adjustments are prohibited after specific dates.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjustments refer to modifications permitted under specific conditions regarding site dimensions and density standards for cottage clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjustments refer to modifications made to land use applications or requirements based on specific circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c2d80fd8407d1e9806e03445c7d0a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee4ba726d698227e002aae5c6cc82e38</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lots">
      <data key="d0">Lots</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lots refer to parcels of land that are subject to development regulations under the planning and zoning ordinances.&lt;SEP&gt;Lots refer to parcels of land with specific characteristics, including average slope and elevation differences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95645a65574ce270cd08fff187fbb27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825dcc9caa885b9e5aef8f2ccbaf183d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 266-4">
      <data key="d0">Table 266-4</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 266-4 provides minimum parking space and aisle dimensions as part of the regulations for parking area layouts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Figure 266-3">
      <data key="d0">Figure 266-3</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Figure 266-3 illustrates how a landscaped area may be included at the front of a parking space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
