    <node id="Tree Canopy">
      <data key="d0">Tree Canopy</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Tree Canopy refers to the shade provided by trees, which must cover at least 40 percent of a parking area as per new standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Tree Canopy refers to the layer of leaves and branches formed by the crowns of trees, which must shade at least 40 percent of a parking area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc01e5a62a9dbd8bf10a560a6ed844cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Solar Panels">
      <data key="d0">Solar Panels</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Solar Panels are required to generate at least 0.5 kilowatts per parking space in new parking area developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar Panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity, required to generate at least 0.5 kilowatts per parking space at a site.&lt;SEP&gt;Roof mounted solar panels that can extend above the height limit depending on their placement on flat or pitched roofs.&lt;SEP&gt;Solar panels are devices that convert sunlight into electricity and are proposed as an option for new buildings with residential use in certain zones until January 1, 2029.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc01e5a62a9dbd8bf10a560a6ed844cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7896cc3191620f9cfec1d8626e62a156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71ef8e763b48167f014ebc29d2564293</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parking Area Layouts">
      <data key="d0">Parking Area Layouts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking Area Layouts refer to the design considerations for access to parking spaces, dimensions, and required features such as maneuvering areas and landscaping.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimum Dimensions">
      <data key="d0">Minimum Dimensions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimum Dimensions specify the required sizes for parking spaces and aisles as per the regulations outlined in Table 266-4.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Disabled Person Parking Standards">
      <data key="d0">Disabled Person Parking Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Disabled Person Parking Standards pertain to the regulations governing the access and dimensions of parking spaces allocated for disabled persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc6b437da193232c09faa03338cb2957</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alternative Design Density Overlay Zone">
      <data key="d0">Alternative Design Density Overlay Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Alternative Design Density Overlay Zone is a zoning specification added to regulate design density in urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f2e828d0ef40701ea87d62c0b01bd2f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
