    <node id="Residential Development">
      <data key="d0">Residential Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential Development encompasses guidelines and standards for constructing living spaces in designated areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential Development encompasses zoning classifications and standards aimed at housing construction and maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential development refers to the construction and growth of housing to accommodate various households.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5555f01efc47b9ad220ce985153f9292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Underground Parking">
      <data key="d0">Underground Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Underground parking is a strategy encouraged through bonus options to maximize land usage while minimizing surface disruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Underground Parking refers to vehicle parking structures located below ground level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7a46ce2a41072cf8f503e930128f86</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="I-405 Freeway">
      <data key="d0">I-405 Freeway</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">I-405 Freeway is a transportation route in the region, which influences building regulations and development plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bonus Options">
      <data key="d0">Bonus Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bonus Options are provisions that allow developers to increase building height and floor area in exchange for contributions or compliance with certain housing regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bonus options provide additional allowances for building height, density, and parking in exchange for specific development commitments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2c7926ceca17c4d0d7614d1c8acec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bonus Floor Area">
      <data key="d0">Bonus Floor Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bonus Floor Area refers to additional floor area allowed as an incentive for developments that provide community benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Bonus Floor Area is additional space allocated in building projects that may require public benefits in exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;Bonus floor area refers to additional allowable building volume that can be earned through various incentive programs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c07c29cf0579682841d3d14fca9fead2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d0e3bbe363516aa161846014338967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-753992cd5e3f8a1085d378bbba8d5aab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
