    <node id="Residential Dwelling Unit">
      <data key="d0">Residential Dwelling Unit</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A residential dwelling unit is defined living space where certain bicycle parking provisions apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac9c74456e021e6800b45f3d57ae1aea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expedited Land Division">
      <data key="d0">Expedited Land Division</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Expedited Land Division is a streamlined administrative procedure designed to facilitate the division of land parcels with enhanced efficiency. This process focuses on simplifying the Review of Preliminary Plans, enabling local governments to process land division decisions and appeals more quickly. 

The Expedited Land Division operates under specific regulatory guidelines dictated by state regulations, particularly the Oregon Revised Statutes (ORS). It allows for public notice requirements to be observed without necessitating a formal hearing, contributing to its expedited nature. This makes the process not only faster but also more accessible for stakeholders involved in land division.

In essence, Expedited Land Division serves as a specialized mechanism that adjusts traditional land division procedures to meet urgent needs while ensuring compliance with established regulations. It offers a coherent pathway for local governments to undertake land divisions efficiently and effectively, potentially varying in requirements and processing times compared to standard land division practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d7961ce66e26136990bb4bb54c838e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e86c208ee49379750e080df5cf9722&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219169bf18bf9f73b3370be8bd44ed1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e988f81291359d27584c02f5af917de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2546da1b6188ab781e1777780334eb3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781097</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bicycle Parking Fund">
      <data key="d0">Bicycle Parking Fund</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bicycle Parking Fund is a financial resource collected by the Bureau of Transportation to enhance bicycle parking facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bicycle Parking Fund is a financial resource collected and administered by the Bureau of Transportation for the purpose of installing bicycle parking and improvements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac9c74456e021e6800b45f3d57ae1aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78b8d8f5df1d607fc21562bc53c145e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Short-Term Bicycle Parking">
      <data key="d0">Short-Term Bicycle Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Short-Term Bicycle Parking refers to facilities located in publicly accessible areas intended for visitors to buildings for brief durations.&lt;SEP&gt;Short-term bicycle parking pertains to facilities designed for temporary bicycle storage, generally located close to entrances.&lt;SEP&gt;Short-term bicycle parking serves visitors who generally stay for a short time and can include shoppers and customers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac9c74456e021e6800b45f3d57ae1aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bcd05068dc776f6a4ff3953570df7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad3df252c10f7d3d9869375a3dd70b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electrical Outlet Requirement">
      <data key="d0">Electrical Outlet Requirement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The electrical outlet requirement specifies that certain bicycle parking spaces must have accessible electrical sockets for charging.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac9c74456e021e6800b45f3d57ae1aea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mitigation and Restoration Plantings">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation and Restoration Plantings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mitigation and Restoration Plantings refers to practices aimed at restoring and enhancing vegetation in urban settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation and Restoration Plantings refer to plans aimed at offsetting significant detrimental impacts from development on functional values of water quality resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Construction Management Plan">
      <data key="d0">Construction Management Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Construction Management Plan details measures to protect resources during construction and remediation, ensuring minimal disturbance to the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A Construction Management Plan is a strategy that outlines measures to protect functional values during construction or remediation activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Construction Management Plan outlines measures to protect resources during construction or remediation activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The construction management plan outlines measures to protect resources and functional values during construction or remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Construction Management Plan outlines measures to protect natural and scenic resources during construction activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51dc10f7cf6f3ff9bea2eb170cf1c4dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b0bd3b13a0c05d569d6126ad180bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mitigation or Remediation Plan">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation or Remediation Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Mitigation or Remediation Plan outlines strategies to compensate for unavoidable significant detrimental impacts caused by development or violations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Mitigation or Remediation Plan describes strategies to counteract significant detrimental impacts resulting from development alternatives.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mitigation or Remediation Plan is designed to compensate for significant detrimental impacts resulting from development alternatives or violations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mitigation or Remediation Plan aims to compensate for significant detrimental impacts on natural resources resulting from development actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b0bd3b13a0c05d569d6126ad180bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4fc40bc0c1ae23128f4ba53742ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lower Willamette River Wildlife Habitat Inventory">
      <data key="d0">Lower Willamette River Wildlife Habitat Inventory</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">The Lower Willamette River Wildlife Habitat Inventory provides habitat rankings for wildlife in the riverbank areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lower Willamette River Wildlife Habitat Inventory provides rankings and assessments of habitat quality in areas along the riverbank.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad1968bb57e3baa2ecd3350abe6caf0</data>
