    </node>
    <node id="Final Plat Approval">
      <data key="d0">Final Plat Approval</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Final Plat Approval is an event marking the formal acceptance of land division plans by relevant authorities before development.&lt;SEP&gt;Final Plat Approval is the confirmation required for new land divisions after a preliminary plan has been reviewed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09653fd8cb264cda4f3441bd478fe017</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planned Unit Development (PUD)">
      <data key="d0">Planned Unit Development (PUD)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Planned Unit Development is a type of land development that allows for more flexible land use and site planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a zoning designation that allows for flexible development designs and is subject to specific regulations and approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Unit Development is a type of development that allows for a mix of uses and is subject to approvals that do not expire under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e5352641a4a29255f045f1ffa49de30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2546da1b6188ab781e1777780334eb3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
