    <node id="Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals">
      <data key="d0">Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals fall under other categories with specific usage allowances in Single-Dwelling Zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals are facilities for accommodating passengers in transportation systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals are facilities for passenger and freight movement, subject to specific approval criteria concerning their impacts on land use.&lt;SEP&gt;Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals include facilities for the landing and takeoff of flying vehicles and related passenger services.&lt;SEP&gt;Aviation And Surface Passenger Terminals are facilities supporting transportation by air and other surface means.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e255ad4213c8ff69b61a260e064f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6144b313ccb84dbccd73dbf4dd1e5c6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial/Mixed Use 1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">Commercial/Mixed Use 1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commercial/Mixed Use 1 Zone (CM1) is a small-scale zone intended for mixed-use development in lower density residential areas and neighborhood corridors.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commercial/Mixed Use 1 Zone (CM1) allows for mixed commercial and residential activities in diverse neighborhoods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial/Mixed Use 2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">Commercial/Mixed Use 2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commercial/Mixed Use 2 Zone (CM2) is a medium-scale zone designed for a variety of centers with frequent transit service, allowing a mix of commercial and residential uses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commercial/Mixed Use 2 Zone (CM2) offers regulatory guidelines for mixed use developments across varied urban contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial/Mixed Use 3 Zone">
      <data key="d0">Commercial/Mixed Use 3 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commercial/Mixed Use 3 Zone (CM3) is a large-scale zone for high-capacity transit areas, allowing diverse commercial and residential uses with a focus on urban development.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commercial/Mixed Use 3 Zone (CM3) is designed for larger development intents combining commercial and residential spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial Employment Zone">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Employment Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commercial Employment Zone (CE) allows a mix of commercial uses along higher traffic corridors and emphasizes commercial development with some residential options.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commercial Employment Zone (CE) prioritizes areas for job creation and business activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Central Commercial Zone">
      <data key="d0">Central Commercial Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Central Commercial Zone (CX) is intended for high-intensity commercial and mixed-use development in Portland's Central City and Gateway Regional Center.&lt;SEP&gt;The Central Commercial Zone (CX) is focused on high-intensity commercial activities in urban centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2479ef8bb8da38cfb1bfe208f9246ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.251">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.251</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.251 discusses planning and zoning regulations governing manufactured homes and parks, including development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.251 refers to a section of regulations that pertains to planning, zoning, manufactured homes, and manufactured dwelling parks.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 33.251 sets forth the development standards specific to Manufactured Homes and Manufactured Dwelling Parks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-083abb85def98a799fa4d4f0c3d8ab61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41abaceb8097519bba26a5ccb4274c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc6ceed3be738324a1eb3f18282ffbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922c2152929ae106e2a8f4d1e7a324cf</data>
