    <node id="National Register District">
      <data key="d0">National Register District</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A National Register District is a designated area recognized for its historical significance, subject to specific regulations for resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;A National Register District is a designated area where historic resources are recognized for their significance and are subject to specific regulations regarding development and demolition.&lt;SEP&gt;National Register District is an area that includes historic resources recognized for their significance on a national level.&lt;SEP&gt;A national register district is a district listed by the federal Keeper of the National Register of Historic Places without local designation.&lt;SEP&gt;A National Register District is a district listed by the federal Keeper of the National Register of Historic that has not been designated by the City as a Historic District or Conservation District.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-505f218cdd094bc3f7a968cd178d268b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23ded3ed670f5e7749c36c4406da450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8034fc51f3b39a89498e8a31263eac35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41bf3bf1621f4152946908d459e677ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tree">
      <data key="d0">Tree</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Tree refers to a natural plant with a trunk that provides shade and aesthetic value in landscaping.&lt;SEP&gt;A tree is a natural object that may need removal based on specific conditions outlined in the regulations, such as being dead, dying, or dangerous.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ca2fc1b73b6e1ae4e82cbaf205ce719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3fdad639580e09c9504162fba29af8</data>
