    <node id="Facade Articulation">
      <data key="d0">Facade Articulation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Facade Articulation refers to the design standards aimed at breaking up building facades to enhance visual interest and architectural variety.&lt;SEP&gt;Facade Articulation standards promote visual diversity and structural character by dictating design elements of building facades.&lt;SEP&gt;Facade Articulation is a standard requiring that street-facing facades meet specific design criteria to enhance visual interest.&lt;SEP&gt;Facade articulation pertains to design standards regulating the visual aspects of building facades in zoning areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Facade Articulation refers to the design standards concerning the aesthetic aspects of campus buildings, focusing on how they interact with public spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Facade Articulation refers to the design requirement that facades must have certain offsets to enhance visual interest and variety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dce4a7be57273a9865cad046f69ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd63fde7af35a2611f3f81cc2e72e533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f45e86d97574f9fac5d7d012bcae97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2574af8787db7883bc15da7cbabd3a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639e5332d0e90ed7ad51bb327c530214</data>
