    <node id="Community Gardens">
      <data key="d0">Community Gardens</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Community Gardens serve as shared spaces for growing produce with regulations focusing on sales and area constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Community gardens are shared plots for personal food production, supported by regulations to enhance community interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Community Gardens are allowed on school sites, focusing on sustainable gardening practices for community engagement.&lt;SEP&gt;Community gardens are shared spaces within recreational areas where residents grow plants and vegetables, mentioned within the context of development standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50ff07d99a0c758d3b51f7e05d950738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52cbe23eb8de6a4318808cef3ac4f682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-552034cbee7413e9d44334c40a7cb832&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41bc0f6125b16239a39dfeccb2bc43f</data>
