    <node id="Residential Structure Types">
      <data key="d0">Residential Structure Types</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential Structure Types refer to various forms of housing that comply with specific zoning regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential Structure Types encompass various forms of housing units outlined in the Planning and Zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential Structure Types include classifications like Duplex and Dwelling Unit that define housing types within zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential structure types include various forms of housing, such as manufactured dwellings and traditional houses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a5ea5fe5eea40eab34623aa7e60f482&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142263ca6fb69f507db833e40c26eab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028c3c84ee58774048f304cfbc47c40a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94d2f2ba51a73a23de500a4e54b5f682</data>
