    <node id="Religious Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Religious Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Religious Institutions are defined as organizations or establishments dedicated to spiritual and religious activities, serving as places of worship for various faith communities. They play a vital role in providing meeting areas for religious gatherings and associated community activities, often facilitating a broad range of religious practices.

In the context of urban planning and zoning regulations, Religious Institutions are recognized as permitted active uses within Single-Dwelling Zones. Their establishment contributes to community services and is subject to specific zoning guidelines, including designated parking space requirements that depend on the size of their assembly areas and building area. This categorization underscores their importance and recognition within municipal frameworks, allowing them to operate effectively while adhering to local regulations.

Overall, Religious Institutions are pivotal in fostering spiritual engagement and community cohesion, embodying both a physical space for worship and a community service hub.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5cc02978e3319b39c1038d83f233d71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7a3faa53abe19fba4ba510e5addfc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5758ac5ffbd319aede8587861c56d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34de9e34b3c0011d322a8520a1091e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e255ad4213c8ff69b61a260e064f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d22ee5e42bbb3db37d28f3801d3229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4551ce1e7653dda2331ab8ba0712bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d760ad8fe7df68e6c9eb96417c57c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028c3c84ee58774048f304cfbc47c40a</data>
