    <node id="Conditional Uses">
      <data key="d0">Conditional Uses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Conditional Uses refer to land use permissions that necessitate specific approval through a review process prior to being allowed. This concept encompasses particular types of developments or activities that can only be permitted under defined conditions or additional requirements, as outlined in various chapters and zoning regulations. Conditional Uses represent not just permissions but also regulations relevant to how land is developed and utilized, ensuring that designated land activities align with community standards and do not pose adverse effects.

These uses are critical components of urban planning, requiring a thorough evaluation against certain criteria before they can be approved. Typically, Conditional Uses may involve practices or developments that, while potentially beneficial, necessitate oversight due to their possible impacts on the surrounding environment and community. Furthermore, in specific zoning areas, such as Subdistricts A through D of the Marquam Hill Plan District regulations, Conditional Uses are delineated by more particularized criteria.

Conditional Uses serve as a regulatory measure that allows for flexibility in land use while protecting community interests. By requiring these uses to adhere to certain conditions, municipalities aim to mitigate adverse outcomes and ensure that development aligns with broader planning goals. Overall, the concept of Conditional Uses is pivotal in the realm of zoning regulations, facilitating a balanced approach to land development and usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fab78bf22476f90e50de5d511279727d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8df1a5c0d5ee049ecbdb2f03fc22c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78724ed583edac4d2f2940a886eda8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2474dfd41e2575d0e3e9c1417c737dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a05752417b511c6e703a9f6b6aac007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f47b636277f1f82c9c5a27142d87d13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc3ba891360a2a54cb8bbb9f425464c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f2df84aea0e28175d739f9e39d7ac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d28f6febcf4de65239d0203f2197382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12fb6a1cf486f1a95c94d657ea8ccfeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781101</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guilds Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District">
      <data key="d0">Guilds Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District focuses on the industrial use and zoning of the Guild's Lake area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District is a designated area aimed at preserving industrial activity adjacent to Portland’s central city.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District is an area outlined in zoning regulations emphasizing industrial character and development standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District is a designated area with specific regulations to preserve its suitability for industrial uses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District denotes a zoning area relevant to conditional uses in Chapter 33.815.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guild’s Lake Industrial Sanctuary Plan District is a designated area where specific regulations apply to industrial operations and development proposals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd5e24f7c98b2b609a3ed6656b608420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f47b636277f1f82c9c5a27142d87d13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61687599149060b1e058a26bfd55caee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d66ea593dc4ac52ad4236580e597c48b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12fb6a1cf486f1a95c94d657ea8ccfeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0147b437f8af7c9b75d571f1f8e2392</data>
