    <node id="River Bank Complexity">
      <data key="d0">River Bank Complexity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">River Bank Complexity refers to a combination of conditions along a river shore that enhances its ecological diversity and habitat.&lt;SEP&gt;River bank complexity describes the varied conditions present along riverbanks that influence aquatic and terrestrial habitats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7aa2e9895420bcb5392c9333db8bab4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781103</data>
