    <node id="Accessory Short-Term Rentals">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Short-Term Rentals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessory Short-Term Rentals involve regulations for renting out residential units on a short-term basis.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Short-Term Rentals are temporary lodging options that may require a conditional use review under zoning laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory short-term rentals refer to residential units where individuals or families rent out bedrooms to guests for fewer than 30 consecutive days.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory short-term rentals refer to rental arrangements that allow homeowners to rent their space to short-term guests, typically regulated by zoning laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessory Short-Term Rentals are defined in Chapter 33.207, outlining regulations for renting out properties temporarily.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9130a83a79296ac327e3b931ef6f9c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11fb000daddf2f11413b9c98892fc17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2215c0dede8ee98027b1212757bd97af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825dcc9caa885b9e5aef8f2ccbaf183d</data>
