    <node id="Common Green">
      <data key="d0">Common Green</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Common greens are landscaped areas that provide access for pedestrians and bicycles without motor vehicle access, serving as open space amenities.&lt;SEP&gt;Common green refers to a classification tied to street types, indicating communal natural spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;A common green is a street designed for pedestrian and bicycle access while restricting vehicle access, functioning as a community space.</data>
