    <node id="Maximum FAR">
      <data key="d0">Maximum FAR</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum FAR defines the maximum floor area ratio allowed for buildings in different zoning categories, influencing building density and design.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum Floor Area Ratio (FAR) is defined as 1.2 to 1, imposing limits on the total allowable building area relative to the lot size.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum floor area ratio (FAR) is a measure of building density defined in Title 33 planning documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum Floor Area Ratio (FAR) specifies the maximum allowed built area in relation to the site area within zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b8e38ccecc8aee043d4f983d468a91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee4ba726d698227e002aae5c6cc82e38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2574af8787db7883bc15da7cbabd3a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c01837a01a91075eb01c907ccb32c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27242cf75127df0f7d45a0655595e417</data>
