    <node id="Review Body">
      <data key="d0">Review Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Review Body is a pivotal entity tasked with evaluating and approving applications related to land use, particularly regarding greenway reviews. It is responsible for ensuring that these applications comply with established criteria and applicable regulations. As part of its function, the Review Body hears new requests within a reconsideration process and conducts public hearings to gather evidence and perspectives relevant to the cases at hand.

In addition to assessing greenway applications, the Review Body addresses a broader range of zoning matters. It makes determinations on appeals and other related decisions, showcasing its critical role in the regulatory landscape of land use. This entity operates as a committee or panel, consisting of various individuals or groups such as commissions and councils, each contributing to the decision-making process based on comprehensive evaluations of presented information.

The Review Body also evaluates conditional use master plans, ensuring adherence to defined standards and criteria. In summary, it functions both as a deliberative body conducting public hearings and as a decision-making authority integral to the governance of land use, balancing community needs with regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d6359633c178583bad809c59ed226cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1723045914c4b67577d06510a65e499e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4206e3cd861a4b477fd8fedb965c2584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa32294cb8855f6032b144b5ecb04092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cad83ae88a9187d47c9acf881162cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a414888338825a53493117bb9837d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e988f81291359d27584c02f5af917de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bde6fb397c7366841124f779d183b6c</data>
