    <node id="Subdistricts C and D">
      <data key="d0">Subdistricts C and D</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Subdistricts C and D are designated areas where existing parking can be reconfigured or demolished exempt from certain requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Subdistricts C and D are areas defined by zoning regulations that follow base zone floor area bonus regulations with specific additional options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d36b64a92b4e219eb8b81cf9934efff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e6e0a14b42f25e67a43e11831d8486</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inclusionary Housing Bonus">
      <data key="d0">Inclusionary Housing Bonus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Inclusionary Housing Bonus is a specific FAR bonus option outlined in Subparagraph 33.510.205.C.2.a.&lt;SEP&gt;Inclusionary Housing Bonus is a zoning incentive that allows extra floor area for developments that include affordable housing units.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d36b64a92b4e219eb8b81cf9934efff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e8e418ed77b8672d2e0bbc7d7689df</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planned Development Bonus">
      <data key="d0">Planned Development Bonus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Planned Development Bonus refers to an allowance within zoning regulations that may grant additional height and FAR for certain developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned Development Bonus is a zoning option that allows certain benefits for larger site developments following specific guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d36b64a92b4e219eb8b81cf9934efff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Floor Area Bonus Options">
      <data key="d0">Floor Area Bonus Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Floor area bonus options represent additional development potential gained for projects that include specified features.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Area Bonus Options refers to zoning regulations that allow increases in floor area under specific conditions in the context of urban planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d36b64a92b4e219eb8b81cf9934efff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93214ee5c49fbb5384175df60c9eafe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Overall Maximum FAR with Bonus">
      <data key="d0">Overall Maximum FAR with Bonus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Overall Maximum FAR with Bonus outlines the maximum Floor Area Ratio allowable with bonus options in Subdistricts, as specified in zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d36b64a92b4e219eb8b81cf9934efff</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
