    <node id="Street-Facing Building Facades">
      <data key="d0">Street-Facing Building Facades</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Street-facing building facades are the outward-facing walls of a building that can affect configuration and zoning compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Street Lot Line Setbacks">
      <data key="d0">Street Lot Line Setbacks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Street lot line setbacks are regulations dictating the distance between the structures and the street lot line to ensure adequate space and privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zoning Standards">
      <data key="d0">Zoning Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Zoning standards are regulations that define how land can be used and what structures can be built in certain areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Zoning Standards encompass the regulations and requirements established for the development and placement of structures, including those for Radio Frequency Transmission Facilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ba8ca0ee507a65dfd09ccd9194cfe1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R10 through R2.5 Zones">
      <data key="d0">R10 through R2.5 Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R10 through R2.5 Zones refer to specific residential zoning classifications with distinct building and setback requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Porch">
      <data key="d0">Porch</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A porch is an external structure at the main entrance of a dwelling, which must meet certain size and design specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;A porch is a structure that can be part of a primary structure, requiring specific design standards regarding size and placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-606354f765e28b95d29b753fc9fe43fd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Landscaped Buffer Area">
      <data key="d0">Landscaped Buffer Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A landscaped buffer area is a designated green space around a flag lot intended to separate it from neighboring properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c39c2445529fc5f3c446d8b193bcf5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mass Shelter">
      <data key="d0">Mass Shelter</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mass Shelter denotes types of larger temporary accommodations that can be classified as an allowed use or conditional use based on compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass shelter refers to a facility offering open sleeping areas without individual bedrooms, managed by public or non-profit organizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass Shelter refers to a type of shelter accommodating many individuals, typically managed during emergency situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass shelter denotes facilities providing accommodation without individual rooms.&lt;SEP&gt;A mass shelter is a temporary facility providing accommodation for individuals in need, typically operated by public or non-profit agencies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad3df252c10f7d3d9869375a3dd70b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9588cab79f107d9108d8259469c3e906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0278556ab1bb29e843d8346fe04d58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C, E, and CI2 Zones">
      <data key="d0">C, E, and CI2 Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">C, E, and CI2 Zones are specific zoning classifications where short term shelters are allowed under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OS and I Zones">
      <data key="d0">OS and I Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">OS and I Zones are specific zoning classifications where short term shelters are prohibited.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exemption for Domestic Violence Shelters">
      <data key="d0">Exemption for Domestic Violence Shelters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The exemption allows shelters specifically serving victims of sexual or domestic violence to operate in certain zones without special review.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RM1-RMP, CI, and IR Zones">
      <data key="d0">RM1-RMP, CI, and IR Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">RM1-RMP, CI, and IR Zones are designated areas where shelters for victims of violence may operate by right.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RF-R2.5 Zones">
      <data key="d0">RF-R2.5 Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">RF-R2.5 Zones are a type of zoning where specific limitations apply for shelters serving victims of violence with a cap on building area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expansion of Net Building Area">
      <data key="d0">Expansion of Net Building Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Expansion of Net Building Area refers to the increase in the physical space occupied by a shelter, regulated under certain conditions depending on the type of shelter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9b6bab9ce7b032e19e3926b9ed2fd8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quality and Resilience Standards">
      <data key="d0">Quality and Resilience Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality and Resilience Standards outline guidelines for creating functional, adaptable buildings and site designs that enhance livability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="On-site Common Areas">
      <data key="d0">On-site Common Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">On-site Common Areas are designated spaces within a development that serve as shared outdoor locations for residents or users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1643cca9962c7d0ac7fc6f08d56ed54</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Covers">
      <data key="d0">Covers</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Covers refer to protective layers or fixtures that can be associated with pipes in ventilation systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Architectural Features">
      <data key="d0">Architectural Features</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Architectural features refer to required design elements on primary structures that enhance their appearance and character.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural features include elements like windows, doors, and cornices that are considered in the placement of vents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1abf9c5e7468a8aa27d8da7b65c0352</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fire Escapes">
      <data key="d0">Fire Escapes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fire escapes are emergency exit routes designed for safety, which must also adhere to distance regulations from streets.&lt;SEP&gt;Fire escapes need to be positioned at least 40 feet from all streets according to the established regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fire escapes are emergency exits from buildings that can be modified or removed following safety regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3722780cf7d6963b782ca94662383bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9e945a4de0eb93decd93ac5bbc54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b729b503408753bfb450541d299ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Guarantee">
      <data key="d0">Performance Guarantee</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Performance Guarantee is a security measure required to ensure the completion of reclamation plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Guarantee is a requirement that ensures the construction, monitoring, and maintenance of mitigation sites comply with established plans.&lt;SEP&gt;A Performance Guarantee is a requirement for applicants, ensuring that they will meet conditions of land use approvals, often in the form of a bond or cash.&lt;SEP&gt;A Performance Guarantee is a form of security that ensures compliance with approved planning documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31a92cc8ee690c44538d0568e543e8a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc617f6f881f3f98f97136cfa84f2ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca18882d6a8207dec4b469f7a2654fd4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Building Permits">
      <data key="d0">Building Permits</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Building permits are required for certain fences as per the building code, managed by PP&amp;D.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Permits are necessary for construction activities and may be issued only after proof of covenant recording is provided.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e75ce8cc1ed34d85d9e574add4504b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indemnity Agreements">
      <data key="d0">Indemnity Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indemnity Agreements are contracts that may be used by governmental agencies as performance guarantees in land use approvals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77e32332dad5644a1592ba93791f21ff</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781104</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Living Area">
      <data key="d0">Living Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The living area refers to the residential space that needs to be visually connected to the street and emphasizes its prominence.&lt;SEP&gt;Living Area represents the total gross building area of a residential structure, excluding certain areas such as garages and basements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781105</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Detached Garage">
      <data key="d0">Detached Garage</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A detached garage is a nonconforming structure that can be rebuilt under specific conditions when it does not meet zoning setbacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781105</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="R10 to R2.5 Zones">
      <data key="d0">R10 to R2.5 Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">R10 to R2.5 zones are specific residential zoning classifications that govern construction and accessory structures like garages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781105</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Preliminary Plan Approval">
      <data key="d0">Preliminary Plan Approval</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Preliminary plan approval is a regulatory milestone that exempts certain subdivisions from specific standards related to garage construction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e340681b50bf551a0c9458d916a1b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9fa0abfcd845e14321262101dfa625</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781105</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 33.110 Title 33">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.110 Title 33</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
