    <node id="River Setback">
      <data key="d0">River Setback</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The River Setback refers to the designated area adjacent to a river that may have specific development regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The River Setback is a designated area intended to separate structures from the river to protect natural qualities.&lt;SEP&gt;The River Setback is a defined area landward of which regulation applies to the removal of trees and vegetation near the river.&lt;SEP&gt;River setback refers to a designated buffer area adjacent to a river where specific landscaping regulations must be followed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e88e3e2ec290b90a147566b3c2e07270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc3fc3ad91ea490a2f8ffb98e83e2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034b368053d2bf03704822c6c98238c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c7c788c54dd25901bd6c8ddfb5d32d</data>
