    <node id="River Review">
      <data key="d0">River Review</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">River Review refers to a comprehensive assessment process focused on riverfront development and management strategies. It is a regulatory mechanism that evaluates the environmental impacts and resource management strategies of projects that potentially affect river systems and their associated resources. Specifically, River Review is applied to development proposals within designated water-related zones, particularly the River Environmental overlay zone, to safeguard and enhance environmental resources.

The River Review process establishes specific criteria and procedures deemed necessary for assessing the implications of proposed developments. It ensures compliance with various regulations imposed by the City, which govern land use applications and modifications to already approved projects. Moreover, this review process plays a crucial role in determining approval for development scenarios that may alter the environmental balance of river ecosystems.

In summary, River Review encompasses a structured evaluation aimed at assessing and regulating activities that could impact waterways, thereby playing a pivotal role in sustainable river management and development planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d65c927885cd8918e2dccfdeeb204f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7822437163e35b6c56d5560ac87ff1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7777fdca5bcbd3670723d206cd8f5757&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49961939512caa6917f2206eb92e7d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8304e315438268768f83d85e05fcf463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9baf563ec9df2a33ac29db9f4fc53fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a4fda2a7ebb04a6a59cff745526b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53b762b810e686427f2749d1fda54aca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644152b6276c54299003f76b5630241f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781108</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
