      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pedestrian Districts are designated areas designed to encourage foot traffic and pedestrian-friendly development.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Districts are areas where specific building setback regulations apply differently compared to other zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Districts are designated areas meant to enhance pedestrian environments and accessibility, governed by specific design standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Districts are designated areas where drive-through facilities are not allowed to ensure pedestrian-friendly environments.</data>
