    <node id="Pedestrian Standards">
      <data key="d0">Pedestrian Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pedestrian Standards establish guidelines for the design and infrastructure supporting pedestrian movement and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian standards are regulations aimed at ensuring safe and effective pedestrian circulation within developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian standards refer to guidelines that encourage safe and attractive pedestrian circulation in employment zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Standards are guidelines for creating walkable environments and ensuring safe pedestrian access in development plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Standards are regulations aimed at creating attractive and accessible environments for pedestrians within the East Corridor Plan District.&lt;SEP&gt;Pedestrian Standards regulate direct pedestrian connections to enhance walkability and amenity in the urban environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ce4a0b57a87c710f0ef76d5570894bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14a3fd9ec346cf135da2b0299cad1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7afd4cd98781a0f8a75a7fa3cd365098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2003f93c2ff07e93de1875ffe1520e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e317f6dbe5f15015c8e4149009a9021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b403688e7e60056001325caf3e9e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4328dc69e2d2b9998d2666c8193b0245</data>
