    <node id="Standards of This Chapter">
      <data key="d0">Standards of This Chapter</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards of this chapter refer to the rules and criteria that applicants must follow when proposing landscaping materials and tree selections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99992d12911944db6172dcc6b2ae4ab5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781115</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ground Floor">
      <data key="d0">Ground Floor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ground Floor is the first level of a building, often designated for specific uses as per zoning laws that aim to maximize accessibility and functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground floor refers to the first level of a building where certain design standards must be met for pedestrian access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cac21afda0123f450c6fc8b893e703d6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781115</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seating or Bench">
      <data key="d0">Seating or Bench</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Seating or bench are required elements near main entrances to provide comfort and accessibility to the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781115</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Outdoor Plaza">
      <data key="d0">Outdoor Plaza</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Outdoor plaza is a designated space that must meet specific requirements related to size and landscaping as per zoning regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781115</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PR11 Separation of Dwelling Unit Entry from Vehicle Areas">
      <data key="d0">PR11 Separation of Dwelling Unit Entry from Vehicle Areas</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PR11 Separation of Dwelling Unit Entry from Vehicle Areas refers to design standards for new buildings to ensure adequate separation of dwelling unit entrances from adjacent vehicle areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce84b33b7ab639d2d53ae06b94dc49e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
