    <node id="Employment and Industrial Zones">
      <data key="d0">Employment and Industrial Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment and Industrial Zones are specific areas designated for industrial and employment-generating activities, subject to zoning regulations aimed at controlling land use for these purposes. These zones are part of a city’s urban planning framework and encompass various classifications of land uses defined in local regulations.

These zones serve as designated areas within city plans specifically allocated for business and industrial activities, including nonresidential land uses that align with employment objectives. Employment and Industrial Zones are established to facilitate job-related development and incorporate policies governing different industries within the community. 

Moreover, they are represented in legal contexts as sections within Title 33, which relates to different types of zoning. Overall, the primary focus of Employment and Industrial Zones is to create organized spaces for work-related developments that support economic growth and employment opportunities within urban settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b50b722c831d7fd62efdf07089cb44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ce319f7fcb7893676edd6b489a8b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5555f01efc47b9ad220ce985153f9292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e927f3c64b3afc1f943e861ae4fac76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c05d0565960f8c21b2582374b4856a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541798bed671b97a824c372f4887511f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec6039135156cca92456b8fc09b0f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422a1c7b762d9ab38fe2197b504ec353</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781116</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="South Waterfront">
      <data key="d0">South Waterfront</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The South Waterfront is a subdistrict of the Central City Plan District in Portland subject to zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;South Waterfront is a subdistrict in Portland where specific land use regulations apply and where the bonus floor area may be used.&lt;SEP&gt;South Waterfront is an area referenced in urban planning documents related to building heights and design reviews.&lt;SEP&gt;South Waterfront is a district with specific planning and zoning regulations, particularly involving accessways and building dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;The South Waterfront is an area that features recreational trails and is involved in planning and zoning regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;South Waterfront is a subdistrict in Central City where specific parking regulations and eligibility criteria are applied.&lt;SEP&gt;The South Waterfront is a subdistrict of the Central City plan district associated with bicycle parking regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d832d62a221ee980072fc5fd0b98677e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e6e0a14b42f25e67a43e11831d8486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9989ec0c8f4e7c8e5d3d6ed67ed8d7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2da4d204d050cba040fddbe243ce05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbf21d0ccd80cdf97bfee50d738455e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2341ab772a74f1ba57e44df79eb3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-701c3f15dff43f3530bb018f9bae2909</data>
