    <node id="Campus Institutional Zones">
      <data key="d0">Campus Institutional Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Campus Institutional Zones are designated areas within urban planning that cater specifically to educational and institutional facilities. These zones are governed by established planning and zoning regulations, which dictate various development standards including building heights and setbacks, as outlined in Title 33, Chapter 33.150.

These zones play a crucial role in the regulation of land use, allowing for the development of educational and medical institutions while also considering their proximity to residential zones. The zoning classifications associated with Campus Institutional Zones establish the permitted uses and development parameters that institutions must adhere to, ensuring that institutional developments are appropriately integrated within the surrounding community.

Additionally, specific conditional uses may be permitted within these zones, contingent upon meeting defined approval criteria. Overall, Campus Institutional Zones are essential for managing the growth and placement of institutional facilities in an organized and regulated manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17a8112955d64121a20078f6914b8018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37fe28a6c33ecbcbe2396156e4ee10e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b45e62181c08d6aef102ffa4458a5226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2574af8787db7883bc15da7cbabd3a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4e7feaddec557941c697fec7b2e2763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf1cc9b5437586cfb484233e2286c341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639e5332d0e90ed7ad51bb327c530214</data>
