    <node id="FAR">
      <data key="d0">FAR</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FAR refers to Floor Area Ratio, a zoning regulation that affects building coverage and density.&lt;SEP&gt;FAR, or Floor Area Ratio, is a measure used in zoning regulations to determine the amount of floor space a building may have in relation to the size of the lot it occupies.&lt;SEP&gt;FAR (Floor Area Ratio) is a measure used in urban planning to determine the density of buildings on a specific site regarding the total square footage of the building in relation to the area of the lot.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a7c158baba6b66776b2fa39c55edd02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d788f2bb3749862ef8f88846b7f7ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49acd712739227babe51a65cf9f9e8be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe493d8ddd3157de8f252cc78bfde3db</data>
