    </node>
    <node id="South Waterfront Subdistrict">
      <data key="d0">South Waterfront Subdistrict</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The South Waterfront Subdistrict is a defined area within the Central City Plan District of Portland, Oregon, characterized by specific zoning regulations and development guidelines. This subdistrict encompasses a mixed-use neighborhood that aims to support growth and development while adhering to established construction standards. 

Particularly notable are the area’s zoning rules that govern floor area ratio (FAR), height bonuses, and incentives for open space. Developers within the South Waterfront Subdistrict must follow regulations concerning major public trails, building height corridors, and visual access to ensure both compliance and the enhancement of the neighborhood environment. Additionally, there are unique standards in place for new developments and significant remodels, which include the provision of amenities facilitating alternative transportation modes such as biking and walking.

The South Waterfront Subdistrict also allows for surface parking operated by the City of Portland on sites earmarked for future park development, adding another layer to its planning framework. Overall, the subdistrict's regulations foster a balanced approach to urban development while prioritizing community amenities and transportation strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4749d2209607255edbe985025b727249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-464a103ac291e4d5b8cfdd5b7c5b692f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5981b497cbbe74619a5ea1cae750089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb900a5dfbcef784bb89e24f0c85c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c127588b3effb62124f2b4367f10741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3687e34f528a78261767a8a0c1b6b6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7896cc3191620f9cfec1d8626e62a156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d0e3bbe363516aa161846014338967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbed3d0d9f1ce8f7b4b9d7df85935cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9a5a4577f7544b4671be7b0e59a2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a1f6c75ad3d0c1fd2c336ca22bead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71ef8e763b48167f014ebc29d2564293</data>
