      <data key="d0">Design Advice Request</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Design Advice Request is a preliminary consultation process required before submitting an application for design review in development projects.&lt;SEP&gt;A Design Advice Request is a preliminary step in the design review process, requiring feedback before a formal application submission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Design Advice Request is a required step before submitting an application for historic resource review, ensuring compliance with design standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1347219a19de2480f10b4ab0d1cc91d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64ae29063e6b41ec74fbbe9839ad342b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inner Neighborhoods Pattern Area">
      <data key="d0">Inner Neighborhoods Pattern Area</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inner Neighborhoods Pattern Area is a designated urban development zone within which alternative landscaping options may be applied.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large-Canopy Tree">
      <data key="d0">Large-Canopy Tree</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Large-Canopy Trees are defined requirements within the zoning regulations that can help fulfill landscaped area standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-160a32f5ce16b3d3271378c2f5cf5dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CCRC">
      <data key="d0">CCRC</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CCRC stands for Continuing Care Retirement Community, which is a type of housing that offers various levels of care and services to residents, primarily seniors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Greater Area Median Family Income">
      <data key="d0">Greater Area Median Family Income</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Greater Area Median Family Income is a benchmark used to determine affordability standards for housing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Title 30">
      <data key="d0">Title 30</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Title 30 refers to a section of regulations that allows for alternative calculations for affordable dwelling units based on total bedrooms.&lt;SEP&gt;Title 30 refers to legislation that establishes affordability levels and guidelines for housing developments in the area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.700.060">
      <data key="d0">33.700.060</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.700.060 outlines specific requirements related to covenants for affordable housing in the city.&lt;SEP&gt;33.700.060 addresses the requirements for covenants with the City regarding the maintenance and operation of properties.&lt;SEP&gt;33.700.060 refers to specific covenants with the City that outline the requirements for maintenance and features of open space.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93214ee5c49fbb5384175df60c9eafe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4177bfbc917fc82fda498c4d1f0e571f</data>
