      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.245.040">
      <data key="d0">33.245.040</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.245.040 outlines the inclusionary housing standards that dictate the requirements for affordable dwelling units in developments.&lt;SEP&gt;33.245.040 is part of the zoning code specifying standards that projects may comply with to qualify for bonus FAR.&lt;SEP&gt;33.245.040 is a regulation standard that must be adhered to for obtaining bonus floor area in development projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04d6cd35d45d8e93ff5e834df187ee1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.245.050">
      <data key="d0">33.245.050</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.245.050 specifies the compliance requirements for developments to adhere to the inclusionary housing standards.&lt;SEP&gt;33.245.050 is another part of the zoning code providing additional standards related to Inclusionary Housing and FAR bonuses.&lt;SEP&gt;33.245.050 is another regulation standard that complements 33.245.040 for bonus floor area qualifications in development projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5169c21d505e8c064ac1ba9c16c3eb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04d6cd35d45d8e93ff5e834df187ee1</data>
