      <data key="d5">1768781123</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Floor Area">
      <data key="d0">Floor Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Floor Area refers to the space measured in square feet used for various classifications in zoning, impacting allowed uses on a site.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Area describes the total area of a building's floor space that is subject to regulations regarding bonuses and open area requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Area refers to the total space occupied by a conditional use, significant in determining the need for a master plan review.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Area refers to the total area of all floors of a building, with specific exclusions outlined for measurement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d08b01451771b358c77494f198e0c0a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d06cb95ab17fc909ffe773dee0f0a731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b2c3f3b605bc9f877b7485abc23364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d46523b43ad78784d5fd13052c9870a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781123</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bonus FAR">
      <data key="d0">Bonus FAR</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bonus FAR refers to additional floor area ratio allowances that can be earned under certain conditions, such as inclusionary housing requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Bonus FAR (Floor Area Ratio) refers to the additional square footage allowed in building development in exchange for contributions to fund affordable housing initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Bonus FAR is a zoning incentive that allows additional floor area ratio for projects meeting certain criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c02275a7d3d6fe5e228c10bb5e48bb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ae74afee809cbeca89eeeb5025a2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7afd4cd98781a0f8a75a7fa3cd365098</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781123</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
