      <data key="d2">Map 510-1 depicts the boundaries of the Central City plan district and its associated subdistricts.&lt;SEP&gt;Map 510-1 is a reference map used to identify proposals and their requirements within the Central City plan district.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809349c43acd176bb535a05d03c6c5c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b121eab358b392062623a0c2554b90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot of Record">
      <data key="d0">Lot of Record</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A lot of record refers to a plot of land not created through subdivision and recorded before July 26, 1979.&lt;SEP&gt;The lot of record is a defined term related to lot ownership and zoning regulations in planning and zoning contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lot Remnant">
      <data key="d0">Lot Remnant</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A lot remnant is a portion of a lot that has undergone alterations to its lines, recorded prior to July 26, 1979.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot remnant refers to a leftover parcel of land that remains after part of the lot has been sold or developed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintained Street">
      <data key="d0">Maintained Street</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A maintained street has been accepted for maintenance by relevant government authorities, such as the City of Portland or Multnomah County.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1daea73587f156d45df1e0850a2216e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintenance consists of activities aimed at preventing the deterioration of structures or their components, such as painting or re-roofing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Major Remodeling">
      <data key="d0">Major Remodeling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Major remodeling involves significant construction changes, typically increasing a structure's floor area by 50% or more.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manufactured Dwelling Park">
      <data key="d0">Manufactured Dwelling Park</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A manufactured dwelling park is a site with four or more manufactured dwellings for residential use, rented for over 30 days.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Marina">
      <data key="d0">Marina</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Marina is a facility for docking and storing boats and yachts, often providing services and amenities for boaters.&lt;SEP&gt;A marina provides secure moorings for recreational or commercial boats and does not include houseboat moorages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86420cc97941914b0b1ab8dfd5d58107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mass Shelter Beds">
      <data key="d0">Mass Shelter Beds</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mass shelter beds are accommodations for individuals in mass shelters, determined by the maximum overnight capacity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mixed-Use">
      <data key="d0">Mixed-Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mixed-use refers to developments combining residential and commercial or industrial uses within the same site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Near Shore Complexity">
      <data key="d0">Near Shore Complexity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Near shore complexity describes conditions in a river channel characterized by diverse vegetation, varied water flow, and structural elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-407b70ec9a0d07610f2396b7da298ad6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Institutional Campus">
      <data key="d0">Institutional Campus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An institutional campus refers to a group of buildings and facilities used for educational, medical, or community purposes, subject to specific development standards and impact mitigation plans.&lt;SEP&gt;An Institutional Campus is an area designated for educational institutions, allowing specific facility types and event hosting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Institutional Campus is the geographical area where the institution operates and plans its development activities.&lt;SEP&gt;An Institutional Campus is a site for medical or educational institutions measuring at least 5 acres in area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6d86139e9f8ebbadc462769659fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a263606fc895d08c7f7b3c2d745536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed8af90c52cb663785082c6731625b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exterior Display Standards">
      <data key="d0">Exterior Display Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Exterior display standards regulate the display of goods outside buildings to ensure aesthetic consistency and to avoid negative impacts on the community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Accessory Retail Sales and Service">
      <data key="d0">Accessory Retail Sales and Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessory retail sales and service uses refer to secondary commercial activities that support primary institutional functions and must adhere to specific access and signage requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Truck and Equipment Parking Standards">
      <data key="d0">Truck and Equipment Parking Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Truck and equipment parking standards define the regulations governing the parking and storage of various categories of trucks and equipment on institutional campuses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="College or Medical Center">
      <data key="d0">College or Medical Center</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A College or Medical Center refers to institutions that provide education or healthcare services, which are relevant to the standards and requirements outlined for the institutional campus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a7c1254b8df2c92949dbb5d7386e2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MOU">
      <data key="d0">MOU</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">The signed Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) specifies the required documentation for resource recovery plans in compliance with development activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-903c333e61f6db5523241ff9b270a90f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781124</data>
