      <data key="d0">Type II, Type IIx or Type III Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Type II, Type IIx or Type III Decision refers to classifications of decisions made regarding land use actions that are subject to specific appeal processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-644cc4e15ec9d767b69917b94f282c47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ldn (or DNL)">
      <data key="d0">Ldn (or DNL)</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Ldn is an averaged sound level measurement taken over a 24-hour period, used for assessing nighttime noise impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Light Rail Line">
      <data key="d0">Light Rail Line</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Light Rail Line is a transportation project that necessitates the construction of parking facilities to replace lost parking spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;A Light Rail Line is a public rail transit system providing high-capacity service and usually shares a street right-of-way.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a05752417b511c6e703a9f6b6aac007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Light Rail Alignment">
      <data key="d0">Light Rail Alignment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Light Rail Alignment refers to the paths or routes designated for light rail transit, affecting nearby developments and facility regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Light rail alignment is the designated path or route for light rail transit services, affecting land use regulations in its vicinity.&lt;SEP&gt;Light Rail Alignment refers to a designated public right-of-way or easement for light rail lines, identified by city and regional authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a103c5d3dba321e0474c52d261504cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78575afc304e77ddac795549d18c014</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Live Stake">
      <data key="d0">Live Stake</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Live Stake is a rootable vegetative cutting used in various applications, including bioengineering to stabilize slopes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Loading Area">
      <data key="d0">Loading Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Loading Area is designated space for vehicles to maneuver and stand while loading or unloading passengers and goods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Long Term Parking">
      <data key="d0">Long Term Parking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Long Term Parking refers to parking spaces allocated for durations exceeding four hours.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rooftop Solar Energy Systems">
      <data key="d0">Rooftop Solar Energy Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Rooftop Solar Energy Systems are installations located on the rooftops of buildings specifically designed for solar energy generation. These systems are subject to a range of regulations that dictate their size, placement, mounting, visibility, and compliance with local guidelines concerning the structure's physical modifications. 

The regulations surrounding Rooftop Solar Energy Systems ensure that these installations conform to aesthetic and structural requirements appropriate for different types of roofs, as well as maintain the integrity of the building's footprint and peak height. For instance, certain guidelines prevent alterations that could impact the building’s visual impact or diminish the surrounding environment, especially in conservation districts.

In addition, Rooftop Solar Energy Systems must adhere to specified standards for mounting and screening to ensure compliance with local ordinances. This means that while they provide an important source of renewable energy, their integration into the architectural fabric of existing structures is carefully managed to align with community standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1abf9c5e7468a8aa27d8da7b65c0352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-861e9e945a4de0eb93decd93ac5bbc54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c5e50780fccc672722393ad08acacb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daeac152d9d697433ef7be1355d6e8e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3fdad639580e09c9504162fba29af8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37ff07ffa7013303eef3ff22ca4c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49385b6cdb2ddda6bb336746708e24c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495bf4fb125321f6e8595e2bd9e90b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b729b503408753bfb450541d299ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Longest Street-Facing Wall">
      <data key="d0">Longest Street-Facing Wall</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Longest Street-Facing Wall is defined as the wall of a structure that faces the street and is the longest among those walls.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adjusted Lot">
      <data key="d0">Adjusted Lot</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Adjusted Lot is a lot that underwent changes to its boundaries either through a deed or property line adjustments, maintaining a minimum size requirement.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjusted Lot relates to lot-related definitions in zoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-815bfa0ca1f2854481b5b5b608fdc5d0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Corner Lot">
      <data key="d0">Corner Lot</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A corner lot is defined according to specific zoning and land use regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Corner Lot is defined as a lot with frontages on more than one intersecting street.&lt;SEP&gt;A corner lot is defined as a lot with frontages that intersect, typically at angles less than or equal to 120 degrees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a117438300054dc6a03e64e7a5e6bdcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ab589ad2a81c7f7964b172f2ba2949a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11738f034d5f65fb344c5bf37019ca51</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Landscaping and Screening Standards">
      <data key="d0">Landscaping and Screening Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Landscaping and Screening Standards are a set of regulations addressing the design and implementation of landscaping measures in urban areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="33.248">
      <data key="d0">33.248</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 33.248 specifies landscaping and screening standards associated with helicopter landing facilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 33.248 includes regulations regarding landscaping and screening standards within the City of Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ca5fc3d28aa819abc484b86dc468ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Street Trees">
      <data key="d0">Street Trees</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Street Trees are trees planted along streets that contribute to urban aesthetics and environmental benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3404eafc9757fc05febd370a1ac85737</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Washington Land Use Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Washington Land Use Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Washington Land Use Regulations govern the planning and zoning rules that apply to land use within designated districts, including the Central City Plan District.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5981b497cbbe74619a5ea1cae750089</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Noise Insulation Standard">
      <data key="d0">Noise Insulation Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Noise Insulation Standard requires new dwelling units near industrial areas to achieve specific sound insulation to mitigate noise impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Noise Insulation Standard requires new dwelling units to achieve a day/night average noise level of 45 dBA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5981b497cbbe74619a5ea1cae750089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a1f6c75ad3d0c1fd2c336ca22bead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e474c16a2f491d5d3d21de73c32071c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781125</data>
