    <node id="Chapter 33.510">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 33.510</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 33.510 refers to a specific legislative section within the wider framework of Title 33, which addresses Planning and Zoning regulations in the Central City Plan District. This chapter provides detailed guidelines and standards that govern various aspects of urban development in the district, including regulations that pertain to building heights, zoning standards, parking requirements, and preservation issues.

Particularly, Chapter 33.510 contains provisions related to the planning and zoning standards applicable to different urban zones within the Central City Plan District and is essential for establishing the regulatory environment for urban development. The chapter emphasizes the integration of zoning and planning concepts to ensure that development aligns with the district's growth and preservation objectives.

Furthermore, the chapter specifically addresses issues concerning parking, providing regulations that detail the different types of parking structures and requirements necessary within the Central City Plan District. Additionally, it incorporates considerations for the Greenway Setback Area, highlighting its relevance in the context of urban planning and environmental preservation. 

Overall, Chapter 33.510 serves as a comprehensive guide for developers, city planners, and stakeholders involved in the urban development process, outlining the necessary standards and regulations to facilitate orderly growth and maintain the integrity of the Central City Plan District.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d2c06f5978724095d6914de0f870d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-157f892dc3db1b7d5113b58ec80ccd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e8e418ed77b8672d2e0bbc7d7689df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781cca6130ae27c4d81ffe1ab1fb3d43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba31ae20af3e709ad848c12217e0c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9a5a4577f7544b4671be7b0e59a2ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2341ab772a74f1ba57e44df79eb3af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4ea648c5114e40203cea6e5e6e2bb27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-701c3f15dff43f3530bb018f9bae2909</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781129</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kenton Conservation District">
      <data key="d0">Kenton Conservation District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Kenton Conservation District is a designated district where specific architectural materials and standards are required for buildings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Kenton Conservation District has specific requirements for new buildings, particularly regarding the materials used on street-facing elevations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Kenton Conservation District mandates that new commercial buildings use cast stone on their street-facing elevations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c5e50780fccc672722393ad08acacb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2020f8cb9e1e9fff0f2699c2142d64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af58e78814991f9a5ecdccb7e8088e42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781129</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Woodlawn Conservation District">
      <data key="d0">Woodlawn Conservation District</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Woodlawn Conservation District is an area where buildings must not be located in the vacated portions of the angled street pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District is an area where specific architectural standards and street patterns are implemented.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District is an area designated with particular guidelines to manage development and building patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District is an area where specific street patterns influence building placement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District has specific guidelines restricting certain building placements within its vacated street patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District sets standards that apply to commercial buildings within its boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woodlawn Conservation District requires commercial buildings to use wood as the exterior finish material for street-facing elevations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6c5e50780fccc672722393ad08acacb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6a99f5dabcc8fb084171f333a7bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2020f8cb9e1e9fff0f2699c2142d64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57a10d5dc00da1681573c18ad3bbe22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af58e78814991f9a5ecdccb7e8088e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495bf4fb125321f6e8595e2bd9e90b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7643c0f4d3b8e865b2421a8cf1882d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781129</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Arcade Option">
