    <node id="Urban Growth Boundary">
      <data key="d0">Urban Growth Boundary</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Urban Growth Boundary is a defined area used to manage urban development and zoning regulations, affecting decision notifications based on proximity to sites.&lt;SEP&gt;The Urban Growth Boundary is a land-use planning boundary that influences land development regulations within the City of Portland.&lt;SEP&gt;The Urban Growth Boundary defines the limits for property owner notifications in the review process based on proximity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Urban Growth Boundary delineates areas for urban development and can affect zoning map corrections.</data>
