    <node id="Marine Drive">
      <data key="d0">Marine Drive</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Marine Drive is a significant scenic roadway located in Portland, recognized for its elevated position and specific standards that enhance its character. It runs adjacent to the Columbia River, making it a major route that combines both developmental compatibility and scenic qualities. The roadway is noted not only for its aesthetic appeal but also for its function as a corridor that supports public views along the water.

In addition to its scenic value, Marine Drive is integral to the landscaping guidelines set within the Columbia South Shore Plan District. These guidelines dictate specific planting requirements along its slopes and vegetation planting along its frontage, ensuring that the landscape remains visually appealing and environmentally sustainable. The road’s design also adheres to particular streetscape standards that maintain its overall character and integration with surrounding environments.

Furthermore, Marine Drive is a vital route where rooftops and structures are notably visible from various vantage points, influencing the design considerations for new developments. The combination of landscaping, setback standards, and design guidelines contributes to the well-planned environment that characterizes Marine Drive, making it a significant element of the urban landscape in Portland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df3a6e155b7b2dbe62a2cf5f8c6d3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-441c51a51f44fd3d962a1948c121fd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c95bddb922c68491a627c84908a1149&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f465b3d8f13fedcc409a730049f471&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ba38f00281849bf4c2c4102963efade&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b847fda67c001cd22d177dc64c0dcbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37c56c223dd5bef0b4b081153775bf0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2536df7b2db91f19a3efb52a5bbd6e81</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
