    <node id="Statutory Authority">
      <data key="d0">Statutory Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Statutory Authority refers to the legal powers granted to agencies like CCLD under Oregon statutes such as ORS 183.459 and ORS 329A.260.&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory authority refers to the legal authority under ORS 329A.260 governing the operation of certified child care centers and their regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory Authority refers to the legal basis for the child care regulations as indicated by Oregon Revised Statutes (ORS).&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory authority refers to the legal foundations under which educational regulations and requirements are established.&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory Authority refers to the legal framework governing child care rules in Oregon, specifically ORS 329A.260.&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory authority refers to the legal provisions under which agencies like the Oregon Health Authority operate and enforce health regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Statutory authority refers to the legal provisions such as ORS 329A.260 that mandate specific regulations for child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ba168f74a8dc5d017a0cbbf45d41055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8783a3d51dfcd420464a5d189210c543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7b17c24300e18201fee673b061b7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062714e04d9fd0b42d61158f90679830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a50fa93a5c42a28ff7fb62790e9d920</data>
