    <node id="Civil Penalty">
      <data key="d0">Civil Penalty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Civil Penalty is a monetary fine imposed for violations of child care regulations, with a specified maximum amount for unlawful care instances.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Penalty is a financial penalty imposed for violations of the care regulations as defined in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Penalty refers to a fine imposed by the Child Care Licensing Division (CCLD) for violations of applicable rules or statutes.&lt;SEP&gt;A Civil Penalty is a fine imposed for violations of child care regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Civil Penalty is a financial punishment that CCLD may impose for violations of child care certification rules, with a maximum amount of $2500 per violation.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil penalty refers to the monetary fines imposed for violations of child care regulations, with specific amounts depending on the severity of the violation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-547bb6fbc5bd4c5ae228dca862543bcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4225b326e03d893cc33c6027465e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7e722cae59daaee8fda98d23a46ba9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83ce9fe8422a2f2222e5b139696e0df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8fafcea08c68d1f3b7fabaf975e06cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62d9cafe8310da83e372ee898f31f20</data>
