    <node id="Occasional Care">
      <data key="d0">Occasional Care</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Occasional Care describes temporary child care that occurs for no more than 70 days in a calendar year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-deb527afbb4ed29de2c78fcaed8b968e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child Care Home Facility">
      <data key="d0">Child Care Home Facility</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Child Care Home Facility is a registered or certified establishment that provides care for children during specific operating hours and is subject to licensing requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Related Day Care Program">
      <data key="d0">Employment Related Day Care Program</data>
      <data key="d1">program</data>
      <data key="d2">The Employment Related Day Care Program provides financial assistance for child care services but does not cover certain types of care outlined in the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Union Representative">
      <data key="d0">Union Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Union Representative is an advocate for licensed child care providers in contested case hearings who is not an attorney but can present evidence and make arguments related to the case.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child">
      <data key="d0">Child</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Child refers to an individual receiving care at a child care facility, whose status and care arrangements are subject to specific licensing provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A Child refers to an individual who is under the care of a child care center or facility.&lt;SEP&gt;A child refers to an individual receiving care at a certified child care center, whose safety and permissions are paramount.&lt;SEP&gt;A child is an individual under the age of 18 who is under the care of a certified child care center and may be affected by various conditions requiring attention.&lt;SEP&gt;A child is an individual enrolled in a certified child care center, whose allergies and health well-being are managed through written care plans and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are individuals who are cared for in certified child care centers and are the focus of the protective actions outlined in the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deb527afbb4ed29de2c78fcaed8b968e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7087b54a804a29c105437eb0d2b68809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d13cb0ba705ad4a6ab71f56146accae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6e6b460e08a011ec1cf8cf0ffb87ce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa2d41b2e76e1a0f5b5372a2bcd97bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62d9cafe8310da83e372ee898f31f20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Labor Union">
      <data key="d0">Labor Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Labor Union is an organization that represents workers, including providers of subsidized child care in legal and administrative matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="License-Exempt Child Care Facility">
      <data key="d0">License-Exempt Child Care Facility</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A License-Exempt Child Care Facility is an establishment that is not required to be licensed to provide child care under specific circumstances as outlined in the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Caregiver">
      <data key="d0">Caregiver</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Caregiver is an individual who provides care in a license-exempt child care facility, including for their own child or any child residing with them.&lt;SEP&gt;A Caregiver is a person who directly interacts with and provides care for children in a center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16982ad53929c50839970fc08b877b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83ce9fe8422a2f2222e5b139696e0df</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child Abuse or Neglect">
      <data key="d0">Child Abuse or Neglect</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Child Abuse or Neglect refers to various forms of harm to children, including physical, emotional, and sexual abuse, as defined in legal terms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e4225b326e03d893cc33c6027465e12</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781439</data>
      <data key="d6" />
