    <node id="Physical Restraint">
      <data key="d0">Physical Restraint</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical Restraint involves limiting or obstructing a person's bodily movement, with specific exceptions provided for comforting or safely moving a child.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical Restraint refers to the practice of holding a child to control their movement, subject to strict conditions and regulations for safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4ccb0f82480e6741e25e253a6be980a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a7904f1485b792ad0d6843358b9f8d</data>
