    <node id="Movable Barrier">
      <data key="d0">Movable Barrier</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A movable barrier, such as a baby gate, is required at stairways accessible to infants and toddlers within certified child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be090fdda697a58316cf9a10e3df9d86</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Closing Apparatus">
      <data key="d0">Self-Closing Apparatus</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A self-closing apparatus is required for exterior screens or storm doors in certified child care centers to enhance safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be090fdda697a58316cf9a10e3df9d86</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine-Meshed Screens">
      <data key="d0">Fine-Meshed Screens</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">Fine-meshed screens are installed on doors and windows used for ventilation in certified child care centers to ensure safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be090fdda697a58316cf9a10e3df9d86</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parental Permissions">
      <data key="d0">Parental Permissions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parental permissions encompass the necessary authorizations from parents or guardians for various activities, medications, and rights regarding their children in a care setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Field Trip">
      <data key="d0">Field Trip</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A field trip refers to an organized activity away from the care center that requires parental permission and specific details regarding dates and locations.&lt;SEP&gt;Field Trip is an excursion or program activity conducted away from the child care center's property.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chronic Medical Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Medical Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic medical conditions are ongoing health issues that require specific management and parental consent for care in a child care setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child Immunizations">
      <data key="d0">Child Immunizations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Child immunizations refer to the vaccines required for children attending a certified child care center, governed by the Oregon Health Authority's regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emergency Access to Records">
      <data key="d0">Emergency Access to Records</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Emergency access to records is a requirement that ensures children's records are readily available to caregivers during emergencies or for children with specific care needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Foster Care">
      <data key="d0">Foster Care</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Foster care involves providing temporary accommodation and care for children who are unable to live with their biological parents, often requiring specific permissions in a child care setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
