    </node>
    <node id="Sleeping Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Sleeping Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sleeping equipment refers to items like mats and cots used for children's rest within a child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Sleeping equipment includes beds, cribs, and mattresses that accommodate children's sleeping needs in a certified child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eca846957ee3e21ee367da6260a78bc3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Night Care">
      <data key="d0">Night Care</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Night Care refers to care provided between 9:00 p.m. and 5:00 a.m. or during the time when any enrolled child sleeps for more than 3 hours at the center.&lt;SEP&gt;Night Care refers to the provision of child care services during nighttime hours, requiring specific approvals and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Night care refers to the provision of child care services during evening and nighttime hours, requiring specific regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a7904f1485b792ad0d6843358b9f8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a937432c260b698de8b9ef1c8dc1d423</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Hygiene Provisions">
      <data key="d0">Personal Hygiene Provisions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Provisions for personal hygiene ensure that children have access to necessary hygiene items and facilities while in care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Staff-to-Child Ratio">
      <data key="d0">Staff-to-Child Ratio</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staff-to-child ratio defines the number of staff required to care for a specific number of children, essential for safe and effective supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;The staff-to-child ratio is a regulatory requirement specifying the minimum number of staff present for a set number of children in a child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e9646c597721b8d034971e1b9500b32</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OAR 414-305-1110">
      <data key="d0">OAR 414-305-1110</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">OAR 414-305-1110 outlines the nutritional needs of children in evening and night care in child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sleeping Children">
      <data key="d0">Sleeping Children</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sleeping children refer to those children who are in care during night hours and require appropriate sleeping arrangements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea137d7dd7f5c9ecf47913a29d8d0d20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parents">
      <data key="d0">Parents</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Parents are individuals responsible for the care and upbringing of children enrolled in a child care center, required to provide essential information and support to the center.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are guardians or caregivers who enroll their children in a certified child care center and must be informed of policies and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are individuals who provide information about their child's care needs for assessments conducted by the child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are responsible for ensuring the safety and wellbeing of their children, including being notified about allergies and incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are individuals responsible for the care and supervision of children and play a role in child care center regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are individuals who have children in care at child care centers and must be notified of any suspension or closure of these centers.&lt;SEP&gt;Parents are guardians of the children enrolled in the child care center, who are provided with information about menus and food served.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d13cb0ba705ad4a6ab71f56146accae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe199d52c89bc867bc7b50bd194e532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf3185b5c7893f155386b9b16e739f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60c35b5c4ccdef38598f6b916ce964a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62d9cafe8310da83e372ee898f31f20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint Investigation">
      <data key="d0">Complaint Investigation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Complaint Investigation is an official process conducted by CCLD to assess allegations concerning child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Suspension">
      <data key="d0">Suspension</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Suspension is the action taken by CCLD to temporarily revoke a Certified Child Care Center's certification due to safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dinner">
      <data key="d0">Dinner</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dinner is a meal that must be provided to children in night care if they are present after their scheduled dinner time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nutritious Snack">
      <data key="d0">Nutritious Snack</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Nutritious Snack is intended to be offered to all children after dinner service and before bed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breakfast">
      <data key="d0">Breakfast</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Breakfast is a meal that must be served to each child present at the scheduled time unless specified otherwise by parents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Written Permission">
      <data key="d0">Written Permission</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Written Permission refers to the necessary authorization from parents for siblings to bathe together.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ce955faabf384dfbebc7b43e9c41b22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Experience and Training Qualification Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Experience and Training Qualification Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Experience and training qualification requirements outline the necessary training and experience levels for aides based on their assigned age group.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 2">
      <data key="d0">Table 2</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 2 lists specific criteria for experience and training qualifications in an educational context.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 lists experience and training qualification requirements for teachers based on the age group they are assigned to.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80a366bf46647b53ade9fdc7a4ebe0a6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 3">
      <data key="d0">Table 3</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 3 outlines additional experience and training qualification requirements specifically for school-age only classrooms.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 3 specifies the experience and/or training qualification requirements for classrooms that cater to school-age children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80a366bf46647b53ade9fdc7a4ebe0a6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Duties and Qualifications of Aides">
      <data key="d0">Duties and Qualifications of Aides</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Duties and qualifications of aides describe the responsibilities and minimum qualifications necessary for aides working in educational settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aide I">
      <data key="d0">Aide I</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Aide I is a designation for a type of aide who must meet certain age and training requirements outlined in educational guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aide II">
      <data key="d0">Aide II</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Aide II refers to a classification of aides with more experience and higher qualification standards than Aide I.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Teacher Training Program">
      <data key="d0">Teacher Training Program</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Teacher Training Program requires completion of specific core knowledge categories and training hours for staff members in child care.&lt;SEP&gt;A teacher training program involves structured learning designed for aides to fulfill educational qualifications and provide instruction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8783a3d51dfcd420464a5d189210c543</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Initial Training Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Initial Training Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Initial training requirements outline the foundational training that aides must complete to begin their roles in educational settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="240 Documented Hours">
      <data key="d0">240 Documented Hours</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">240 documented hours refers to the minimum hours of experience required for an Aide II, including specific regulations regarding age groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Staff-to-Child Ratios">
      <data key="d0">Staff-to-Child Ratios</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staff-to-child ratios are guidelines that stipulate the number of staff members required to supervise a specific number of children for safety and quality care.&lt;SEP&gt;Staff-to-Child Ratios are the specified ratios determining the number of staff required per child in various age groups at child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b45afced76b5464d04d87323292d537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a937432c260b698de8b9ef1c8dc1d423</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Infants">
      <data key="d0">Infants</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Infants are young children who require assistance with feeding and are provided with individual sleeping equipment in a certified child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Infants are children under 12 months of age who require specific care and feeding schedules in a certified child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Infants are children under one year old who require specific care and attention in a certified child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-413de6970c782ab39f7b5ab84bc167b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb4d5cfab6fb222aa4a2485da799adb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Toddlers">
      <data key="d0">Toddlers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Toddlers are young children, typically ages one to three, who have specific developmental and care needs addressed in a child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Toddlers are young children who, along with infants, are served by certified child care centers and have developmental needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb4d5cfab6fb222aa4a2485da799adb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OAR 414-305-0520">
      <data key="d0">OAR 414-305-0520</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">OAR 414-305-0520 outlines activities that must be provided in a certified child care center for the growth and development of children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OAR 414-305-0530">
      <data key="d0">OAR 414-305-0530</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">OAR 414-305-0530 specifies requirements for school-age activity planning in a certified child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OAR 414-305-0600">
      <data key="d0">OAR 414-305-0600</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">OAR 414-305-0600 outlines general requirements for the care of infants and toddlers in certified child care settings.&lt;SEP&gt;OAR 414-305-0600 defines general requirements related to the care of infants and toddlers in a certified child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7087b54a804a29c105437eb0d2b68809</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Screen Time">
      <data key="d0">Screen Time</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Screen time refers to the amount of time children spend using electronic devices, which is regulated in a certified child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Developmentally Appropriate Activities">
      <data key="d0">Developmentally Appropriate Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Developmentally appropriate activities are those that meet children's needs and abilities, facilitating growth in various areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmentally appropriate activities are experiences designed to promote various aspects of children's growth, including cognitive and emotional development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395c45f0f36a4c698dc34df7ec97f30</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Creative Expression Through The Arts">
      <data key="d0">Creative Expression Through The Arts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Creative expression through the arts refers to activities that allow children to explore and express their creativity using various artistic mediums.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dramatic Play">
      <data key="d0">Dramatic Play</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dramatic play involves children acting out roles and stories, promoting imagination and social skills within a child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gross Motor Development">
      <data key="d0">Gross Motor Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Gross motor development includes activities that promote physical skills and coordination, essential for children's physical growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine Motor Development">
      <data key="d0">Fine Motor Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fine motor development focuses on developing small muscle control and coordination through specific activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Music And Movement">
      <data key="d0">Music And Movement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Music and movement activities encourage physical activity and musical expression in a developmentally appropriate context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Concept Development">
      <data key="d0">Concept Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Concept development involves learning and understanding ideas and categories, an essential part of children's cognitive growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sensory Play">
      <data key="d0">Sensory Play</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sensory play provides children with opportunities to explore and engage their senses, benefiting their overall development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbd4705daa9719f4dc3e5f22eb98c2fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Disinfect">
      <data key="d0">Disinfect</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Disinfect refers to the process of eliminating germs from surfaces using specific cleaning methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Drop-in Care">
      <data key="d0">Drop-in Care</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Drop-in Care refers to irregular child care services provided for short durations, up to 25 hours per week per child.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fire Code Official">
      <data key="d0">Fire Code Official</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Fire Code Official includes titles such as Fire Inspector II and Fire Marshal, responsible for ensuring fire safety compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The fire code official ensures that child care centers comply with fire safety regulations and issues approvals required for certification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d97297fd1fc20be9b71da55cbb584d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Infant">
      <data key="d0">Infant</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Infant refers to children aged 6 weeks to 12 months.&lt;SEP&gt;An infant is a young child, specifically under the age of one, who is fed using human milk or formula and has specific dietary guidelines to follow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae0627674c0e92dcdf8ea4b85fa330da</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="License">
      <data key="d0">License</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A License is a document issued by CCLD certifying a child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-site Coordinator">
      <data key="d0">Multi-site Coordinator</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Multi-site Coordinator manages the operations of multiple sites in a multi-site program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-210861f5af273887fc0b0ae0fd07edfd</data>
