      <data key="d0">Children</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Children are the individuals receiving care and supervision within a Certified Child Care Center, whose activities must be monitored for safety and developmental support.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are the primary beneficiaries of the certified child care center's services, requiring care, support, and various learning opportunities.&lt;SEP&gt;Children refers to the individuals that the certified child care center provides care for, with specific regulations related to their facility requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Children refer to young individuals who are the primary focus of the regulations outlined for safety and care at the child care center.&lt;SEP&gt;Children refers to young individuals who are under the supervision of a child care center and are the primary beneficiaries of outdoor play areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1ef5f193aed0479a33045cd9d6e34ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d71ecbdda9f0050185892674522421a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395c45f0f36a4c698dc34df7ec97f30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a9d69b412438d9027f85a2c39c69e7</data>
