    <node id="USDA Child and Adult Care Food Program">
      <data key="d0">USDA Child and Adult Care Food Program</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The USDA Child and Adult Care Food Program (USDA-CACFP) sets meal pattern requirements to ensure nutritional standards are met for meals served to children.&lt;SEP&gt;The USDA Child and Adult Care Food Program (USDA-CACFP) establishes meal pattern requirements to support the nutritional needs of children in care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99c8fc03de81f88ed62176dceb12b7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nutritional Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Nutritional Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nutritional Requirements refer to the standards that food must meet in order to be considered safe and beneficial for children's health within the care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Field Trips">
      <data key="d0">Field Trips</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Field trips are excursions organized by certified child care centers for children, requiring specific oversight and documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Field Trips are excursions that the child care center organizes to provide educational and recreational experiences outside the facility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b42c9a94a5a6a4d816abf87a18c33c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Raw Animal Foods">
      <data key="d0">Raw Animal Foods</data>
      <data key="d1">product</data>
      <data key="d2">Raw Animal Foods include potentially hazardous items like raw fish, meat, and eggs that cannot be served to children due to safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Written Instructions">
      <data key="d0">Written Instructions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Written Instructions are formal documents provided by medical practitioners or dieticians guiding dietary practices for children in the center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Statutes">
      <data key="d0">Statutes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Statutes refer to written laws or regulations that govern the operations and standards of the child care center, such as ORS 329A.260.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parental Consent">
      <data key="d0">Parental Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parental consent is required for giving infant formula to an infant who consumes human milk, ensuring parents' preferences are respected.&lt;SEP&gt;Parental Consent refers to the formal agreement from a parent or guardian, which is necessary for dietary modifications or special diets for children in the child care center.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e40e701e0c3d6dec9b45cdf7565fd4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb4d5cfab6fb222aa4a2485da799adb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco Products">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco Products</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tobacco products include items like cigarettes, cigars, and smokeless or vaping devices, which are prohibited within the center during operating hours.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guns and Firearms">
      <data key="d0">Guns and Firearms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Guns and firearms are weapons that are explicitly prohibited on the premises of the child care center at all times.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pools and Bodies of Water">
      <data key="d0">Pools and Bodies of Water</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pools and other bodies of water, including hot tubs and ponds, must be made inaccessible to ensure children's safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Insects and Rodents">
      <data key="d0">Insects and Rodents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Insects and rodents are considered pests that the child care center must keep the environment free from to promote health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dropping Off Children">
      <data key="d0">Dropping Off Children</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dropping off children refers to the process of leaving children at the child care center, which must be done safely and within regulated areas away from traffic.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Protection Agency">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Protection Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Environmental Protection Agency is a federal authority that regulates and ensures the safe use of sanitizers and disinfectants in childcare settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31244a2cb576a9cb8a62df97448f0e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1768781567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
