    <node id="Oregon Health Authority">
      <data key="d0">Oregon Health Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Oregon Health Authority (OHA) is a pivotal state agency responsible for the oversight of health regulations and standards related to child care centers in Oregon. It plays a critical role in ensuring compliance with public health guidelines, which includes setting and enforcing administrative rules that govern immunization practices for children attending certified child care centers. 

One of the key responsibilities of the OHA is to define child care-restrictable diseases, necessitating notification from child care centers when such cases occur. This oversight is essential for maintaining health and safety standards within these environments. Additionally, the OHA provides technical assistance to child care centers, particularly regarding water-related issues, and it closely monitors health regulations pertaining to food service and safety, including the approval of food sources and adherence to food preparation standards.

Furthermore, the OHA is tasked with overseeing the licensing of swimming pools utilized by certified child care centers, ensuring that all recreational facilities meet health and safety criteria. Overall, the Oregon Health Authority serves as the main governing body that enforces stringent health regulations, thereby safeguarding the well-being of children in a child care setting across the state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb113bc290514e50db6d44d2d83ee490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090946030f17ced3a228932753442ee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7b088891170652a6ae3540112924504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2bf51b699c37ac628327d3b24203494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a50fa93a5c42a28ff7fb62790e9d920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc8af7a631ba667698fda678ebafaca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c811f360e8fba8363059151e17bf37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d327b69848990feffa0bdfcf7346e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99c8fc03de81f88ed62176dceb12b7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ded3783740615f87802a00d127b69b5</data>
