    <edge source="City" target="Covenant">
      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation known as the City-Covenant represents a formal legal agreement that must be executed between property owners and the City, particularly in the context of zoning regulations. The Covenant is a crucial component in the density transfer process, ensuring that property developments remain aligned with the established laws and guidelines that govern land use and urban planning.

Property owners are required to enter into these covenants as a means of solidifying their commitment to adhere to varying zoning requirements. These agreements outline conditions related to different aspects of property development, including compliance with nonresidential use regulations and the maintenance of designated open space features. By executing a Covenant with the City, property owners agree to uphold these standards, which are vital for maintaining the integrity of the urban environment.

Moreover, the City mandates that these covenants detail specific conditions that must be followed to promote responsible development and land management. In particular, the necessity for a Covenant is emphasized when ensuring that the properties meet conditions related to zoning compliance. Ultimately, the City-Covenant relationship is integral for facilitating organized development while ensuring that the community's zoning objectives are consistently met.</data>
      <data key="d9">agreement,agreement requirement,density regulation,development requirement,formal agreement,legal agreement,local governance,maintenance requirement,property development,property regulation,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory requirement,zoning compliance</data>
