    <edge source="Preliminary Plan" target="Final Plat">
      <data key="d7">9.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between the Final Plat and the Preliminary Plan is critical in the land division process. The Preliminary Plan is a foundational step that must be approved prior to moving forward with the Final Plat. This initial plan outlines the proposed land division and must conform to established requirements that will later be reflected in the Final Plat. The approval of the Preliminary Plan is a prerequisite for obtaining the Final Plat, which signifies the final stage of authorization in land use and development.

Once the Preliminary Plan is approved, the Final Plat must be created based on this approved version. Therefore, any deviations from the approved Preliminary Plan may necessitate further review before the Final Plat can be finalized. It is essential that the Final Plat aligns with the specifications and standards set forth in the Preliminary Plan, ensuring that the overall land division process adheres to regulatory requirements.

In summary, the Final Plat is dependent on the successful approval of the Preliminary Plan, and it represents the culmination of the planning and approval stages required for land division. The relationship between these two elements is foundational for facilitating development and ensuring compliance with planning standards.</data>
      <data key="d9">application process,approval chain,approval process,approval stages,compliance,conformance,development approval,development phases,document relationship,land division,land use,planning process,planning stages,planning standards,regulatory compliance,review process</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-0017e9ee882283347e4f97cb10636de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c866b4b0736bc538364f76d18bd9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2bdb61444de27eb1c904251335348f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f464bb6caf4196f9f098e5debb9f7fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32beb3a9e96c3d41cc526d4dbd0b1f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41abaceb8097519bba26a5ccb4274c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19ac885283037176486bf6beb78cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594964a698a9063f34a66127a99f84d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2546da1b6188ab781e1777780334eb3</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1768781256</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
