    <edge source="Oregon Health Authority" target="Certified Child Care Center">
      <data key="d7">7.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Oregon Health Authority provides necessary health approvals for certified child care centers as part of the licensing process.&lt;SEP&gt;The certified child care center must comply with the Oregon Health Authority's regulations on immunizations for children.&lt;SEP&gt;The certified child care center is required to contact the Oregon Health Authority regarding any lead hazards discovered on the premises.&lt;SEP&gt;The certified child care center must comply with regulations set forth by the Oregon Health Authority regarding child health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The certified child care center operates under the regulations set forth by the Oregon Health Authority, ensuring health standards are met.&lt;SEP&gt;The Certified Child Care Center must comply with regulations set by the Oregon Health Authority to ensure safe food handling.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oregon Health Authority oversees the licensing of swimming pools used by certified child care centers.</data>
      <data key="d9">approval,compliance,food safety,health oversight,health standards,licensing,oversight,regulatory compliance,regulatory oversight,safety measures</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8814ece3ffb64da75040ca0fc0bc2fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb113bc290514e50db6d44d2d83ee490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090946030f17ced3a228932753442ee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a50fa93a5c42a28ff7fb62790e9d920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc8af7a631ba667698fda678ebafaca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99c8fc03de81f88ed62176dceb12b7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ded3783740615f87802a00d127b69b5</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
